msgid_plural "crime novels"
msgstr[0] "novela policial"
msgstr[1] "novelas policiales"

#. ~ Description for crime novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"After their diamond heist goes wrong, the surviving criminals begin to "
"suspect that one of them is a police informant."
msgstr ""
"Luego de que fallara el robo del diamante, los criminales supervivientes "
"empiezan a sospechar que uno de ellos es un informante de la policía."

#. ~ Description for crime novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A story about three people in the fictional city of Los Santos, a gangster, "
"an upper-class man, and a psychopath, eventually banding together to pull-"
"off the biggest heist in the city's history"
msgstr ""
"Una historia acerca de tres personas viviendo en la ciudad ficticia de Los "
"Santos: un gángster, un hombre de clase alta y un psicópata, que "
"eventualmente se unen para cometer el mayor atraco en la historia de la "
"ciudad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Murdered by the Grapevine"
msgid_plural "copies of Murdered by the Grapevine"
msgstr[0] "Asesinado por la Vid"
msgstr[1] "copias de Asesinado por la Vid"

#. ~ Description for Murdered by the Grapevine
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This cheap paperback tells the story of a mob boss done in by mere "
"suspicion.  She never breaks a confidence, never rats out an accomplice, and"
" never turns her back on a friend.  Nonetheless her grip on the reigns of "
"the underworld is eroded by rumor and paranoia."
msgstr ""
"Este libro barato cuenta la historia de un jefe de la mafia asesinado por "
"meras sospechas. Nunca rompe una confidencia, nunca delata a un cómplice, y "
"nunca le da la espalda a un amigo. Sin embargo, su control sobre el reino de"
" los bajos fondos está erosionado por los rumores y la paranoia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Midnight Cop"
msgid_plural "copies of Midnight Cop"
msgstr[0] "Policia de MediaNoche"
msgstr[1] "copias de Policia de MediaNoche"

#. ~ Description for Midnight Cop
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this bare-knuckled potboiler, a ruthless police detective schemes to shut"
" down local crime lords by pitting them against each other.  When long-"
"simmering resentments finally flare the city learns why they call it \"the "
"dead of night.\""
msgstr ""
"En este libro para escrito para cubrir gastos, un despiadado detective de la"
" policía planea acabar con los señores del crimen local enfrentándolos entre"
" sí. Cuando los resentimientos de larga duración finalmente se encienden, la"
" ciudad aprende por qué la llaman \"la muerte de la noche\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "drama novel"
msgid_plural "drama novels"
msgstr[0] "novela dramática"
msgstr[1] "novelas dramáticas"

#. ~ Description for drama novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A real book for real adults."
msgstr "Un verdadero libro para verdaderos adultos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "erotic novel"
msgid_plural "erotic novels"
msgstr[0] "novela erótica"
msgstr[1] "novelas eróticas"

#. ~ Description for erotic novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A hackneyed fictional narrative concealing low-grade literary smut."
msgstr ""
"Una narrativa ficticia trillada que oculta una obscenidad literaria de bajo "
"grado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "experimental novel"
msgid_plural "experimental novels"
msgstr[0] "novela experimental"
msgstr[1] "novelas experimentales"

#. ~ Description for experimental novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bizarre play about the philosophy of existential absurdity.  Or maybe it's"
" about two guys waiting for their friend to show up.  It's confusing."
msgstr ""
"Una obra extraña acerca de la filosofía del absurdo existencial. O tal vez "
"sea acerca de dos tipos esperando a un amigo que aparezca. Es un poco "
"confusa."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "fantasy novel"
msgid_plural "fantasy novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de fantasía"
msgstr[1] "novelas de fantasía"

#. ~ Description for fantasy novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Basic sword & sorcery."
msgstr "Puramente espadas y hechicería."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "horror novel"
msgid_plural "horror novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de terror"
msgstr[1] "novelas de terror"

#. ~ Description for horror novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Maybe not the best reading material considering the situation."
msgstr ""
"Tal vez no sea el material de lectura más indicado para la situación en que "
"estás."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "mystery novel"
msgid_plural "mystery novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de misterio"
msgstr[1] "novelas de misterio"

#. ~ Description for mystery novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A detective investigates an unusual murder in a secluded location."
msgstr "Un detective investiga un inusual asesinato en un lugar aislado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "road novel"
msgid_plural "road novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de carretera"
msgstr[1] "novelas de carretera"

#. ~ Description for road novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A tale about a group of friends who wander the USA in the 1960s against a "
"backdrop of jazz, poetry and drug use."
msgstr ""
"Una historia acerca de un grupo de amigos que viajan por EE.UU. en la década"
" de 1960, con un fondo de jazz, poesía y drogas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "romance novel"
msgid_plural "romance novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de romance"
msgstr[1] "novelas de romance"

#. ~ Description for romance novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Drama and mild smut."
msgstr "Drama y obscenidades tiernas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Love and Circuses"
msgid_plural "copies of Love and Circuses"
msgstr[0] "Amor y Circos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Amor y Circos"

#. ~ Description for Love and Circuses
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The passionate saga of two Boston politicians fiercely battling each other "
"for the mayor's office, and for Lydia's hand in marriage."
msgstr ""
"La apasionada saga de dos políticos de Boston luchando ferozmente por la "
"alcaldía y por pedir la mano de Lydia en matrimonio."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Cloven Kisses"
msgid_plural "copies of Cloven Kisses"
msgstr[0] "Besos Partidos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Besos Partidos"

#. ~ Description for Cloven Kisses
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When the devil falls in love with a warlock, his proposal must be infernally"
" wicked.  Will hooves, horns, and the scent of sulphur condemn love's flames"
" to hellfire?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando el diablo se enamora de un hechicero, su propuesta debe ser "
"infernalmente malvada. ¿Condenarán las pezuñas, los cuernos y el olor a "
"azufre las llamas del amor al fuego del infierno?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Conquer Me Sweetly"
msgid_plural "copies of Conquer Me Sweetly"
msgstr[0] "Conquístame Dulcemente"
msgstr[1] "copias de Conquístame Dulcemente"

#. ~ Description for Conquer Me Sweetly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Sweet Providence Books is delighted to offer you this romantic tale of "
"delicious dalliances and daring delights."
msgstr ""
"Libros Sweet Providence se complace en ofrecerles este romántico relato de "
"deliciosos bailes y atrevidas delicias."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Dubliner's Debutante"
msgid_plural "copies of Dubliner's Debutante"
msgstr[0] "Debutante de Dublin"
msgstr[1] "copias del Debutante de Dublin"

#. ~ Description for Dubliner's Debutante
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"His love songs were only for me, but I preferred the banjo over bagpipes.  "
"How could I ever love a kilted yankee of foreign breeding?"
msgstr ""
"Sus canciones de amor eran sólo para mí, pero yo prefería el banjo a la "
"gaita. ¿Cómo podría amar a un yanqui con kilt de raza extranjera?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Blood Diodes"
msgid_plural "copies of Blood Diodes"
msgstr[0] "Diodos de Sangre"
msgstr[1] "copias de Diodos de Sangre"

#. ~ Description for Blood Diodes
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"He is an automaton, she is a reformed vampire, can love find a way?  In this"
" edgy romance by acclaimed author Kea Dekker, heartbreak is just the "
"beginning."
msgstr ""
"Él es un autómata, ella es una vampira reformada, ¿puede el amor encontrar "
"un camino? En este romance nervioso de la aclamada autora Kea Dekker, la "
"angustia es sólo el comienzo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Envying Heaven"
msgid_plural "copies of Envying Heaven"
msgstr[0] "Envidiar al Cielo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Envidiar al Cielo"

#. ~ Description for Envying Heaven
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When her fiancee names a star for her Wanda begins to wonder if an "
"astronomer's wife can ever compete with the allure of the cosmos."
msgstr ""
"Cuando su prometido nombra una estrella para ella, Wanda comienza a "
"preguntarse si la esposa de un astrónomo puede competir con el encanto del "
"cosmos"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Tall, Dark, and Gruesome"
msgid_plural "copies of Tall, Dark, and Gruesome"
msgstr[0] "Alto, Oscuro, y Espantoso"
msgstr[1] "copias de Alto, Oscuro, y Espantoso"

#. ~ Description for Tall, Dark, and Gruesome
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Fatima's obsession with the dead threatens to consume her when she falls in "
"love with a restless ghost.  In this provocative romp celebrated author Kea "
"Dekker gently lifts the thin veil separating cold bodies from warm."
msgstr ""
"La obsesión de Fátima por los muertos amenaza con consumirla cuando se "
"enamora de un fantasma inquieto. En este provocador romance, la célebre "
"autor Kea Dekker levanta suavemente el delgado velo que separa los cuerpos "
"fríos de los calientes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Along Came a Rider"
msgid_plural "copies of Along Came a Rider"
msgstr[0] "A lo largo llegó un jinete"
msgstr[1] "copias de A lo largo llegó un jinete"

#. ~ Description for Along Came a Rider
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When Beth's career as a pro steeplechase jockey threatens to divide her from"
" her lover, Beth has to act fast.  Will she ever find a man that can keep up"
" with her racing heart?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando la carrera de Beth como jinete profesional de obstáculos amenaza con "
"separarla de su amante, Beth tiene que actuar rápido. ¿Encontrará alguna vez"
" un hombre que pueda seguir el ritmo de su corazón acelerado?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Rogue's Virtue"
msgid_plural "copies of Rogue's Virtue"
msgstr[0] "La Virtud del Picaro"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Virtud del Picaro"

#. ~ Description for Rogue's Virtue
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Can Victoria reform the fugitive from justice who wooed her with false "
"pretenses and true passion?"
msgstr ""
"¿Puede Victoria reformar al fugitivo de la justicia que la cortejó con "
"falsas pretensiones y verdadera pasión?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Death of My Secret Life"
msgid_plural "copies of The Death of My Secret Life"
msgstr[0] "La Muerte de Mi Vida Secreta"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Muerte de Mi Vida Secreta"

#. ~ Description for The Death of My Secret Life
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Makeda comes out to her family, but she's still got plenty of skeletons in "
"her closet.  Best selling authoress Kea Dekker breaks all the rules in this "
"macabre story of love and lies."
msgstr ""
"Makeda sale del armario con su familia, pero todavía tiene muchos esqueletos"
" en su armario. La autora del best seller Kea Dekker rompe todas las reglas "
"en esta macabra historia de amor y mentiras."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "samurai novel"
msgid_plural "samurai novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de samurai"
msgstr[1] "novelas de samurai"

#. ~ Description for samurai novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The classic tale of a wandering swordsman who comes to a small settlement "
"and is hired to help the townsfolk defend themselves from a band of "
"marauding outlaws.  This hardback is quite hefty."
msgstr ""
"La clásica historia de un espadachín errante que llega a un pequeño "
"asentamiento y es contratado para ayudar a la gente del pueblo a defenderse "
"de una banda de forajidos merodeadores. Este libro de tapa dura es bastante "
"pesado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "satire novel"
msgid_plural "satire novels"
msgstr[0] "novela satírica"
msgstr[1] "novelas satíricas"

#. ~ Description for satire novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A political satire of the pre-apocalypse world.  Looking back on it from "
"this side of Armageddon makes it seem all the more ridiculous."
msgstr ""
"Una sátira política del mundo pre-apocalíptico. Mirándola ahora desde este "
"lado del Armagedón, la hace parecer mucho más ridículo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The House of God"
msgid_plural "copies of The House of God"
msgstr[0] "La Casa de Dios"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Casa de Dios"

#. ~ Description for The House of God
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Set in a lightly disguised Boston hospital of high repute, Samuel Shem’s "
"novel dives deep into the agony of absurdity."
msgstr ""
"Situada en un oscuro hospital de Boston de gran reputación, la novela de "
"Samuel Shem se sumerge en la agonía del absurdo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Catch-22"
msgid_plural "copies of Catch-22"
msgstr[0] "Catch-22"
msgstr[1] "copias de Catch-22"

#. ~ Description for Catch-22
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"There is a short informational forward in this paperback edition of "
"Catch-22.  Apparently the original title for Joseph Heller’s excruciatingly "
"brilliant war satire was \"Catch-11.\""
msgstr ""
"Hay un breve avance informativo en esta edición de bolsillo de Catch-22. "
"Aparentemente el título original de la insoportablemente brillante sátira de"
" guerra de Joseph Heller era \"Catch-11\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Master and Margarita"
msgid_plural "copies of Master and Margarita"
msgstr[0] "Maestro y Margarita"
msgstr[1] "copias de Maestro y Margarita"

#. ~ Description for The Master and Margarita
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Featuring a cast that includes Satan, Pontius Pilate, Jesus Christ, "
"vampires, a talking cat, and the literary elite of Moscow, this novel by "
"Mikhail Bulgakov explores philosophical issues on the nature of good and "
"evil."
msgstr ""
"Con un reparto que incluye a Satanás, Poncio Pilatos, Jesucristo, vampiros, "
"un gato que habla y la élite literaria de Moscú, esta novela de Mikhail "
"Bulgakov explora cuestiones filosóficas sobre la naturaleza del bien y del "
"mal."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A Handful of Dust"
msgid_plural "copies of A Handful of Dust"
msgstr[0] "Un Puñado de Arena"
msgstr[1] "copias de Un Puñado de Arena"

#. ~ Description for A Handful of Dust
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Laced with cynicism, Evelyn Waugh's \"A Handful of Dust\" satirizes a "
"stratum of characters who have wealth, but lack any other credentials."
msgstr ""
"Enfrentada al cinismo, \"Un puñado de polvo\" de Evelyn Waugh satiriza un "
"estrato de personajes que tienen riqueza, pero carecen de otras credenciales"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Cat’s Cradle"
msgid_plural "copies of Cat’s Cradle"
msgstr[0] "Cuna de Gato"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cuna de Gato"

#. ~ Description for Cat’s Cradle
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A paperback edition of Kurt Vonnegut's fourth novel, in which the threat of "
"nuclear destruction isn't much of an influence on human nature."
msgstr ""
"Una edición en bolsillo de la cuarta novela de Kurt Vonnegut, en la que la "
"amenaza de la destrucción nuclear no influye mucho en la naturaleza humana."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "spy novel"
msgid_plural "spy novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de espías"
msgstr[1] "novelas de espías"

#. ~ Description for spy novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A tale of intrigue and espionage amongst Nazis, no, Commies, no, Iraqis!"
msgstr ""
"Una historia de intriga y espionaje entre ¡nazis, no, comunistas, no, "
"iraquíes!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Come Fly the Treacherous Skies"
msgid_plural "copies of Come Fly the Treacherous Skies"
msgstr[0] "Ven a Volar a los Cielos Traicioneros"
msgstr[1] "copias de Ven a Volar a los Cielos Traicioneros"

#. ~ Description for Come Fly the Treacherous Skies
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This tale of intrigue betrays the story of a debonair mechanic driven by a "
"lust for revenge.  As she uncovers a sophisticated network of amateur pilots"
" turned smugglers, the good guys and the bad guys begin to all look the "
"same."
msgstr ""
"Este cuento de intriga traiciona la historia de un mecánico desamparado "
"impulsado por el deseo de venganza. A medida que descubre una sofisticada "
"red de pilotos aficionados convertidos en contrabandistas, los buenos y los "
"malos empiezan a parecer todos iguales."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Lies, Damn Lies, and Rocket Science"
msgid_plural "copies of Lies, Damn Lies, and Rocket Science"
msgstr[0] "Mentiras, Malditas Mentiras y Ciencia de cohetes"
msgstr[1] "copias de Mentiras, Malditas Mentiras y Ciencia de cohetes"

#. ~ Description for Lies, Damn Lies, and Rocket Science
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spy novel tells the story of a jaded rocket scientist looking for "
"redemption in all the wrong places.  As selling state secrets becomes her "
"career, she learns there isn't much of difference between a double-agent and"
" a triple-agent."
msgstr ""
"Esta novela de espías cuenta la historia de un cansado científico de cohetes"
" que busca la redención en todos los lugares equivocados. A medida que la "
"venta de secretos de estado se convierte en su carrera, aprende que no hay "
"mucha diferencia entre un agente doble y uno triple."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "swashbuckling novel"
msgid_plural "swashbuckling novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de caballería"
msgstr[1] "novelas de caballería"

#. ~ Description for swashbuckling novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An exciting seventeenth century tale of how an enslaved Irish doctor and his"
" comrades-in-chains escape and become heroic pirates of the Robin Hood "
"variety."
msgstr ""
"Una excitante historia del siglo XVII acerca del escape de un doctor "
"irlandés esclavizado y sus compañeros esclavos, y su conversión en piratas "
"heroicos al estilo de Robin Hood."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Black Freighter"
msgid_plural "copies of The Black Freighter"
msgstr[0] "El Carguero Negro"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Carguero Negro"

#. ~ Description for The Black Freighter
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Who watches the watchmen?  Pirate Jenny, that's who!  This swashbuckling "
"adventure novel will make you feel swell."
msgstr ""
"¿Quién vigila a los vigilantes? La pirata Jenny, ¡es quien! Esta novela de "
"aventuras de espadachines te hará sentir bien."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Captain Gosgold and the Sea Rovers of Buzzards Bay"
msgid_plural "copies of The Sea Rovers"
msgstr[0] "Los Vagabundos del Mar"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Vagabundos del Mar"

#. ~ Description for Captain Gosgold and the Sea Rovers of Buzzards Bay
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This lengthy paperback novel describes the ocean exploits of Captain "
"Gosgold.  The British consider him an outlaw, but in America he is a "
"patriot."
msgstr ""
"Esta larga novela de bolsillo describe las hazañas oceánicas del Capitán "
"Gosgold. Los británicos lo consideran un forajido, pero en América es un "
"patriota."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Code of the Buccaneer"
msgid_plural "copies of The Buccaneer"
msgstr[0] "El Código del Bucanero"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Bucanero"

#. ~ Description for The Code of the Buccaneer
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The cover of this paperback pirate story shows a shirtless man and a near "
"shirtless woman.  Clearly it is not a dress code."
msgstr ""
"La portada de esta historia de piratas en bolsillo muestra a un hombre sin "
"camisa y a una mujer casi sin camisa. Claramente no es un código de "
"vestimenta."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "thriller novel"
msgid_plural "thriller novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de suspenso"
msgstr[1] "novelas de suspenso"

#. ~ Description for thriller novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A suspenseful tale of betrayal and revenge."
msgstr "Una historia de suspenso con engaños y venganzas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "tragedy novel"
msgid_plural "tragedy novels"
msgstr[0] "novela trágica"
msgstr[1] "novelas trágicas"

#. ~ Description for tragedy novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The story of two young lovers whose feuding families threaten to keep them "
"apart."
msgstr ""
"La historia de dos jóvenes amantes cuyas familias enemistadas amenazan con "
"mantenerlos separados."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "war novel"
msgid_plural "war novels"
msgstr[0] "novela bélica"
msgstr[1] "novelas bélicas"

#. ~ Description for war novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A thrilling narrative of survival in a prisoner of war camp during the "
"Second World War, filled with riveting subplots about rat farming and "
"dysentery."
msgstr ""
"Una narrativa llena de suspenso sobre la supervivencia de un prisionera de "
"guerra durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial, llena de fascinantes tramas "
"secundarias acerca de la crianza de ratas y la disentería."

#. ~ Description for war novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A story about a Bosnian citizen who goes through many hardships and near "
"death during the breakup of Yugoslavia."
msgstr ""
"Es la historia de un ciudadano bosnio que pasa por varios momentos difíciles"
" y a estar cerca de la muerte durante el desmembramiento de Yugoslavia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "western novel"
msgid_plural "western novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de vaqueros"
msgstr[1] "novelas de vaqueros"

#. ~ Description for western novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The classic tale of a gunfighting stranger who comes to a small settlement "
"and is hired to help the townsfolk defend themselves from a band of "
"marauding outlaws."
msgstr ""
"La clásica historia de un desconocido pistolero que llega a un pequeño "
"poblado y es contratado para ayudar a sus habitantes a defenderse de una "
"banda de forajidos saqueadores."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Atwixt a Brace of Cacti"
msgid_plural "copies of Atwixt a Brace of Cacti"
msgstr[0] "Atwixt un Corsé de Cacti"
msgstr[1] "copias de Atwixt un Corsé de Cacti"

#. ~ Description for Atwixt a Brace of Cacti
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A grizzled clodhopper interviews a mess of rangehands, flummoxing longhorns "
"and tenderfoot alike in a flusteration of jawing."
msgstr ""
"Un saltamontes canoso entrevista a un lío de mano de campo, cuernos largos y"
" pies tiernos por igual en una agitación de mandíbula."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Stinky Bart Puts on Starch"
msgid_plural "copies of Stinky Bart Puts on Starch"
msgstr[0] "El Apestoso Bart se Aplica Almidón"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Apestoso Bart se Aplica Almidón"

#. ~ Description for Stinky Bart Puts on Starch
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A local bandit, driven by sadistic impulses, begins offering unlicensed "
"dentistry to brave frontiersmen with few options and fewer teeth."
msgstr ""
"Un bandido local, impulsado por impulsos sádicos, comienza a ofrecer "
"odontología sin licencia a los valientes fronterizos con pocas opciones y "
"menos dientes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Six Beans in the Wheel"
msgid_plural "copies of Six Beans in the Wheel"
msgstr[0] "Seis Habas en la Rueda"
msgstr[1] "copias de Seis Habas en la Rueda"

#. ~ Description for Six Beans in the Wheel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The safety is off in this gun slinging tale of revenge and redemption by "
"acclaimed author El Amor."
msgstr ""
"La seguridad se ha quitado en este cuento de venganza y redención del "
"aclamado autor El Amor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Irons at Calico Queen Annex"
msgid_plural "copies of Irons at Calico Queen Annex"
msgstr[0] "Hierros en el Anexo de la Reina de Calico"
msgstr[1] "copias de Hierros en el Anexo de la Reina de Calico"

#. ~ Description for Irons at Calico Queen Annex
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The establishment of a telegraph line into the recently named town of Calico"
" Queen threatens to bring with it the long arm of the law.  A trio of "
"enterprising gunfighters hatches a plan to keep Calico Queen wild by looting"
" the supply wagons."
msgstr ""
"El establecimiento de una línea de telégrafo en la recién nombrada ciudad de"
" Calico Queen amenaza con traer consigo el largo brazo de la ley. Un trío de"
" pistoleros emprendedores traman un plan para mantener a Calico Queen "
"salvaje saqueando los vagones de provisiones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Riot on the Range"
msgid_plural "copies of Riot on the Range"
msgstr[0] "Disturbios en la Cordillera"
msgstr[1] "copias de Disturbios en la Cordillera"

#. ~ Description for Riot on the Range
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Best selling author El Amor paints a visceral study in red with his latest "
"western saga: Riot on the Range."
msgstr ""
"El autor más vendido, El Amor, pinta de rojo un estudio visceral con su "
"última saga occidental: Disturbios en la Cordillera."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Vaquero Sun"
msgid_plural "copies of Vaquero Sun"
msgstr[0] "Sol Vaquero"
msgstr[1] "copias del Sol Vaquero"

#. ~ Description for Vaquero Sun
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Western author El Amor relates the story of a dispossessed young man "
"inspired by a heat stroke delusion to pursue justice against an evil land "
"baron."
msgstr ""
"El autor occidental El Amor relata la historia de un joven desposeído "
"inspirado por un delirio de insolación para buscar justicia contra un "
"malvado barón de la tierra."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Vendetta Riders"
msgid_plural "copies of The Vendetta Riders"
msgstr[0] "Los Jinetes de Vendetta"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Jinetes de Vendetta"

#. ~ Description for The Vendetta Riders
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wild young man, fast on the draw, who thinks he has nothing to lose, falls"
" in with a group of gun runners."
msgstr ""
"Un joven salvaje, rápido al desenfundar, cree que no tiene nada que perder, "
"cae con un grupo de traficantes de armas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "phone book"
msgid_plural "phone books"
msgstr[0] "guía telefónica"
msgstr[1] "guías telefónicas"

#. ~ Description for phone book
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hefty volume contains the telephone numbers of individuals, businesses,"
" and utilities in the nearby area, pretty useless during the apocalypse and "
"all."
msgstr ""
"Este pesado libro contiene las direcciones y los números de teléfono de las "
"personas, negocios y empresas de servicios públicos de toda la zona. "
"Bastante inútil durante un apocalipsis."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "photo album"
msgid_plural "photo albums"
msgstr[0] "álbum de fotos"
msgstr[1] "álbumes de fotos"

#. ~ Description for photo album
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A leather album full of photos of somebody's family.  You don't know any of "
"the people in them, but seeing these pictures still makes you think of "
"happier times."
msgstr ""
"Un álbum de cuero de fotos de alguna familia. No conoces a ninguno de los "
"que aparecen en ellas, pero mirar las fotos te hace pensar en tiempos más "
"felices."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of plays"
msgid_plural "books of plays"
msgstr[0] "libro de obras teatrales"
msgstr[1] "libros de obras teatrales"

#. ~ Description for book of plays
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of plays by various authors from around the world, including "
"scripts by Wilde, Beckett, Checkov, and Shakespeare."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de obras teatrales de diversos autores de todo el mundo, "
"incluyendo obras de Wilde, Beckett, Chéjov y Shakespeare."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of poetry"
msgid_plural "books of poetry"
msgstr[0] "libro de poesía"
msgstr[1] "libros de poesía"

#. ~ Description for book of poetry
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of poetry by various authors from around the world, including "
"writings by Dickinson, Goethe, Thoreau, and Yeats."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de poesía por varios autores de todo el mundo, incluyendo "
"piezas de Dickinson, Goethe, Thoreau y Yeats."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "priest's diary"
msgid_plural "priests' diaries"
msgstr[0] "diario de un sacerdote"
msgstr[1] "diarios de un sacerdote"

#. ~ Description for priest's diary
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small book filled with journal entries in Latin.  You can read Latin, "
"right?"
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño libro lleno de entradas en latín de un diario. Puedes leer en "
"latín, ¿verdad?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "corporate accounting ledger"
msgid_plural "corporate accounting ledgers"
msgstr[0] "libros de contabilidad de corporaciones"
msgstr[1] "libros de contabilidad de corporaciones"

#. ~ Description for corporate accounting ledger
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "If you knew what to look for something might stand out…"
msgstr "Si supieras qué buscar, algo podría sobresalir..."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "patient treatment records"
msgid_plural "patient treatment records"
msgstr[0] "registros de pacientes"
msgstr[1] "registros de pacientes"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'patient treatment records'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A massive stack of medical records that contain every gory detail."
msgstr ""
"Un pila enorme de registros médicos que contienen todos los detalles "
"cruentos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "national weather transcripts"
msgid_plural "national weather transcripts"
msgstr[0] "transcripciones del clima nacional"
msgstr[1] "transcripciones del clima nacional"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'national weather transcripts'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Old weather records are about as interesting as a rock."
msgstr "Viejos registros del clima que son tan interesantes como una piedra."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "big book of short stories"
msgid_plural "big books of short stories"
msgstr[0] "gran libro de pequeñas historias"
msgstr[1] "grandes libros de pequeñas historias"

#. ~ Description for big book of short stories
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This humongous volume contains a vast collection of short stories by "
"different authors, spanning a wide variety of topics and genres."
msgstr ""
"Este gigantesco volumen contiene una vasta colección de cuentos de "
"diferentes autores, cubriendo una gran variedad de tópicos y géneros."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of tall tales"
msgid_plural "books of tall tales"
msgstr[0] "libro de relatos fantásticos"
msgstr[1] "libros de relatos fantásticos"

#. ~ Description for book of tall tales
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An entertaining collection of early American folklore, featuring tales of "
"larger than life individuals and their amazing adventures."
msgstr ""
"Una entretenida colección de relatos tradicionales americanos, con historias"
" sobre individuos de proporciones épicas y sus aventuras extraordinarias."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Visions in Solitude"
msgid_plural "copies of Visions in Solitude"
msgstr[0] "Visiones en Soledad"
msgstr[1] "copias de Visiones en Soledad"

#. ~ Description for Visions in Solitude
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A small book detailing 'visions' a prisoner had on death row."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño libro detallando las \"revelaciones\" que tuvo un prisionero en "
"el corredor de la muerte."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of classic literature"
msgid_plural "books of classic literature"
msgstr[0] "libro de literatura clásica"
msgstr[1] "libros de literatura clásica"

#. ~ Description for book of classic literature
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book of classic literature, timeless and enjoyable but a bit dense to "
"read."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de literatura clásica, atemporal y entretenido pero un poco denso "
"de leer."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Dickens' \"Bleak House\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Casa desolada\" de Dickens."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Great Expectations\" by Charles Dickens."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Grandes esperanzas\" de Charles Dickens."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of William Shinderling's \"Under the Beech Trees\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Bajo las hayas\" de William Shinderling."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a collection of three Jane Austen novels: \"Pride and Prejudice\", "
"\"Sense and Sensibility\", and \"Emma\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de tres novelas de Jane Austen: \"Orgullo y "
"prejuicio\", \"Sentido y sensibilidad\" y \"Emma\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a well-worn paperback copy of \"Lord of the Flies\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda bastante desgastada de \"El señor de las "
"moscas\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" by Harper Lee."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Matar a un ruiseñor\" de Harper Lee."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of F. Scott Fitzgerald's \"The Great Gatsby.\""
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El Gran Gatsby\" de F. Scott Fitzgerald."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is copy of Michael Abanaderly's lesser-known work, \"He Walks\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de uno de los trabajos menos conocidos de Michael "
"Abanaderly, \"Camina\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a collection of several vintage science fiction stories by Ray "
"Bradbury."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de varias obras de ciencia ficción de Ray Bradbury."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Adventures of Tom Sawyer\" by Mark Twain."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Las aventuras de Tom Sawyer\" de Mark Twain."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is an illustrated copy of \"Innocents Abroad\" by Mark Twain."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia ilustrada de \"Los inocentes en el extranjero\" de Mark "
"Twain."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Bram Stoker's \"Dracula\", with scholarly commentary in "
"the margins."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Drácula\", de Bram Stoker, con anotaciones académicas"
" en los márgenes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large print copy of Tolstoy's \"War and Peace\".  It might make a "
"decent improvised weapon."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una larga copia impresa de \"Guerra y paz\" de Tolstoy. Podría "
"funcionar decentemente como arma improvisada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a paperback copy of the well-known classic \"Dark Days Ahead\", by "
"K. G. Ranade.  There are scrawled margin notes all over it, apparently the "
"workings of a confused and feverish mind."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda del conocido clásico \"Dark Days Ahead\" de"
" K. G. Ranade. Hay anotaciones garabateadas por todos los márgenes, "
"aparentemente el trabajo de una mente confusa y febril."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Jane Eyre\".  The cover art is quite out of place, "
"making it look more like a dime-store romance novel."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Jane Eyre\". El arte de la cubierta está bastante "
"fuera de lugar, haciendo que parezca más una novela de romance barata."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a perfectly preserved hardcover copy of \"The Gunslinger\" by "
"Stephen King, autographed by the author.  It contains a certificate of "
"authenticity pronouncing it to be a first edition."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa dura bien conservada de \"El pistolero\" de "
"Stephen King, autografiada por el autor. Contiene un certificado de "
"autenticidad acreditando que es primera edición."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This paperback copy of \"Wuthering Heights\" has a large coffee stain on the"
" first page."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"Cumbres borrascosas\". Tiene una gran "
"mancha de café en la primera página."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hardbound copy of \"Lady Chatterly's Lover\", by D. H. Lawrence.  "
"It has some very explicit illustrations."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia encuadernada de \"El amante de Lady Chatterly\", de D. H. "
"Lawrance. Tiene algunas ilustraciones muy explícitas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hardbound copy of \"The Catcher in the Rye.\".  It has some very "
"nicely done illustrations."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia encuadernada de \"El guardián entre el centeno\". Tiene "
"algunas ilustraciones muy bien realizadas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a collection of classic renaissance era stories, headlined by \"Don "
"Quixote\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de historias clásicas del Renacimiento, encabezadas "
"por \"El Quijote\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a paperback copy of \"The Fellowship of the Ring\" by Tolkien."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"La compañía del anillo\" de Tolkien."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a paperback copy of \"The Two Towers\" by Tolkien."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"Las dos torres\" de Tolkien."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a paperback copy of \"The Return of the King\" by Tolkien."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"El retorno del rey\" de Tolkien."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hardbound collection of George Orwell's works, including \"1984\" "
"and \"Animal Farm\" as well as many of his less infamous titles."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia encuadernada de las obras de George Orwell, incluyendo "
"\"1984\" y \"Rebelión en la granja\" así como muchos de sus títulos menos "
"conocidos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a paperback copy of \"Little Women\" by Louisa May Alcott.  It "
"appears to have been read a great many times."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"Mujercitas\" de Louisa May Alcott. "
"Parece haber sido leída muchas veces."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a paperback copy of \"Of Mice and Men\" by Steinbeck."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de tapa blanda de \"De ratones y hombres\" de Steinbeck."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty hardcover copy of \"Run and Run Again\" by Finn Calpay.  "
"There is a lengthy forward about the controversy around the book's release."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran copia en tapa dura de \"Corre y corre otra vez\" de Finn "
"Calpay. Hay un largo prólogo sobre la controversia alrededor del lanzamiento"
" del libro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hardcover copy of \"The Gates Have Opened\" by Arianna Methusalah."
"  You feel like you've read this before, but can't remember where.  "
"Something about the book fills you with unease."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia en tapa dura de \"Las puertas se han abierto\" de Arianna "
"Methusalah. Sientes que lo has leído antes, pero no sabes dónde. Hay algo "
"acerca del libro que te hace sentir incomodez."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Count of Monte Cristo\" by Dumas."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El conde de Montecristo\" de Dumas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Secret Garden\" by Frances Burnett."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El jardín secreto\" de Frances Burnett."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Lieutenant Hornblower\" by C.S. Forester."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia del \" El Teniente de Navío Hornblower\" de C.S. Forester."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Master and Commander\" by Patrick O'Brian."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Capitán de mar y guerra\" de Patrick O'Brian."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Warden\" by Anthony Trollope."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"The Warden\" de Anthony Trollope."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Far Side of the World\" by Patrick O'Brian."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"The Far Side of the World\" de Patrick O'Brian."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"HMS Surprise\" by Patrick O'Brian."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"HMS Surprise\" de Patrick O'Brian."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Barchester Towers\" by Anthony Trollope."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Barchester Towers\" de Anthony Trollope."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Land Ironclads\" by H.G. Wells."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"The Land Ironclads\" de H.G. Wells."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Great Boer War\" by Arthur Conan Doyle."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"The Great Boer War\" de Arthur Conan Doyle."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Crime of the Congo\" by Arthur Conan Doyle."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El crimen del Congo\" de Arthur Conan Doyle."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Parasite\" by Arthur Conan Doyle."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El Parásito\" de Arthur Conan Doyle."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"By Stroke of Sword\" by Andrew Balfour."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"By Stroke of Sword\" de Andrew Balfour."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Secret Agent\" by Joseph Conrad."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El Agente Secreto\" de Joseph Conrad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Lord Jim\" by Joseph Conrad."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Lord Jim\" de Joseph Conrad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Vanity Fair\" by William Makepeace Thackeray."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La feria de las vanidades\" de William Makepeace "
"Thackeray."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Luck of Barry Lyndon\" by William Makepeace "
"Thackeray."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Suerte de Barry Lyndon\" de William Makepeace "
"Thackeray."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"North and South\" by Elizabeth Gaskell."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Norte y Sur\" de Elizabeth Gaskell."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Mayor of Casterbridge\" by Thomas Hardy."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El alcalde de Casterbridge\" de Thomas Hardy."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Wessex Tales\" by Thomas Hardy."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Misterios de Wessex\" de Thomas Hardy."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Far from the Madding Crowd\" by Thomas Hardy."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Lejos del mundanal ruido\" de Thomas Hardy."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Captains Courageous\" by Rudyard Kipling."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Capitanes Intrépidos\" de Rudyard Kipling."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Canterbury Tales\" by Geoffrey Chaucer."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Los Cuentos de Canterbury\" de Geoffrey Chaucer."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Harold, the Last of the Saxons\" by Edward Bulwer-"
"Lytton."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Harold, the Last of the Saxons\" de Edward Bulwer-"
"Lytton."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Mr Midshipman Easy\" by Frederick Marryat."
msgstr "Esta es una copia del \"El guardiamarina Easy\" de Frederick Marryat."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Peter Simple\" by Frederick Marryat."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Pedro Simple\" de Frederick Marryat."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "collector's edition book"
msgid_plural "collector's edition books"
msgstr[0] "libro de edición de coleccionista"
msgstr[1] "libros de edición de coleccionista"

#. ~ Description for collector's edition book
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A unique, valuable book that has been kept as a collector's item."
msgstr ""
"Un libro único y valioso que ha sido almacenado como un objeto de "
"coleccionista."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of Charles Dickens' \"A Tale of "
"Two Cities\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de cuero encuadernado de \"Historia de dos ciudades\" de "
"Charles Dickens."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very old but well-preserved copy of Charles Dickens' \"Oliver "
"Twist\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia antigua pero bien conservada de \"Oliver Twist\" de "
"Charles Dickens."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This high-quality copy of Jane Austen's \"Pride and Prejudice\" is dog-eared"
" and looks to have been read many times."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de alta calidad de \"Orgullo y prejuicio\" de Jan Austen. "
"Está doblado en las esquinas y parece haber sido leído muchas veces."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty, hardcover print of William Shinderling's \"Vanity before "
"Justice\" with beautiful illustrations."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran copia en tapa dura de \"Vanidad antes que justicia\" de "
"William Shinderling, con hermosas ilustraciones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Jane Austen's \"Sense and Sensibility\" has a certificate of "
"authenticity declaring it to be an early edition.  It would have been worth "
"an enormous amount of money, not long ago."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Sentido y sensibilidad\" de Jane Austen. Tiene un "
"certificado de autenticidad que la clasifica como una de las primeras "
"ediciones. Hubiera valido mucho dinero, no hace tanto tiempo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an excellent quality copy of \"To Kill a Mockingbird\" by Harper "
"Lee."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de excelente calidad de \"Matar a un ruiseñor\" de Harper "
"Lee."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of F. Scott Fitzgerald's \"The "
"Great Gatsby.\""
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de cuero encuadernado de alta calidad de \"El Gran "
"Gatsby\" de F. Scott Fitzgerald."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hefty, hardcover print of Michael Abanaderly's opus, \"Lady "
"Wanderlust\".  It is over a hundred years old, but doesn't look it."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran copia en tapa dura de \"Lady Wanderlust\", la gran obra de "
"Michael Abanaderly. Tiene cerca de cien años, pero no lo parece."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Ray Bradbury's \"Fahrenheit 451\" has a certificate of "
"authenticity declaring it to be an early edition.  It would have been worth "
"an enormous amount of money, not long ago."
msgstr ""
"Esta copia de \"Fahrenheit 451\" de Ray Bradbury tiene un certificado de "
"autenticidad que dice ser una primera edición. Podría haber valido una "
"fortuna en un pasado no muy lejano."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This high-quality copy of \"Pride and Prejudice and Zombies\" has been "
"autographed by the author."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de alta calidad de \"Orgullo, prejuicio y zombis\" "
"autografiada por el autor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of \"The Adventures of Huckleberry"
" Finn\" by Mark Twain.  It contains some margin notes which themselves are "
"quite old, and look to have been done by a scholar of some sort."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de cuero encuadernado de \"Las aventuras de Huckleberry "
"Finn\" de Mark Twain. Contiene algunas notas al margen bastante antiguas, "
"que parecen haber sido hechas por algún tipo de académico."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very nice print of Bram Stoker's \"Dracula\".  It has a "
"certificate of authenticity with it that declares it a genuine early "
"edition."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia muy buena de \"Drácula\" de Bram Stoker. Tiene un "
"certificado de autenticiad que la declara una de las primeras ediciones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This copy of Douglas Adams' \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" has a "
"certificate of authenticity declaring it to be a first edition, and is "
"autographed by the author himself."
msgstr ""
"Esta copia de \"La Guía del Autoestopista galactico\" de Douglas Adams tiene"
" un certificado de autenticidad que declara que es una primera edición, y "
"está autografiada por el propio autor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high-quality leather bound copy of the well-known classic \"Dark "
"Days Ahead\", by K. G. Ranade."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de cuero encuadernado de alta calidad del conocido clásico"
" \"Dark Days Ahead\" de K. G. Ranade."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a well-kept leather bound copy of \"Oryx and Crake\" by Margaret "
"Atwood.  Inscribed in the inner cover is a faded note wishing the owner a "
"happy birthday."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia encuadernada en cuero bien conservada de \"Oryx y Crake\" "
"de Margaret Atwood. En la cubierta interior hay una nota borrosa deseando al"
" propietario un feliz cumpleaños."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This bright orange hardcover copy of \"1984\" by George Orwell has been "
"carefully preserved, and appears to be a first or second edition judging "
"from the publisher's information."
msgstr ""
"Esta copia en tapa dura de un naranja chilón de \"1984\" de George Orwell ha"
" sido cuidadosamente conservada y parece ser una primera o segunda edición, "
"a juzgar por la información del editor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a very nice copy of \"Lady Chatterly's Lover\", probably quite "
"expensive in the days before the apocalypse."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia muy buena de \"El amante de Lady Chatterly\", "
"probablemente bastante valiosa en los días antes del apocalipsis."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a high quality early edition hardcover copy of \"The Handmaid's "
"Tale\" by Margaret Atwood, signed by the author."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia en tapa dura de alta calidad de \"El cuento de la criada\""
" de Margaret Atwood, firmada por la autora."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This ancient and worn book looks to be an 18th or early 19th century "
"handwritten copy of \"Don Quixote\".  In the days of book traders it would "
"have been worth an absolute fortune.  Now it's either a priceless piece of "
"history, some light reading before bed, or excellent kindling."
msgstr ""
"Este antiguo y desgastado libro parece ser una copia del siglo XVIII o "
"principios del XIX manuscrita a mano de \"El Quijote\". En los días de los "
"comerciantes de libros hubiera valido una absoluta fortuna. Ahora o bien es "
"una pieza inestimable de la Historia, una lectura ligera antes de irse a "
"dormir, o un combustible fantástico."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a first edition copy of Terry Pratchett's \"The Colour of Magic\".  "
"In the inner cover is a handwritten note that reads \"To Chris, thanks for "
"believing I could do it.  Best regards, Terry.\""
msgstr ""
"Esta es una primera edición de \"El color de la magia\" de Terry Pratchett. "
"En la cubierta interior hay una nota escrita a mano que dice \"Para Chris, "
"gracias por creer que podía hacerlo. Atentamente, Terry.\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Economicon of Dobbs"
msgid_plural "copies of The Economicon"
msgstr[0] "El Economicon"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Economicon"

#. ~ Description for The Economicon of Dobbs
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"These are the prescriptures Pile 18 Disk sg30 File 14.  \"Look, small brain "
"of pink earth inside my null-grasping, and she/he receives Logos; and it lay"
" with the Wor.\""
msgstr ""
"Estas son las prescripciones de la pila 18 del disco sg30 del archivo 14. "
"\"Mira, pequeño cerebro de tierra rosada dentro de mi nulidad, y recibe a "
"Logos; y se acostó con el Wor.\""

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Bobliographon"
msgid_plural "copies of The Bobliographon"
msgstr[0] "El Bobliographon"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Bobliographon"

#. ~ Description for The Bobliographon
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The back cover of this cheaply published paperback reads: \"These newly-"
"released SubGenius revelations will SHOCK those who think they know Bob!  "
"Unpredictables are not alone and possess amazing hidden powers of their own!"
"  In a world without slack, a yeti lust revival saunters about.  WARNING: Do"
" not fail to pay full price for this book; JHVH-1's wrath knows some "
"bounds.\""
msgstr ""
"La contraportada de esta edición barata de bolsillo dice: \"¡Estas "
"revelaciones de SubGenius recién publicadas impactarán a aquellos que creen "
"conocer a Bob! ¡Los impredecibles no están solos y poseen increíbles poderes"
" ocultos propios! En un mundo sin holguras, un Yeti lujurioso reavivador "
"anda por ahí. ADVERTENCIA: No dejes de pagar el precio completo de este "
"libro; la ira de JHVH-1 conoce algunos límites.\""

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Glimpses of Solomon in Yellow"
msgid_plural "copies of Solomon in Yellow"
msgstr[0] "Salomón en amarillo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Salomón en amarillo"

#. ~ Description for Glimpses of Solomon in Yellow
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This paperback is titled \"Glimpses of Solomon in Yellow; The Initiation "
"Rites of the Starry Wisdom Covenant, by Dr. Enoch Craven.\"  It describes "
"not just the investiture of new adherents, but the history and beliefs of "
"the Church of Starry Wisdom.  Someone has defaced the sparse citations "
"section by scrawling \"PUPPETS OF ROME!\" over its few pages.  The book does"
" not provide any biography for Dr. Craven, let alone academic credentials."
msgstr ""
"Este libro se titula \" Miradas de Salomón en amarillo; los ritos de "
"iniciación del Pacto de la Sabiduría Estelar, por el Dr. Enoch Craven\". "
"Describe no sólo la investidura de nuevos adherentes, sino la historia y las"
" creencias de la Iglesia de la Sabiduría Estelar. Alguien ha desfigurado la "
"escasa sección de citas garabateando \"¡Títeres de Roma!\" en sus pocas "
"páginas. El libro no proporciona ninguna biografía para el Dr. Craven, y "
"mucho menos credenciales académicas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of philosophy"
msgid_plural "books of philosophy"
msgstr[0] "libro de filosofía"
msgstr[1] "libros de filosofía"

#. ~ Description for book of philosophy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A deep discussion of morality with an emphasis on epistemology and logic."
msgstr ""
"Una profunda discusión sobre moralidad con el énfasis en la epistemología y "
"la lógica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Nietzsche's \"Beyond Good and Evil\".  Its cover is dog-"
"eared and creased."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Más allá del bien y del mal\" de Nietzsche. Su "
"portada esta doblada y arrugada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Unique and Its Property\" by Max Stirner.  A modern "
"translation by Wolfi Landstreicher."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Único y su Propiedad\" de Max Stirner. Una "
"traducción moderna de Wolfi Landstreicher."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large, extended version of \"Madness and Civilisation\" by Michel "
"Foucault.  The cover features a striking image of a Panopticonic Prison."
msgstr ""
"Una versión grande y extendida de \"Historia de la locura en la época "
"clásica\" de Michel Foucault. La portada muestra una impactante imagen de "
"una prisión panóptica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Postmodern Condition: A Report on Knowledge\" by "
"Lyotard."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La condición postmoderna\": Informe sobre el saber\" "
"de Lyotard."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of texts and essays by Jacques Derrida.  Its pages are loose "
"and yellowed - you should probably handle it with care."
msgstr ""
"Es una colección de textos y ensayos de Jacques Derrida. Las páginas están "
"sueltas y amarillentas - vas a tener que usarlo con cuidado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Society of the Spectacle\" by Guy Debord.  Its cover "
"shows rows of adults staring placidly into a screen."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Sociedad del Espectáculo\" de Guy Debord. Su "
"portada muestra filas de adultos mirando plácidamente a una pantalla."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a split copy of both \"An Ethic of Sexual Difference\" and \"This "
"Sex Which Is Not One\" by Luce Irigaray."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia dividida de \"Una Ética de la Diferencia Sexual\" y \"Ese "
"sexo que no es uno\" de Luce Irigaray."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Baudrillard's \"Simulation and Simulacra\".  The cover "
"contains an image of a man holding a colored pill in each hand, with the "
"caption \"Welcome to the Desert of the Real.\".  You think you've seen this "
"movie."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Simulación y Simulacro\" de Baudrillard. La portada "
"contiene una imagen de un hombre sosteniendo una píldora de color en cada "
"mano, con la leyenda \"Bienvenido al desierto de lo real\". Crees que has "
"visto esta película."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a small, pocket version of Sartre's \"Existentialism and Humanism\"."
"  It looks to have been used as a coaster in a past life."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una pequeña versión de bolsillo de \"El existencialismo es un "
"humanismo\" de Sartre. Parece haber sido usado como posavasos en una vida "
"pasada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Practical Ethics\" by Peter Singer.  From the local "
"university press."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Ética Práctica\" de Peter Singer. De la prensa "
"universitaria local."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a photocopied spiral-bound copy of \"Industrial Society and Its "
"Future\" by 'Freedom Club'.  The original looks to have been written on a "
"typewriter before being copied."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia fotocopiada en espiral de \"La sociedad industrial y su "
"futuro\" de 'Freedom Club'. El original parece haber sido escrito en una "
"máquina de escribir antes de ser copiado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Industrial Society and Its Future\" by Ted Kaczynski.  "
"Its cover is an image of a hand-crafted wooden box filled with wiring and an"
" ominous looking metal tube.  Provocative."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La sociedad industrial y su futuro\" de Ted "
"Kaczynski. Su portada es una imagen de una caja de madera hecha a mano, "
"llena de cables y un tubo de metal de aspecto ominoso. Provocativo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a small reader on Hegel's Dialectics."
msgstr "Este es un pequeño lector de La Dialéctica de Hegel."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The State and Revolution\" by Vladimir Lenin.  In "
"English, thankfully."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Estado y la Revolución\" de Vladimir Lenin. En "
"español, por suerte."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"In Defense of Marxism\" by Leon Trotsky."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"En defensa del marxismo\" de León Trotsky."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Steal This Book\" by Abbie Hoffman.  There is a security"
" tag on the back cover.  It appears to still be active."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Roba este libro\" de Abbie Hoffman. Hay una etiqueta "
"de seguridad en la contraportada. Parece que todavía está activa."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Walden: Or Life In The Woods\" by Henry David Thoreau.  "
"It contains a dried and pressed leaf as a bookmark."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Walden\" de Henry David Thoreau. Contiene una hoja "
"seca y prensada como marcador de libros."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Female Eunuch\" by Germaine Greer.  A child has "
"scribbled over the contents page in red crayon."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Mujer Eunuco\" de Germaine Greer. Un niño ha "
"garabateado sobre la página de contenidos con un lápiz rojo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"An Introduction to Metaphysics\" by Bergson."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Una introducción a la metafísica\" de Bergson."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Four Fundamental Concepts of Psychoanalysis\" by "
"Jacques Lacan."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Los Cuatro Conceptos Fundamentales del "
"Psicoanálisis\" de Jacques Lacan."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Machiavelli's \"The Prince\".  With intro by Q. Skinner."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Príncipe\" de Maquiavelo. Con introducción de Q. "
"Skinner."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"On The Revolution of Everyday Life\" by Raul Vangeigem."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La revolución de la vida cotidiana\" de Raoul "
"Vaneigem."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a pocket copy of \"An Essay on Liberation\" by Herbert Marcuse.  The"
" cover contains an image of a pelican."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de bolsillo de \"Un ensayo sobre la liberación\" de "
"Herbert Marcuse. La portada contiene una imagen de un pelícano."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Either-Or\" by Søren Kierkegaard."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"O lo uno o lo otro\" de Søren Kierkegaard."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Allegory of the Cave\" by Plato."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Alegoría de la Caverna\" de Platón."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Leviathan\" by Thomas Hobbes."
msgstr "Esta es una copia del \"Leviatán\" de Thomas Hobbes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Critique Of Pure Reason\" by Immanuel Kant."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Crítica de la Razón Pura\" de Immanuel Kant."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Principles of Philosophy\" by Descartes."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Principios de la Filosofía\" de Descartes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of both \"On The Genealogy of Morals\" and \"The Gay "
"Science\" by Friederich Nietzsche."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Genealogía de la moral\" y \"La gaya ciencia\" de "
"Friederich Nietzsche."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Myth of Sisyphus\", and other essays, by Albert "
"Camus.  The cover depicts a bare-chested man and a large boulder."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El mito de Sísifo\", y otros ensayos, de Albert "
"Camus. La portada muestra un hombre con el pecho desnudo y una gran roca."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Sickness Unto Death\" by Søren Kierkegaard.  The "
"pages are dotted with post-it notes."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La enfermedad mortal\" de Søren Kierkegaard. Las "
"páginas están salpicadas de notas post-it."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Defence of Terrorism\" by Leon Trotsky.  Despite the"
" title, it does not actually appear to be defending terrorism."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Defensa del Terrorismo\" de Leon Trotsky. A pesar "
"del título, no parece estar defendiendo el terrorismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Enquiry Concerning Political Justice\" by William "
"Godwin.  This thick book is filled with antiquated phrases."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Justicia Politica\" de William Godwin. Este grueso "
"libro está lleno de frases anticuadas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Abolition of Work and Other Essays\" by Bob Black.  "
"It is likely that \"The Abolition of Work\" is the most famous essay in this"
" book."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La abolición del trabajo y otros ensayos\" de Bob "
"Black. Es probable que \"La Abolición del Trabajo\" sea el ensayo más famoso"
" de este libro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"What is Property?\" by Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.  It looks"
" like this book has a surprisingly long track record of owners."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"¿Qué es la propiedad?\" de Pierre-Joseph Proudhon. "
"Parece que este libro tiene un sorprendente largo historial de propietarios."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Conquest of Bread\" by Peter Kropotkin.  There is a "
"picture of an old philosopher with magnificent beard, instead of bread, on "
"the cover."
msgstr ""
"Es una copia de \"La conquista del pan\" de Peter Kropotkin. En la tapa "
"tiene una imagen de un viejo filósofo con una barba magnífica, en lugar de "
"pan."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Trouble with Being Born\" by Emil Cioran.  This book"
" might have been printed decades before the Cataclysm since the cover is "
"quite weathered."
msgstr ""
"Es una copia de \"Del inconveniente de haber nacido\" de Emil Cioran. Este "
"libro puede haber sido impreso décadas antes del Cataclismo, ya que la tapa "
"está bastante desgastada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The World as Will and Representation\" by Arthur "
"Schopenhauer.  It contains a few undecipherable notes and scribbles."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El mundo como voluntad y representación\" de Arthur "
"Schopenhauer. Contiene algunas notas y garabatos indescifrables."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Up-Wingers: A Futurist Manifesto\" by FM-2030.  It seems"
" that the author's real name is Fereidoun M. Esfandiary."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Up-Wingers\": Un Manifiesto Futurista\" por FM-2030. "
"Parece que el nombre real del autor es Fereidoun M. Esfandiary."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Bastiat Collection\", a large collection of essays "
"by Frederic Bastiat."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Colección Bastiat\", una gran colección de ensayos"
" de Frederic Bastiat."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Anarchy, State, and Utopia\" by Robert Nozick, one of "
"the most influential books of modern libertarianism."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Anarquía, Estado y Utopía\" de Robert Nozick, uno de "
"los libros más influyentes del libertario moderno."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Socialism\" by Ludwig von Mises, a critical examination "
"of socialism."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Socialismo\" de Ludwig von Mises, un examen crítico "
"del socialismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The ABC of Communism\" by Nikolai Bukharin, one of the "
"most influential books of early Marxism-Leninism."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El ABC del Comunismo\" de Nikolai Bukharin, uno de "
"los libros más influyentes de los primeros tiempos del Marxismo-Leninismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Anti-Capitalist Mentality\" by Ludwig von Mises."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Mentalidad Anticapitalista\" de Ludwig von Mises."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Modal Logic as Metaphysics"
msgid_plural "copies of Modal Logic"
msgstr[0] "Lógica Modal"
msgstr[1] "copias de Lógica Modal"

#. ~ Description for Modal Logic as Metaphysics
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A treatise on applying logical tools to questions about that nature of "
"reality, this book contains detailed discussion of metaphysical issues."
msgstr ""
"Un tratado sobre la aplicación de herramientas lógicas a las preguntas sobre"
" esa naturaleza de la realidad, este libro contiene una discusión detallada "
"de temas metafísicos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Aesthetics: A Critical Anthology"
msgid_plural "copies of Aesthetics"
msgstr[0] "Estética"
msgstr[1] "copias de Estética"

#. ~ Description for Aesthetics: A Critical Anthology
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hardbound anthology presents a collection of readings, scholarly works,"
" and critical analyses on the subject of beauty."
msgstr ""
"Esta dura antología presenta una colección de lecturas, trabajos académicos "
"y análisis críticos sobre el tema de la belleza."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Philosophy of Information"
msgid_plural "copies of The Philosophy of Information"
msgstr[0] "La Filosofía de la Información"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Filosofía de la Información"

#. ~ Description for The Philosophy of Information
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This university text details a critical investigation of the conceptual "
"nature and basic principles of information.  The student will gain a "
"thorough appreciation of the conceptual frameworks commonly used to describe"
" and advance semantic investigations."
msgstr ""
"Este texto universitario detalla una investigación crítica de la naturaleza "
"conceptual y los principios básicos de la información. El estudiante "
"obtendrá una apreciación completa de los marcos conceptuales comúnmente "
"utilizados para describir y avanzar en las investigaciones semánticas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Being and Nothingness"
msgid_plural "copies of Being and Nothingness"
msgstr[0] "El Ser y la Nada"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Ser y la Nada"

#. ~ Description for Being and Nothingness
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This paperback is a copy of Jean-Paul Sartre's \"Being and Nothingness\".  A"
" key work in the existentialist tradition."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Ser y la Nada\" de Jean-Paul Sartre. Una obra "
"clave en la tradición existencialista."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "pulp novel"
msgid_plural "pulp novels"
msgstr[0] "novela pulp"
msgstr[1] "novelas pulp"

#. ~ Description for pulp novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hardboiled detective tale filled with hard hitting action and intrigue."
msgstr ""
"Un historia dura de detectives, llena de acción contundente e intriga."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Black Valkyries From Venus"
msgid_plural "copies of Black Valkyries"
msgstr[0] "Valkirias Negras Desde Venus"
msgstr[1] "copias de Valkirias Negras"

#. ~ Description for Black Valkyries From Venus
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You hold in your hands a weather-beaten novel written by someone named \"Lee"
" Racket.\""
msgstr ""
"Tienes en tus manos una novela gastada por el tiempo escrita por alguien "
"llamado \"Lee Racket\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Wrong Tomorrow"
msgid_plural "copies of Wrong Tomorrow"
msgstr[0] "El Mañana Equivocada"
msgstr[1] "copias de Mañana Equivocada"

#. ~ Description for The Wrong Tomorrow
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You hold in your hands a cheap drugstore paperback written by someone named "
"\"Lee Racket.\""
msgstr ""
"Tienes en tus manos un libro de bolsillo de una farmacia barata escrito por "
"alguien llamado \"Lee Racket\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "No God From a Corpse"
msgid_plural "copies of No God"
msgstr[0] "No hay Dios en un cadáver"
msgstr[1] "copias de No hay Dios"

#. ~ Description for No God From a Corpse
#. ~ 'Hard-boiled enough to break a spoon' means melodramatic, exaggerated,
#. emotional but simple, and possessing a general lack of literary pretense.
#. Weatherworn means damaged by age.  Skirt means woman.
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a weatherworn paperback written by some skirt named \"Lee Racket.\""
"  It tells how rage and jealousy can turn a man, or a woman, into a monster."
"  This story is hard-boiled enough to break a spoon."
msgstr ""
"Este es un libro de bolsillo gastado por el tiempo escrito por una mujer "
"llamada \"Lee Racket\". Cuenta cómo la rabia y los celos pueden convertir a "
"un hombre, o a una mujer, en un monstruo. Esta historia es tan dura como "
"para romper una cuchara."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Deep Dive"
msgid_plural "copies of Deep Dive"
msgstr[0] "Inmersión Profunda"
msgstr[1] "copias de Inmersión Profunda"

#. ~ Description for The Deep Dive
#. ~ Broad is a dismissive and outdated term that simply means "woman."  The
#. term is used because it evokes the (decidedly misogynistic) era in which
#. the pulp genre gained popularity within the United States.
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This dimestore short story about space travel is written by a broad named "
"\"Lee Racket.\""
msgstr ""
"Este cuento corto sobre los viajes espaciales está escrito por una mujer "
"llamada \"Lee Racket\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Planet of the Murderous Squids that Time Forgot!"
msgid_plural "copies of Planet of the Murderous Squids that Time Forgot!"
msgstr[0] "¡El Planeta de los calamares asesinos que el tiempo olvidó!"
msgstr[1] ""
"copias de ¡El Planeta de los calamares asesinos que el tiempo olvidó!"

#. ~ Description for Planet of the Murderous Squids that Time Forgot!
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this psychedelic adventure novel of cosmic exploration, an elderly "
"assassin discovers a planet too good to be true.  Only once it is too late "
"does she discover the harrowing truth at the center of \"The Planet of the "
"Murderous Squids that Time Forgot!\""
msgstr ""
"En esta novela de aventuras psicodélicas de exploración cósmica, un anciano "
"asesino descubre un planeta demasiado bueno para ser verdad. Sólo cuando es "
"demasiado tarde descubre la angustiosa verdad en el corazón de \"El planeta "
"de los calamares asesinos que el tiempo olvidó\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Great Capes of Metropolis"
msgid_plural "copies of The Great Capes of Metropolis"
msgstr[0] "Los Grandes Capas de Metrópolis"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Grandes Capas de Metrópolis"

#. ~ Description for The Great Capes of Metropolis
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this classic pulp paperback of superheroic exploits, a group of masked "
"vigilantes with diverse superpowers learn to work together to defeat the "
"ultimate villain."
msgstr ""
"En este clásico libro de bolsillo de hazañas superhéroicas, un grupo de "
"vigilantes enmascarados con diversos superpoderes aprenden a trabajar juntos"
" para derrotar al villano definitivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Yesterday's Murdered"
msgid_plural "copies of Yesterday's Murdered"
msgstr[0] "Asesinatos de Ayer"
msgstr[1] "copias de Asesinatos de Ayer"

#. ~ Description for Yesterday's Murdered
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this fast paced pulp noir, a hard-drinking detective with nerves of steel"
" has one last shot at vengeance."
msgstr ""
"En este rápido ritmo de novela noir, un detective bebedor con nervios de "
"acero tiene una última oportunidad de venganza."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Flashgun Condor and the Crimson Criminal"
msgid_plural "copies of Flashgun Condor and the Crimson Criminal"
msgstr[0] "Cóndor Flashgun y el criminal carmesí"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cóndor Flashgun y el criminal carmesí"

#. ~ Description for Flashgun Condor and the Crimson Criminal
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hot-blooded photographer who fights crime with film, footage, and fists, "
"Condor is more than a mere shutterbug on the crime beat.  But will she be "
"able to unravel a devious deception and bring the \"Crimson Criminal\" to "
"justice?"
msgstr ""
"Un fotógrafo de sangre caliente que combate el crimen con películas, "
"imágenes y puños, Cóndor es más que un mero obturador en el ritmo del "
"crimen. ¿Pero será capaz de desenredar un engaño retorcido y llevar al "
"\"Criminal Carmesí\" ante la justicia?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "scifi novel"
msgid_plural "scifi novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de ciencia ficción"
msgstr[1] "novelas de ciencia ficción"

#. ~ Description for scifi novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Aliens, ray guns, and space ships."
msgstr "Extraterrestres, pistolas de rayos y naves espaciales."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Gibson's \"Neuromancer\".  Written in the eighties, it was"
" surprisingly accurate in predicting much of modern society…  Until "
"recently."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia del \"Neuromante\" de Gibson. Escrito en los años 80, fue "
"sorprendentemente preciso en la predicción de gran parte de la sociedad "
"moderna... Hasta hace poco."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Stars My Destination\" by Alfred Bester.\n"
"\n"
"Tyger, Tyger, Burning bright,\n"
"In the forests of the night:\n"
"What immortal hand or eye,\n"
"Dare frame thy fearful symmetry?"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Las estrellas son mi destino\" de Alfred Bester.\n"
"\n"
"Tyger, Tyger, Ardiendo brillante,\n"
"En los bosques de la noche:\n"
"¿Qué mano u ojo inmortal,\n"
"¿Te atreves a enmarcar tu temible simetría?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Lathe of Heaven\" by Ursula Le Guin.  Dirty finger-"
"stains have smudged the occasional word."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Torno del Cielo\" de Ursula Le Guin. Sucias "
"manchas de dedos han manchado la palabra ocasional."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Dispossessed\" by Ursula Le Guin."
msgstr "Es una copia de \"Los desposeídos\" de Ursula Le Guin."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Hyperion\" by Dan Simmons."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Hyperion\" de Dan Simmons."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Endymion\" by Dan Simmons.  It opens with a poem by D.H. Lawrence:\n"
"\n"
"Give us gods.  Oh give them us!\n"
"Give us gods.\n"
"We are so tired of men\n"
"And motor-power."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Endymion\" de Dan Simmons. Se abre con un poema de D.H. Lawrence:\n"
"\n"
"\"Danos dioses\". ¡Oh, danos a ellos!\n"
"Danos dioses.\n"
"Estamos tan cansados de los hombres\n"
"Y la potencia de los motores."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Philip K. Dick's \"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"¿Sueñan los androides con ovejas eléctricas?\" de "
"Philip K. Dick."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a dog-eared copy of \"Nova Express\" by William Burroughs."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia marcada con una esquina doblada de \"Nova Express\" de "
"William Burroughs."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Foundation\" by Isaac Asimov.  The back cover has been "
"ripped off."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Fundación\" de Isaac Asimov. La contraportada ha sido"
" arrancada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Trial\" by Franz Kafka.  This book is rather worn."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Juicio\" de Franz Kafka. Este libro está bastante "
"gastado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Handmaid's Tale\" by Margaret Atwood."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"La historia de la sirvienta\" de Margaret Atwood."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Windup Girl\" by Paolo Bacigalupi.  The blurb makes "
"you wonder how Thailand fared the end of the world."
msgstr ""
"Es una copia de \"La chica mecánica\" de Paolo Bacigalupi. La nota en la "
"solapa te hace preguntarte cómo le fue a Tailandia en el fin del mundo. "

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Islands in the Net\" by Bruce Sterling."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Islas en la Red\" de Bruce Sterling."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Foundation and Empire\" by Isaac Asimov.  The back page "
"contains a hand-written grocery list."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Fundación e Imperio\" de Isaac Asimov. La última "
"página contiene una lista de la compra escrita a mano."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an almost new copy of  \"A Scanner Darkly\" by Philip K. Dick.  It "
"still has the smell of new books within its pages."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia casi nueva de \"A Scanner Darkly\" de Philip K. Dick. "
"Todavía tiene el olor de los libros nuevos dentro de sus páginas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Mirrorshades: A Cyberpunk Anthology\" compiled by Bruce "
"Sterling.  The cover has rings of coffee stains over it."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \" Sombras de espejo\": Una Antología Cyberpunk\" "
"compilada por Bruce Sterling. La cubierta tiene anillos de manchas de café "
"sobre ella."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The World of Null-A\" by A. E. van Vogt.  This copy "
"looks to have been used to press flowers."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El Mundo De Los No A\" de A. E. van Vogt. Esta copia "
"parece haber sido usada para prensar flores."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Altered Carbon\" by Richard Morgan."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Altered Carbon\" de Richard Morgan."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Mary Shelly's \"Frankenstein\".  Wasn't that the name of "
"the monster?"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Frankenstein\" de Mary Shelly. ¿No era ese el nombre "
"del monstruo?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Wasp\" by Eric Frank Russel.  The futuristic terrorist's"
" handbook."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Avispa\" de Eric Frank Russel. El manual del "
"terrorista futurista."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"I Am Legend\" by Richard Matheson.  The sleeve is "
"covered in dried blood."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Yo soy la leyenda\" de Richard Matheson. La manga "
"está cubierta de sangre seca."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Forever War\" by Joe Haldeman.  This copy looks as "
"if it's been slightly chewed by a dog or other large animal."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La guerra interminable\" de Joe Haldeman. Esta copia "
"parece como si hubiera sido ligeramente masticada por un perro u otro animal"
" grande."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Moon Is a Harsh Mistress\" by Robert A. Heinlein."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Luna es una cruel amante\" de Robert A. Heinlein."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Samuel R. Delany's \"Nova\".  The cover reads \"Review "
"Copy.  Not for re-sale.\""
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de la \"Nova\" de Samuel R. Delany. En la portada se lee "
"\"Copia para análisis\". No para reventa\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Vonnegut's \"The Sirens of Titan\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Las sirenas de Titán\" de Vonnegut."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Grass\" by Sheri S. Tepper.  A child has scribbled over "
"the first pages in crayon."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Hierba\" de Sheri S. Tepper. Un niño ha garabateado "
"sobre las primeras páginas en crayón."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of William Gibson's \"Count Zero\".  The spine is stamped "
"with 'Library Copy'.  And a sticker reading 'Science Fiction'."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Conde Cero\" de William Gibson. El lomo está sellado "
"con \"Copia de la biblioteca\". Y una pegatina que dice 'Ciencia Ficción'."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Weapon Makers\" by A. E. van Vogt."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Los fabricantes de armas\" de A. E. van Vogt."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Record of a Spaceborn Few\" by Becky Chambers.  It looks"
" almost brand new."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Record of a Spaceborn Few\" de Becky Chambers. Parece"
" casi nuevo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"Use of Weapons\" by Ian M. Banks.  The spine is cracked "
"and worn, some pages appear to be loose."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El uso de armas\" de Ian M. Banks. El lomo está "
"agrietado y desgastado, algunas páginas parecen estar sueltas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Jean-Baptiste Cousin de Grainville's \"Le Dernier Homme\"."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Le Dernier Homme\" de Jean-Baptiste Cousin de "
"Grainville."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Orwell's \"Nineteen Eighty-Four\".  The pages are loose "
"and thin.  You should probably be careful with this copy."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"1984\" de Orwell. Las páginas están sueltas y "
"delgadas. Probablemente deberías tener cuidado con esta copia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Heinlein's \"Stranger in a Strange Land\".  The cover is "
"dog-eared and worn."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El extraño en una tierra extraña\" de Heinlein. La "
"portada es de doblada y está desgastada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Orson Scott Card's \"Ender's Game\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia del \"El Juego de Ender\" de Orson Scott Card."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Lost World\" by Arthur Conan Doyle."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El Mundo Perdido\" de Arthur Conan Doyle."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Islands in the Sky\" by Arthur C. Clarke."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Islas en el cielo\" de Arthur C. Clarke."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of H. G. Wells' \"The Island of Doctor Moreau\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"La isla del Doctor Moreau\" de H. G. Wells."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Stanislaw Lem's \"His Masters Voice\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"La Voz de su Amo\" de Stanislaw Lem."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Fred Hoyle's \"The Black Cloud\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"La Nube Negra\" de Fred Hoyle."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Last and First Men\" by Olaf Stapeldon."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Primer y último hombre\" de Olaf Stapeldon."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Stanislaw Lem's \"Solaris\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Solaris\" de Stanislaw Lem."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Theodore Sturgeon's \"More Than Human\"."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Más que humano\" de Theodore Sturgeon."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Vurt\" by Jeff Noon."
msgstr "Es una copia de \"Vurt\" por Jeff Noon."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"A Canticle for Leibowitz\" by Walter M. Miller Jr."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Cántico para Leibowitz\" de Walter M. Miller Jr."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The War of The Worlds\" by H.G Wells."
msgstr "Es una copia de \"La guerra de los mundos\" de H.G. Wells."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Iron Sunrise\" by Charles Stross."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Amanecer de Hierro\" de Charles Stross."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of \"The Hunger Games\" by Suzanne Collins.  Reading the "
"blurb reminds you of a Japanese movie you think you once caught on the "
"television late at night."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"Los Juegos del Hambre\" de Suzanne Collins. La "
"lectura de la publicidad le recuerda a una película japonesa que cree que "
"una vez vio en la televisión a altas horas de la noche."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Day of the Triffids\" by John Wyndham."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"El día de los trífidos\" de John Wyndham."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"A Clockwork Orange\" by Anthony Burges."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"La Naranja Mecánica\" de Anthony Burges."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Man Who Fell to Earth\" by Walter Tevis."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"El hombre que vino de las estrellas\" de Walter "
"Tevis."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Simulacron-3\" by Daniel F. Galouye."
msgstr "Es una copia de \"Simulacron-3\" de Daniel F. Galouye."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"The Glass Bees\" by Ernst Jünger."
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Abejas de cristal\" de Ernst Jünger."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of \"Journey to The Center of the Earth\" by Jules Verne."
msgstr "Es una copia de \"Viaje al centro de la Tierra\" de Julio Verne."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a copy of Larry Niven's \"Ringworld\".  There are a couple of pages "
"missing from the end of the book.  Luckily only mail-order advertisements."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"MundoAnillo\" de Larry Niven. Faltan un par de "
"páginas al final del libro. Por suerte sólo hay anuncios por correo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a well-worn copy of \"The Hitchhikers Guide to the Galaxy\" by "
"Douglas Adams."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia muy usada de \"Guía del Autoestopista Galáctico\" de "
"Douglas Adams."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Dune"
msgid_plural "copies of Dune"
msgstr[0] "Dune"
msgstr[1] "copias de Dune"

#. ~ Description for Dune
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dog-eared copy of \"Dune\" by Frank Herbert.  It has sand between "
"some of its pages.  Weird."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia con hojas marcadas de \"Dune\" de Frank Herbert. Tiene "
"arena entre algunas de sus páginas. Qué raro."

#. ~ Description for Dune
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sturdy copy of \"Dune\" by Frank Herbert.  It is a fairly new "
"reprint with the words \"SOON TO BE A MAJOR MOTION PICTURE\" splashed across"
" its dust jacket."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia robusta de \"Dune\" de Frank Herbert. Es una reimpresión "
"bastante nueva con las palabras \"PRONTO SERÁ UNA GRAN PELICULA\" manchando "
"su sobrecubierta."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Parable of the Talents"
msgid_plural "copies of Parable of the Talents"
msgstr[0] "Parábola de los Talentos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Parábola de los Talentos"

#. ~ Description for Parable of the Talents
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a sturdy copy of \"Parable of the Talents.\".  It is Octavia "
"Butler's sequel to her book \"Parable of the Sower.\""
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia robusta de \"Parábola de los Talentos\". Es la secuela de "
"Octavia Butler de su libro \"Parábola del Sembrador\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Fifth Season"
msgid_plural "signed copies of Fifth Season"
msgstr[0] "La Quinta Estación"
msgstr[1] "copias firmadas de La Quinta Estación"

#. ~ Description for The Fifth Season
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a signed hardcover copy of the Hugo award winning \"The Fifth "
"Season\" by N.K. Jemisin.  It smells faintly of dirt."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de \"La Quinta Estación\" de N.K. Jemsin. Huele "
"ligeramente a tierra."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "We"
msgid_plural "copies of We"
msgstr[0] "Nosotros"
msgstr[1] "copias de Nosotros"

#. ~ Description for We
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hardback book is titled \"The Annotated We: A New Translation of Evgeny Zamiatin's Novel.\"\n"
"\n"
"It is Vladimir Wozniuk's 2015 translation of \"We,\" originally published in 1924 and generally seen as the first modern dystopian novel.  The commentary examines the profusive allusions and highlights the poetic nature of Zamiatin's language."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de tapa dura se titula \"El nosotros comentado\": Una nueva traducción de la novela de Evgeny Zamiatin\".\n"
"\n"
"Es la traducción de 2015 de \"Nosotros\" de Vladimir Wozniuk, publicada originalmente en 1924 y generalmente considerada como la primera novela distópica moderna. El comentario examina las profusas alusiones y destaca la naturaleza poética del lenguaje de Zamiatin."

#. ~ Description for We
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A seminal work of dystopian fiction, Evgeny Zamiatin's \"We\" was first published in 1924 but suppresed by the Soviet Union until 1988.\n"
"\n"
"This mass-market 1993 edition you've found was translated from the Russian by Clarence Brown and includes a short introduction.  The slightly worn cover features a surrealist photo of a person gazing backward suspiciouly."
msgstr ""
"Una obra fundamental de ficción distópica, \"Nosotros\" de Evgeny Zamiatin se publicó por primera vez en 1924, pero fue suprimida por la Unión Soviética hasta 1988.\n"
"\n"
"Esta edición de 1993 para el mercado de masas que has encontrado fue traducida del ruso por Clarence Brown e incluye una breve introducción. La cubierta ligeramente desgastada presenta una foto surrealista de una persona mirando hacia atrás con recelo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Cyberiad"
msgid_plural "copies of The Cyberiad"
msgstr[0] "Ciberiada"
msgstr[1] "copias de Ciberiada"

#. ~ Description for The Cyberiad
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This 350 page paperback presents the exploits and robotic rivalries of Trurl"
" and Klapaucius.  Originally written in Polish by Stanislaw Lem, it has been"
" masterfully translated into English by Michael Kandel."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de 350 páginas de bolsillo presenta las hazañas y rivalidades "
"robóticas de Trurl y Klapaucius. Originalmente escrito en polaco por "
"Stanislaw Lem, ha sido magistralmente traducido al inglés por Michael "
"Kandel."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Brave New World"
msgid_plural "copies of Brave New World"
msgstr[0] "Un Mundo Feliz"
msgstr[1] "copias de Un Mundo Feliz"

#. ~ Description for Brave New World
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is weather worn copy of \"Brave New World\" by Aldous Huxley looks like"
" it has been left out in rain.  The novel begins in a bleak building where "
"fetuses are grown in bottles on an assembly line."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia gastada por el tiempo de \"Un mundo feliz\" de Aldous "
"Huxley que parece haber sido dejada fuera bajo la lluvia. La novela comienza"
" en un edificio sombrío donde los fetos crecen en botellas en una línea de "
"montaje."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Roadside Picnic"
msgid_plural "copies of Roadside Picnic"
msgstr[0] "Picnic Extraterrestres"
msgstr[1] "copias de Picnic Extraterrestres"

#. ~ Description for Roadside Picnic
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a paperback copy of \"Roadside Picnic\" by Arkady and Boris "
"Strugatsky.  It has been translated into over 20 languages, occasionally "
"under the name \"Stalker.\"  This copy, fortunately for you, just happens to"
" be in your native tongue."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una copia de bolsillo de \"Picnic Extraterrestre\" de Arkady y Boris"
" Strugatsky. Ha sido traducida a más de 20 idiomas, ocasionalmente bajo el "
"nombre de \"Stalker\". Esta copia, afortunadamente para ti, resulta que está"
" en tu lengua materna."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Fahrenheit 451"
msgid_plural "copies of Fahrenheit 451"
msgstr[0] "Fahrenheit 451"
msgstr[1] "copias de Fahrenheit 451"

#. ~ Description for Fahrenheit 451
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This is a copy of Ray Bradbury's \"Fahrenheit 451.\""
msgstr "Esta es una copia de \"Fahrenheit 451\" de Ray Bradbury."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Some joker has gently burnt the exterior edge of this paperback dystopia.  "
"It's still perfectly readable."
msgstr ""
"Algún bromista ha quemado suavemente el borde exterior de esta distopía de "
"bolsillo. Todavía es perfectamente legible."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"\"It was a pleasure to burn.  It was a special pleasure to see things eaten,"
" to see things blackened and changed.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Fue un placer quemarlos. Fue un placer especial ver las cosas consumidas, "
"ver las cosas ennegrecidas y cambiadas.\""

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This 1979 softcover edition of Ray Bradbury's \"Fahrenheit 451\" was once a "
"library book.  It still has a light blue checkout card pocketed on the torn "
"back cover.  One \"Suzanne Collins\" borrowed it in 1981."
msgstr ""
"Esta edición de tapa blanda de 1979 de \"Fahrenheit 451\" de Ray Bradbury "
"fue una vez un libro de biblioteca. Todavía tiene una tarjeta de caja azul "
"claro metida en el bolsillo de la cubierta trasera rota. Una tal \"Suzanne "
"Collins\" lo tomó prestado en 1981."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The red and black paperback novel you hold in your hands is a modern reprint"
" of Ray Bradbury's \"Fahrenheit 451.\""
msgstr ""
"La novela de bolsillo roja y negra que tienes en tus manos es una "
"reimpresión moderna de \"Fahrenheit 451\" de Ray Bradbury."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This scifi novel is divided into three parts: \"The Hearth and the "
"Salamander,\" \"The Sieve and the Sand,\", and \"Burning Bright.\""
msgstr ""
"Esta novela de ciencia ficción se divide en tres partes: \"El Hogar y la "
"Salamandra\", \"El Colador y la Arena\", y \"Ardiente Brillante\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "sports novel"
msgid_plural "sports novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de deportes"
msgstr[1] "novelas de deportes"

#. ~ Description for sports novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The dramatic tale of a small-time boxer who gets a rare chance to fight the "
"heavy-weight champion, and seize his one chance to make a better life for "
"himself while impressing the cute girl who works in the pet store."
msgstr ""
"La historia dramática de un boxeador aficionado que tiene una extraña "
"oportunidad de pelear contra el campeón del peso pesado, e intenta agarrar "
"esta posibilidad de tener una mejor vida mientras impresiona a una chica "
"guapa que trabaja en la tienda de mascotas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Art of Bunting"
msgid_plural "copies of The Art of Bunting"
msgstr[0] "El Arte del Embocado"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Arte del Embocado"

#. ~ Description for The Art of Bunting
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"While you might be forgiven for expecting instructions for party decorating,"
" it is in fact a novel about baseball.  In the final climactic game a young "
"star proves to himself that he is ready for the big leagues."
msgstr ""
"Aunque se le perdone por esperar instrucciones para la decoración de la "
"fiesta, en realidad es una novela sobre el béisbol. En el juego final, una "
"joven estrella se prueba a sí misma que está lista para las grandes ligas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Touchdown Special"
msgid_plural "copies of The Touchdown Special"
msgstr[0] "El Touchdown Especial"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Touchdown Especial"

#. ~ Description for The Touchdown Special
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this absorbing novel of football fandom, a pizza delivery driver makes a "
"desperate gamble on the monday night game."
msgstr ""
"En esta absorbente novela de fútbol aleatorio, un repartidor de pizza hace "
"una apuesta desesperada en el juego del lunes por la noche."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Trophy Envy"
msgid_plural "copies of Trophy Envy"
msgstr[0] "Envidia de Trofeo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Envidia de Trofeo"

#. ~ Description for Trophy Envy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This paperback tells the story of a tennis prodigy who begins to regret her "
"own success."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de bolsillo cuenta la historia de un prodigio del tenis que "
"comienza a arrepentirse de su propio éxito."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Semi-Rough"
msgid_plural "copies of Semi-Rough"
msgstr[0] "Semi-Rugoso"
msgstr[1] "copias de Semi-Rugoso"

#. ~ Description for Semi-Rough
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This novel follows the humorous adventures of a professional athlete turned "
"amateur reporter."
msgstr ""
"Esta novela sigue las divertidas aventuras de un atleta profesional "
"convertido en reportero amateur."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Golf Omnivore"
msgid_plural "copies of The Golf Omnivore"
msgstr[0] "El Golfista Omnivoro"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Golfista Omnivoro"

#. ~ Description for The Golf Omnivore
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hardback book is a collection of short stories in which love and golf "
"are the only two constants."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de tapa dura es una colección de historias cortas en las que el "
"amor y el golf son las dos únicas constantes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Uniform Boy"
msgid_plural "copies of Uniform Boy"
msgstr[0] "Chico de Uniforme"
msgstr[1] "copias de Chico de Uniforme"

#. ~ Description for Uniform Boy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hardback book about an equipment manager for a minor league team "
"explores themes of loyalty and resentment."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de tapa dura sobre un director de equipo de una liga menor "
"explora temas de lealtad y resentimiento."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Budgetball: Winning a Rigged Game"
msgid_plural "copies of Budgetball"
msgstr[0] "Budgetball"
msgstr[1] "copias de Budgetball"

#. ~ Description for Budgetball: Winning a Rigged Game
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Budgetball tells the true story of the curious case of Benny Bobbin and his "
"quixotic quest to defeat the deep-pocketed Orlando O's."
msgstr ""
"Budgetball cuenta la verdadera historia del curioso caso de Benny Bobbin y "
"su quijotesca búsqueda para derrotar a los bolsillos profundos de Orlando "
"O's."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Lads of Summer"
msgid_plural "copies of The Lads of Summer"
msgstr[0] "Los Chicos de Verano"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Chicos de Verano"

#. ~ Description for The Lads of Summer
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This well worn paperback details the early baseball careers of one of the "
"greatest teams professional sports has ever known."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de de bolsillo detalla las primeras carreras de béisbol de uno de"
" los mayores equipos de deportes profesionales que se hayan conocido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Volleyball: Get Ready to Get Ready"
msgid_plural "copies of Volleyball"
msgstr[0] "Volleyball: Preparate Para Prepararte"
msgstr[1] "copias de Volleyball"

#. ~ Description for Volleyball: Get Ready to Get Ready
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"\"Volleyball: Get Ready to Get Ready\" is YOUR illustrated guide to level up"
" your game.  With full-color photos and diagrams, you will learn the drills "
"and techniques you need to dominate the competition."
msgstr ""
"\"Voleibol\": Prepárate para prepararte\" es TU guía ilustrada para subir el"
" nivel de tu juego. Con fotos y diagramas a todo color, aprenderás los "
"ejercicios y técnicas que necesitas para dominar a la competencia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "William G. Morgan, the Godfather of Volleyball"
msgid_plural "copies of The Godfather of Volleyball"
msgstr[0] "William G. Morgan, El Padrino del Voleibol"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Padrino del Voleibol"

#. ~ Description for William G. Morgan, the Godfather of Volleyball
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This odd little hardbound book is only 98 pages long, and a dozen of those "
"are comprised of grainy black and white photos.  If you read this book, you "
"learn that volleyball was originally called \"Mintonette\" and also some "
"biographic details about its inventor."
msgstr ""
"Este extraño libro de tapa dura sólo tiene 98 páginas, y una docena de ellas"
" están compuestas por fotos granuladas en blanco y negro. Si lees este "
"libro, aprenderás que el voleibol fue originalmente llamado \"Mintonette\" y"
" también algunos detalles biográficos sobre su inventor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Legendary Bike Rides"
msgid_plural "copies of Bike Rides"
msgstr[0] "Paseos en Bicicleta Legendarios"
msgstr[1] "copias de Paseos en Bicicleta"

#. ~ Description for Legendary Bike Rides
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This unwieldy coffeetable book is titled \"LEGENDARY Bike Rides Around the "
"WORLD.\"  It provides a wealth of detail about paved bike trails in every "
"part of the globe except New England.  But if you make it to Patagonia on "
"bike, you're all set."
msgstr ""
"Este inmanejable libro de mesa de café se titula \"Paseos LEGENDARIOS en "
"Bicicleta por el MUNDO\". Proporciona una gran cantidad de detalles sobre "
"los caminos pavimentados para bicicletas en todas partes del mundo, excepto "
"en Nueva Inglaterra. Pero si llegas a la Patagonia en bicicleta, estás "
"listo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Natare Ergo Sum"
msgid_plural "copies of Natare Ergo Sum"
msgstr[0] "Natare Ergo Sum"
msgstr[1] "copias de Natare Ergo Sum"

#. ~ Description for Natare Ergo Sum
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The poorly translated title is supposed to be Latin for \"I Swim, Therefore "
"I Am.\"  This short hardback presents \"A Philosophy of Swimming\" and then "
"playfully attributes a variety of famous philosophical expressions into "
"edorsements for the sport of swimming.  It's not a bad book, just a bit odd."
msgstr ""
"El título mal traducido se supone que es latín para \"Nado, luego existo\". "
"Este corto libro presenta \"Una filosofía de la natación\" y luego atribuye "
"juguetonamente una variedad de expresiones filosóficas famosas en los apoyos"
" para el deporte de la natación. No es un mal libro, sólo un poco extraño."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Stratosphere: The Rise of Hoops"
msgid_plural "copies of Stratosphere"
msgstr[0] "Estratosfera: El Ascenso de los Aros"
msgstr[1] "copias de Estratosfera"

#. ~ Description for Stratosphere: The Rise of Hoops
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"\"Stratosphere: The Rise of Hoops\" chronicles four decades of professional "
"basketball against a backdrop of sustained social change."
msgstr ""
"\"Estratosfera\": El Ascenso de los Aros\" relata cuatro décadas de "
"baloncesto profesional en un contexto de cambio social sostenido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Anything Can Be Beautiful"
msgid_plural "copies of Anything Can Be Beautiful"
msgstr[0] "Cualquier Cosa Puede Ser Hermosa"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cualquier Cosa Puede Ser Hermosa"

#. ~ Description for Anything Can Be Beautiful
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Stylist, designer, and glitter goddess, Tiffynie Blust looks at the world "
"one mantra in mind: anything can be beautiful."
msgstr ""
"Estilista, diseñadora y diosa de los brillos, Tiffynie Blust mira al mundo "
"con un mantra en mente: todo puede ser hermoso."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Greatest Rooms of the Century"
msgid_plural "copies of The Greatest Rooms of the Century"
msgstr[0] "Las Habitaciones Más Grandes del Siglo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Las Habitaciones Más Grandes del Siglo"

#. ~ Description for The Greatest Rooms of the Century
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stunning collection of the best living spaces created and commissioned by "
"the most influential people in interior design."
msgstr ""
"Es una colección impresionante de los mejores espacios para vivir creados y "
"encargados por la persona más influyente del diseño interior."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Hands-On Home"
msgid_plural "copies of The Hands-On Home"
msgstr[0] "El Hogar de las Manos"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Hogar de las Manos"

#. ~ Description for The Hands-On Home
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ecologically-minded take on modern homemaking, this is a practical guide "
"to maximising your time in the kitchen and beyond."
msgstr ""
"Una visión ecologista de las tareas domésticas modernas, esta es una guía "
"práctica para maximizar el tiempo en la cocina y más allá."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Rooms We Love"
msgid_plural "copies of Rooms We Love"
msgstr[0] "Habitaciones Que Amamos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Habitaciones Que Amamos"

#. ~ Description for Rooms We Love
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a guide on how to affordably decorate rooms to suit your "
"personality.  In the book, we visit rooms inspired by the needs of each "
"homeowner and will see how they transformed their rooms."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una guía sobre cómo decorar asequiblemente las habitaciones para que"
" se adapten a su personalidad. En el libro, visitamos habitaciones "
"inspiradas en las necesidades de cada propietario y veremos cómo "
"transformaron sus habitaciones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "New York Parties"
msgid_plural "copies of New York Parties"
msgstr[0] "Fiestas de New York"
msgstr[1] "copias de Fiestas de New York"

#. ~ Description for New York Parties
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Visit the homes of savvy tastemakers from the worlds of fashion, finance, "
"and design, with this book of lavish photography."
msgstr ""
"Visita las casas de los sabios creadores de gustos del mundo de la moda, las"
" finanzas y el diseño, con este libro de abundante fotografía."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Best Signature Outdoor Kitchens"
msgid_plural "copies of Best Signature Outdoor Kitchens"
msgstr[0] "La Mejor Marca de Cocinas al Aire Libre"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Mejor Marca de Cocinas al Aire Libre"

#. ~ Description for Best Signature Outdoor Kitchens
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Outdoor space is one of the hottest amenities being considered by new and "
"existing homeowners.  This book will show you how to turn any deck, patio, "
"or other outside area into a great place to cook."
msgstr ""
"El espacio exterior es una de las comodidades más calientes que están siendo"
" consideradas por los nuevos y los ya existentes propietarios. Este libro le"
" mostrará cómo convertir cualquier terraza, patio u otra área exterior en un"
" gran lugar para cocinar."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Art of Using Plants to Transform Your Home"
msgid_plural "copies of The Art of Using Plants to Transform Your Home"
msgstr[0] "El Arte de Usar Plantas Para Transformar Tu Hogar"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Arte de Usar Plantas Para Transformar Tu Hogar"

#. ~ Description for The Art of Using Plants to Transform Your Home
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Bring gorgeous greenery into your life with this delightful guide to "
"decorating your living space with a wide variety of plants.  Illustrated "
"examples enable you to easily transform every corner of your interior space."
msgstr ""
"Trae una hermosa vegetación a tu vida con esta encantadora guía para decorar"
" tu espacio vital con una amplia variedad de plantas. Los ejemplos "
"ilustrados te permiten transformar fácilmente cada rincón de tu espacio "
"interior."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Woman of Color"
msgid_plural "copies of Woman of Color"
msgstr[0] "Mujer de Color"
msgstr[1] "copias de Mujer de Color"

#. ~ Description for Woman of Color
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a collection of essays and advice on style, beauty, and motherhood."
"  Part memoir, part lifestyle guide, this book reflects the author's "
"experience growing up as a woman of color in Brooklyn."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de ensayos y consejos sobre estilo, belleza y "
"maternidad. Parte memorias, parte guía de estilo de vida, este libro refleja"
" la experiencia de la autora al crecer como mujer de color en Brooklyn."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "10 Cool Things About Being A Ring Bearer"
msgid_plural "copies of 10 Cool Things About Being A Ring Bearer"
msgstr[0] "10 Cosas Geniales de Ser Portador de un Anillo"
msgstr[1] "copias de 10 Cosas Geniales de Ser Portador de un Anillo"

#. ~ Description for 10 Cool Things About Being A Ring Bearer
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book is for the delightful little ring bearer in your wedding.  The "
"author depicts the responsibility and honor in being a ring bearer.  Your "
"little angel will cherish this book as he or she learns how to behave on "
"your perfect day."
msgstr ""
"Este libro es para el encantador portador de anillos de tu boda. El autor "
"describe la responsabilidad y el honor de ser un portador de anillos. Tu "
"angelito apreciará este libro mientras aprende a comportarse en tu día "
"perfecto."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "How to Raise a Gentleman: A Civilized Guide to Parenting"
msgid_plural ""
"copies of How to Raise a Gentleman: A Civilized Guide to Parenting"
msgstr[0] ""
"Cómo Criar a un Caballero: Una Guía Civilizada para la Crianza de los Hijos"
msgstr[1] ""
"copias de Cómo Criar a un Caballero: Una Guía Civilizada para la Crianza de "
"los Hijos"

#. ~ Description for How to Raise a Gentleman: A Civilized Guide to Parenting
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A revised edition for parents who hope their little boy children will grow "
"up to be the kind of men who know which fork to use, how to treat others, "
"and generally make their parents proud."
msgstr ""
"Una edición revisada para los padres que esperan que sus hijos pequeños "
"crezcan para ser el tipo de hombres que saben qué tenedor usar, cómo tratar "
"a los demás y, en general, hacer que sus padres se sientan orgullosos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"International Approaches to Securing Radioactive Sources Against Terrorism"
msgid_plural ""
"copies of International Approaches to Securing Radioactive Sources Against "
"Terrorism"
msgstr[0] ""
"Enfoques Internacionales Para Asegurar las Fuentes Radiactivas Contra el "
"Terrorismo"
msgstr[1] ""
"copias de Enfoques Internacionales Para Asegurar las Fuentes Radiactivas "
"Contra el Terrorismo"

#. ~ Description for International Approaches to Securing Radioactive Sources
#. Against Terrorism
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book presents how to enhance cooperation and assistance between "
"countries in support of International Atomic Energy Agency efforts to secure"
" radioactive sources against the threat of terrorism."
msgstr ""
"Este libro presenta cómo mejorar la cooperación y la asistencia entre los "
"países en apoyo de los esfuerzos del Organismo Internacional de Energía "
"Atómica para asegurar las fuentes radiactivas contra la amenaza del "
"terrorismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Principles of Forensic Psychiatry"
msgid_plural "copies of Principles of Forensic Psychiatry"
msgstr[0] "Principios de la Psiquiatría Forense"
msgstr[1] "copias de Principios de la Psiquiatría Forense"

#. ~ Description for Principles of Forensic Psychiatry
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This text addresses standards in the assessment and treatment of aggression "
"and violence as well as psychological and neuroimaging assessments."
msgstr ""
"Este texto aborda los estándares en la evaluación y tratamiento de la "
"agresión y la violencia, y también en la evaluación psicológica y la "
"neuroimagen."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Guide to Reflective Conflict Resolution"
msgid_plural "copies of The Guide to Reflective Conflict Resolution"
msgstr[0] "La Guía para la Resolución Reflexiva de Conflictos"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Guía para la Resolución Reflexiva de Conflictos"

#. ~ Description for The Guide to Reflective Conflict Resolution
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The back cover of this hardbound book reads: \"Why should professionals care"
" about reflective practice?  How do its principles and methods increase "
"competence?  What characteristics distinguish reflective practitioners?\""
msgstr ""
"La contraportada de este libro de tapa dura dice: \"¿Por qué los "
"profesionales deben preocuparse por la práctica de la reflexión? ¿Cómo "
"aumentan sus principios y métodos la competencia? ¿Qué características "
"distinguen a los profesionales de la reflexión?\""

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Oxbridge Handbook of Mood Ailments"
msgid_plural "copies of The Oxbridge Handbook of Mood Ailments"
msgstr[0] "El Manual de Oxbridge Sobre Dolencias del Estado de Ánimo"
msgstr[1] ""
"copias de El Manual de Oxbridge Sobre Dolencias del Estado de Ánimo"

#. ~ Description for The Oxbridge Handbook of Mood Ailments
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Oxbridge Handbook of Mood Ailments provides detailed coverage of the "
"characterization, understanding, and treatment of affective disorders.  It "
"provides coverage of unipolar depression, bipolar disorder, and known "
"variants of these illnesses."
msgstr ""
"El Manual de Oxbridge sobre dolencias del estado de ánimo ofrece una "
"cobertura detallada de la caracterización, comprensión y tratamiento de los "
"trastornos afectivos. Cubre la depresión unipolar, el trastorno bipolar y "
"las variantes conocidas de estas enfermedades."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Phonological Acquisition and Disorders"
msgid_plural "copies of Phonological Acquisition and Disorders"
msgstr[0] "Adquisición y Trastornos Fonológicos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Adquisición y Trastornos Fonológicos"

#. ~ Description for Phonological Acquisition and Disorders
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Studying the phonologies of children with non-organic speech disorders, this"
" volume details the latest findings in optimality theory, phonological "
"acquisition and disorders.  It is intended for linguists and psychologists."
msgstr ""
"Estudiando las fonologías de los niños con trastornos del habla no "
"orgánicos, este volumen detalla los últimos hallazgos en la teoría de la "
"optimización, la adquisición fonológica y los trastornos. Está dirigido a "
"lingüistas y psicólogos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Therapeutic Gardens and Healing Spaces"
msgid_plural "copies of Therapeutic Gardens and Healing Spaces"
msgstr[0] "Jardines Terapéuticos y Espacios de Curación"
msgstr[1] "copias de Jardines Terapéuticos y Espacios de Curación"

#. ~ Description for Therapeutic Gardens and Healing Spaces
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book addresses how to design therapeutic gardens.  It illustrates a "
"variety of landscape designs appropriate for public spaces that promote "
"mental health."
msgstr ""
"Este libro trata de cómo diseñar jardines terapéuticos. Ilustra una variedad"
" de diseños de paisajes apropiados para espacios públicos que promueven la "
"salud mental."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Advances in Drug Delivery Systems"
msgid_plural "copies of Advances in Drug Delivery Systems"
msgstr[0] "Avances en los Sistemas de Suministro de Drogas"
msgstr[1] "copias de Avances en los Sistemas de Suministro de Drogas"

#. ~ Description for Advances in Drug Delivery Systems
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This softcover reprint covers an array of topics in pharmacology.  The "
"physicochemical concepts of the refinement of bioresponsive drug delivery "
"are presented in detail alongside a variety of current approaches employed "
"in the development of zero order release systems."
msgstr ""
"Esta reimpresión en tapa blanda cubre una serie de temas de farmacología. Se"
" presentan en detalle los conceptos fisicoquímicos del perfeccionamiento de "
"la administración de drogas biorreactivas junto con una variedad de enfoques"
" actuales empleados en el desarrollo de sistemas de liberación de orden "
"cero."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Using Art to Treat Eating Disorders"
msgid_plural "copies of Using Art to Treat Eating Disorders"
msgstr[0] "Uso del Arte para Tratar los Trastornos Alimenticios"
msgstr[1] "copias de Uso del Arte para Tratar los Trastornos Alimenticios"

#. ~ Description for Using Art to Treat Eating Disorders
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an introductory guide for those wanting to explore the use of art to"
" address eating disorders.  Art therapy is a particularly effective "
"therapeutic intervention, as it allows people to express uncomfortable "
"thoughts and feelings nonverbally."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una guía introductoria para aquellos que quieran explorar el uso del"
" arte para tratar los trastornos de la alimentación. La terapia artística es"
" una intervención terapéutica particularmente efectiva, ya que permite a las"
" personas expresar pensamientos y sentimientos incómodos de forma no verbal."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A Clinical Guide to Video Gamers"
msgid_plural "copies of A Clinical Guide to Video Gamers"
msgstr[0] "Una Guía Clínica para los Jugadores de Videojuegos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Una Guía Clínica para los Jugadores de Videojuegos"

#. ~ Description for A Clinical Guide to Video Gamers
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This scholarly work considers the role that games play in psychological "
"experiences and mental health.  Chapters examine the factors that compel "
"individual gamers to select and identify with particular games and "
"characters, as well as the different play styles, genres, and archetypes "
"common in video games."
msgstr ""
"Este trabajo académico considera el papel que los juegos juegan en las "
"experiencias psicológicas y la salud mental. Los capítulos examinan los "
"factores que obligan a los jugadores individuales a seleccionar y a "
"identificarse con determinados juegos y personajes, así como los diferentes "
"estilos de juego, géneros y arquetipos comunes en los videojuegos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Paranoia and the History of Madness"
msgid_plural "copies of Paranoia and the History of Madness"
msgstr[0] "Paranoia y la Historia de la Locura"
msgstr[1] "copias de Paranoia y la Historia de la Locura"

#. ~ Description for Paranoia and the History of Madness
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book is an analysis of the use and misuse of paranoia throughout "
"history and in contemporary society.  The impact of paranoia on societies is"
" explored in detail."
msgstr ""
"Este libro es un análisis del uso y mal uso de la paranoia a lo largo de la "
"historia y en la sociedad contemporánea. Se explora en detalle el impacto de"
" la paranoia en las sociedades."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Psychoanalysis and Colonialism"
msgid_plural "copies of Psychoanalysis and Colonialism"
msgstr[0] "Psicoanálisis y el Colonialismo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Psicoanálisis y el Colonialismo"

#. ~ Description for Psychoanalysis and Colonialism
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Freud referred to women's sexuality as a \"dark continent\" for "
"psychoanalysis, drawing on colonial use of the same phrase to refer to "
"Africa.  This book details how the problematic universalism of "
"psychoanalysis led theorists to reject its relevance for postcolonial "
"critique."
msgstr ""
"Freud se refirió a la sexualidad de las mujeres como un \"continente "
"oscuro\" para el psicoanálisis, basándose en el uso colonial de la misma "
"frase para referirse a África. Este libro detalla cómo el problemático "
"universalismo del psicoanálisis llevó a los teóricos a rechazar su "
"relevancia para la crítica postcolonial."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Psychology of Stalking"
msgid_plural "copies of The Psychology of Stalking"
msgstr[0] "La Psicología del Acecho"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Psicología del Acecho"

#. ~ Description for The Psychology of Stalking
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book explores stalking from social, psychiatric, psychological and "
"behavioral perspectives.  Topics include psychiatric diagnoses, offender-"
"victim typologies, cyberstalking, false victimization syndrome, erotomania, "
"domestic violence, the stalking of public figures, and many other aspects of"
" stalking."
msgstr ""
"Este libro explora el acecho desde las perspectivas social, psiquiátrica, "
"psicológica y de comportamiento. Los temas incluyen diagnósticos "
"psiquiátricos, tipologías de delincuentes y víctimas, ciberacecho, síndrome "
"de falsa victimización, erotomanía, violencia doméstica, el acecho de "
"figuras públicas y muchos otros aspectos del acecho."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Tactical Handgun Digest"
msgid_plural "issues of Tactical Handgun Digest"
msgstr[0] "Manejo de Armas Tácticas"
msgstr[1] "Ediciones de Manejo de Armas Tácticas"

#. ~ Description for Tactical Handgun Digest
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A glossy magazine all about handguns and shooting.  There is a good article "
"about proper sighting near the middle."
msgstr ""
"Una revista brillante sobre pistolas y su uso. Tiene un buen artículo sobre "
"la manera apropiada de apuntarle al centro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Tao of the Handgun"
msgid_plural "copies of The Tao of the Handgun"
msgstr[0] "El Tao de las Pistolas"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Tao de las Pistolas"

#. ~ Description for The Tao of the Handgun
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This introspective volume covers proper usage of handguns, from safety and "
"stance, to maintenance and proper sighting technique."
msgstr ""
"Este volumen introspectivo especifica el uso apropiado de las pistolas, "
"desde la seguridad y la postura, hasta el mantenimiento y la técnica "
"adecuada para apuntar."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Modern Rifleman"
msgid_plural "issues of Modern Rifleman"
msgstr[0] "Tirador Moderno"
msgstr[1] "ediciones del Tirador Moderno"

#. ~ Description for Modern Rifleman
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An informative magazine all about rifles and shooting.  There is an "
"excellent article about proper maintenance in this issue."
msgstr ""
"Una revista informativa sobre rifles y su uso. Tiene un excelente artículo "
"acerca de la técnica apropiada de mantenimiento."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "FM 23-16 Army marksmanship manual"
msgid_plural "FM 23-16 Army marksmanship manuals"
msgstr[0] "manual Militar de Puntería FM 23-16"
msgstr[1] "manuales Militares de Puntería FM 23-16"

#. ~ Description for FM 23-16 Army marksmanship manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hefty military field manual about automatic rifle usage and techniques "
"which improve marksmanship and proper weapons-handling."
msgstr ""
"Un manual robusto de temática militar acerca del uso de rifles automáticos y"
" las técnicas para mejorar la puntería, y el manejo adecuado de las armas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Trap and Field"
msgid_plural "issues of Trap and Field"
msgstr[0] "Trampa y Campo"
msgstr[1] "fascículos de Trampa y Campo"

#. ~ Description for Trap and Field
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An in-depth magazine all about shotguns and shooting.  There is an "
"informative article about proper shooting stance in the back pages."
msgstr ""
"Una revista detallada sobre escopetas y su uso. Tiene un artículo "
"informativo sobre la posición adecuada de tiro en las últimas páginas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Shotguns: The Art and Science"
msgid_plural "copies of Shotguns: The Art and Science"
msgstr[0] "Escopetas: El Arte y la Ciencia"
msgstr[1] "copias de Escopetas: El Arte y la Ciencia"

#. ~ Description for Shotguns: The Art and Science
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book claims to address every problem the shotgunner is likely to face, "
"and offers solutions to ensure that shooters can make every shot count."
msgstr ""
"Este libro dice conocer cada problema que alguien con una escopeta puede "
"encontrarse, y ofrece soluciones para asegurarse de que cada disparo sirva."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Submachine Gun Enthusiast"
msgid_plural "issues of Submachine Gun Enthusiast"
msgstr[0] "El Entusiasta de los Subfusiles"
msgstr[1] "Ediciones de El Entusiasta de los Subfusiles"

#. ~ Description for Submachine Gun Enthusiast
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An in-depth magazine about submachine guns and shooting.  There is an "
"exhaustive article about close quarter combat techniques in the front."
msgstr ""
"Una revista detallada sobre subfusiles y su uso. Tiene un artículo "
"exhaustivo acerca de técnicas de combate en espacios cerrados en el frente "
"de batalla."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Submachine Gun Handbook"
msgid_plural "copies of The Submachine Gun Handbook"
msgstr[0] "El Manual del Subfusil"
msgstr[1] "copias del El Manual del Subfusil"

#. ~ Description for The Submachine Gun Handbook
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This concise guide details the proper care and operation of most forms of "
"machine pistols and submachine guns currently used by regular armed and "
"reserve forces, as well as several obsolete weapons."
msgstr ""
"Esta concisa guía detalla el cuidado y el funcionamiento adecuado de la "
"mayoría de las formas de pistolas ametralladoras y subfusiles que utilizan "
"actualmente las fuerzas armadas regulares y de reserva, así como varias "
"armas obsoletas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "US Weekly"
msgid_plural "US Weeklies"
msgstr[0] "EEUU Semanal"
msgstr[1] "EEUU Semanal"

#. ~ Description for US Weekly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Weekly news about a bunch of famous people who're all (un)dead now."
msgstr ""
"Noticias semanales acerca de un montón de gente famosa que ahora son "
"cadáveres o zombis."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Self-Esteem for Dummies"
msgid_plural "copies of Self-Esteem for Dummies"
msgstr[0] "Autoestima para Tontos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Autoestima para Tontos"

#. ~ Description for Self-Esteem for Dummies
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Full of useful tips for showing confidence in your speech."
msgstr "Lleno de consejos útiles para demostrar confianza en tus palabras."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Principles of Effective Communication"
msgid_plural "copies of Principles of Effective Communication"
msgstr[0] "Principios de la Comunicación Eficaz"
msgstr[1] "copias de los Principios de la Comunicación Eficaz"

#. ~ Description for Principles of Effective Communication
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A hardbound book devoted to being an effective and persuasive speaker."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de tapa dura dedicado a cómo ser un orador efectivo y persuasivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Dungeon Master's Guide: 6th Edition"
msgid_plural "copies of Dungeon Master's Guide: 6th Edition"
msgstr[0] "Guía del Maestro de Mazmorras: 6ta edición"
msgstr[1] "copias de Guía del Maestro de Mazmorras: 6ta edición"

#. ~ Description for Dungeon Master's Guide: 6th Edition
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A thick, hardcover volume with everything needed to weave legendary stories."
"  It's full of information, but finding the things you're looking for can be"
" a chore."
msgstr ""
"Un grueso volumen de tapa dura con todo lo necesario para crear legendarias "
"historias. Está lleno de información, pero encontrar lo que deseas puede ser"
" una faena."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Nail Your Law Firm Interview"
msgid_plural "copies of Nail Your Law Firm Interview"
msgstr[0] "Borda Tu Entrevista Con Una Firma de Abogados"
msgstr[1] "copias de Borda Tu Entrevista Con Una Firma de Abogados"

#. ~ Description for Nail Your Law Firm Interview
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This lightweight book proclaims itself to be \"the ONLY gold star interview "
"guide for lawyers interviewing in any type of a job interview.\"  It was "
"supposed to help new lawyers find work."
msgstr ""
"Este libro ligero se proclama como \"la ÚNICA guía de entrevistas para "
"abogados en cualquier tipo de entrevista de trabajo\". Se suponía que "
"ayudaba a los nuevos abogados a encontrar trabajo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "holybook abstract"
msgid_plural "holybook abstracts"
msgstr[0] "libro sagrado abstracto"
msgstr[1] "libros sagrados abstractos"

#. ~ Description for holybook abstract
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "theoretically this isn't a book at all"
msgstr "teóricamente, esto ni siquiera es un libro"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Mycenacean Hymns"
msgid_plural "copies of Mycenacean Hymns"
msgstr[0] "Himnos Micénicos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Himnos Micénicos"

#. ~ Description for Mycenacean Hymns
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A vellum book containing the hymns central to Marloss faith.  As the verses "
"lead to each other, the text sings of unity and promised paradise."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de vitela que contiene los himnos centrales de la fe de Marloss. A "
"medida que los versos se unen, el texto canta sobre la unidad y el paraíso "
"prometido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "King James Bible"
msgid_plural "copies of King James Bible"
msgstr[0] "Biblia del Rey Jacobo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Biblia del Rey Jacobo"

#. ~ Description for King James Bible
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An English translation of the Christian Bible, which originated in England "
"in the early 1600s."
msgstr ""
"Una traducción al español de la Biblia Cristiana, que fue originada en "
"Inglaterra a principios del siglo XVII."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Eastern Orthodox Bible"
msgid_plural "copies of Eastern Orthodox Bible"
msgstr[0] "Biblia Ortodoxa Oriental"
msgstr[1] "copias de la Biblia Ortodoxa Oriental"

#. ~ Description for Eastern Orthodox Bible
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "An English copy of the Eastern Orthodox translation of The Holy Bible."
msgstr ""
"Una copia en español de la versión Ortodoxa de Oriente de la Santa Biblia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Gideon Bible"
msgid_plural "copies of Gideon Bible"
msgstr[0] "Biblia de Gideon"
msgstr[1] "copias de la Biblia de Gideon"

#. ~ Description for Gideon Bible
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An English translation of the Christian Bible, distributed free of charge by"
" Gideons International."
msgstr ""
"Una copia en español de la Biblia Cristiana, distribuida gratuitamente por "
"los Gedeones Internacionales."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Guru Granth Sahib"
msgid_plural "copies of The Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr[0] "El Gurú Granth Sahib"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Gurú Granth Sahib"

#. ~ Description for The Guru Granth Sahib
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A single-volume copy of the central religious texts of Sikhism."
msgstr "Una copia de un solo volumen del texto religioso central del Sijismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Hadith"
msgid_plural "copies of Hadith"
msgstr[0] "Hadith"
msgstr[1] "copias de Hadith"

#. ~ Description for Hadith
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A Muslim religious text containing an account of the sayings and actions of "
"the prophet Muhammad."
msgstr ""
"Un texto religioso musulmán, que contiene un recuento de las palabras y las "
"acciones del profeta Muhammad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Principia Discordia"
msgid_plural "copies of Principia Discordia"
msgstr[0] "Principia Discordia"
msgstr[1] "copias del Principia Discordia"

#. ~ Description for Principia Discordia
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book that embodies the main beliefs of Discordianism.  It seems to "
"primarily concern chaos, and features a card in the back which informs you "
"that you are now a 'genuine and authorized Pope of Discordia'."
msgstr ""
"Un libro que personifica las creencias principales del Discordianismo. "
"Parece concernir primeramente al caos, e incluye una carta en la parte de "
"atrás que te informa que ya eres un 'genuino y autorizado Papa de la "
"Discordia'."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Kojiki"
msgid_plural "copies of The Kojiki"
msgstr[0] "Kojiki"
msgstr[1] "copias del Kojiki"

#. ~ Description for The Kojiki
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The oldest extant chronicle of Japan's myths and history, the stories "
"contained in the Kojiki are part of the inspiration behind Shinto practices."
msgstr ""
"Es la crónica más antigua existente de la historia y los mitos japoneses. "
"Las historias que contiene el Kojiki son parte de la inspiración detrás de "
"las prácticas del Sintoísmo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Book of Mormon"
msgid_plural "copies of The Book of Mormon"
msgstr[0] "El libro del Mormón"
msgstr[1] "copias de El libro del Mormón"

#. ~ Description for The Book of Mormon
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The sacred text of the Latter Day Saint movement of Christianity, originally"
" published in 1830 by Joseph Smith."
msgstr ""
"El texto sagrado del Movimiento de los Santos de los Últimos Días del "
"Cristianismo, originalmente publicado en 1830 por Joseph Smith."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Gospel of the Flying Spaghetti Monster"
msgid_plural "copies of The Gospel of the Flying Spaghetti Monster"
msgstr[0] "El Evangelio del Monstruo del Espagueti Volador"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Evangelio del Monstruo del Espagueti Volador"

#. ~ Description for The Gospel of the Flying Spaghetti Monster
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book that embodies the main beliefs of the Church of the Flying Spaghetti "
"Monster.  It seems to involve a lot of pirates and some sort of invisible "
"drunken monster made of pasta."
msgstr ""
"Un libro que personifica las principales creencias de la Iglesia del "
"Monstruo del Espagueti Volador. Parece implicar muchos piratas y alguna "
"clase de monstruo borracho invisible hecho con pasta."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Quran"
msgid_plural "copies of Quran"
msgstr[0] "Corán"
msgstr[1] "copias del Corán"

#. ~ Description for Quran
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An English translation of the Muslim book of holy scriptures, with "
"explanatory notes and commentaries to aid in understanding."
msgstr ""
"Un traducción al español del libro musulmán de las santas escrituras, con "
"notas explicativas y comentarios para facilitar su comprensión."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Satanic Bible"
msgid_plural "copies of The Satanic Bible"
msgstr[0] "La Biblia Satánica"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Biblia Satánica"

#. ~ Description for The Satanic Bible
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of essays, observations, and rituals published by Anton LaVey "
"in 1969."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de ensayos, observaciones y rituales publicados por Anton "
"LaVey en 1969."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Dianetics"
msgid_plural "copies of Dianetics"
msgstr[0] "Dianética"
msgstr[1] "copias de Dianética"

#. ~ Description for Dianetics
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book is the canonical text of Scientology.  Written by a science "
"fiction author, it contains self-improvement techniques and musings on "
"psychology called Dianetics."
msgstr ""
"Este libro es el texto canónico de la Cienciología. Escrito por un autor de "
"ciencia ficción, contiene técnicas de auto-mejoramiento y reflexiones sobre "
"psicología llamadas Diánetica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Book of the SubGenius"
msgid_plural "copies of The Book of the SubGenius"
msgstr[0] "El Libro de los Subgenios"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Libro de los Subgenios"

#. ~ Description for The Book of the SubGenius
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book about the Church of the SubGenius.  It seems to involve a salesman "
"named J. R. \"Bob\" Dobbs and a concept called 'slack'."
msgstr ""
"Un libro sobre la Iglesia de los Subgenios. Parece que implica un vendedor "
"llamado J. R. \"Bob\" Dobbs y un concepto denominado 'slack'."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Sutras of the Buddha"
msgid_plural "copies of The Sutras of the Buddha"
msgstr[0] "Los Sutras de Buda"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Sutras de Buda"

#. ~ Description for The Sutras of the Buddha
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of discourses attributed to the Buddha and his close disciples."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de los discursos atribuidos a Buda y sus discípulos cercanos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Talmud"
msgid_plural "copies of the Talmud"
msgstr[0] "Talmud"
msgstr[1] "copias del Talmud"

#. ~ Description for Talmud
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"One of the central texts of Rabbinic Judaism, the Talmud expounds upon the "
"Hebrew Bible with teachings and opinions of thousands of rabbis."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los textos centrales del Judaísmo Rabínico, el Talmud explica en "
"profundidad la Biblia Hebrea con enseñanzas y opiniones de cientos de "
"rabinos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Tanakh"
msgid_plural "copies of Tanakh"
msgstr[0] "Tanakh"
msgstr[1] "copias de Tanakh"

#. ~ Description for Tanakh
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A single-volume book containing the complete canon of the Jewish Bible."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de un solo volumen que contiene el canon completo de la Biblia "
"Judía."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Tripitaka"
msgid_plural "copies of The Tripitaka"
msgstr[0] "El Tripitaka"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Tripitaka"

#. ~ Description for The Tripitaka
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of sacred Buddhist writings describing their canons of "
"scriptures."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de textos sagrados Budistas, que describen los cánones de las "
"escrituras."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Upanishads"
msgid_plural "copies of The Upanishads"
msgstr[0] "Los Upanishad"
msgstr[1] "copias de los Upanishad"

#. ~ Description for The Upanishads
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of sacred Hindu writings regarding the nature of reality and "
"describing the character and form of human salvation."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de textos sagrados Hindúes, acerca de la naturaleza de la "
"realidad, y describiendo la forma y el carácter de la salvación humana."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Four Vedas"
msgid_plural "copies of The Four Vedas"
msgstr[0] "Los Cuatro Vedas"
msgstr[1] "copias de los Cuatro Vedas"

#. ~ Description for The Four Vedas
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A single volume containing all four Vedas, which are the oldest scriptures "
"of Hinduism."
msgstr ""
"Un volumen que contiene los cuatro Vedas, que son las escrituras más "
"antiguas del Hinduismo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Hávamál"
msgid_plural "copies of Hávamál"
msgstr[0] "Hávamál"
msgstr[1] "copias del Hávamál"

#. ~ Description for Hávamál
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An English translation of several Old Norse poems.  The poems contain "
"proverbs and stories attributed to the god Odin, many transcribed from oral "
"history."
msgstr ""
"Una traducción inglesa de varios poemas del nórdico antiguo. Los poemas "
"contienen proverbios e historias atribuidas al dios Odín, muchas transcritas"
" de la historia oral."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Duelist's Annual"
msgid_plural "Duelist's Annuals"
msgstr[0] "Duelistas Anual"
msgstr[1] "Duelistas Anual"

#. ~ Description for Duelist's Annual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An annual publication about fencing and dueling.  There are many good "
"illustrations which describe proper technique and form."
msgstr ""
"Una publicación anual sobre esgrima y duelos. Tiene muchas ilustraciones que"
" describen la técnica y la postura adecuadas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "FM 23-25 Army bayonet manual"
msgid_plural "FM 23-25 Army bayonet manuals"
msgstr[0] "manual FM 23-25 de Bayoneta Militar"
msgstr[1] "manuales FM 23-25 de Bayoneta Militar"

#. ~ Description for FM 23-25 Army bayonet manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A hefty military field manual about bayonet usage and combat theory."
msgstr ""
"Un robusto manual militar acerca del uso de la bayoneta y la teoría del "
"combate."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Spetsnaz Knife Techniques"
msgid_plural "copies of Spetsnaz Knife Techniques"
msgstr[0] "Técnicas de Cuchillos Spetsnaz"
msgstr[1] "copias de Técnicas de Cuchillos Spetsnaz"

#. ~ Description for Spetsnaz Knife Techniques
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A classic Soviet text on the art of attacking with a blade."
msgstr "Un texto clásico soviético sobre el arte de atacar con una cuchilla."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Survival Under Atomic Attack"
msgid_plural "copies of Survival Under Atomic Attack"
msgstr[0] "Sobrevivir Bajo Ataques Atómicos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Sobrevivir Bajo Ataques Atómicos"

#. ~ Description for Survival Under Atomic Attack
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wordy and intricate guide to wilderness and urban survival in a worst-case"
" scenario.  While filled with loads of useful information, the madman who "
"wrote this was a terrible writer, and gleaning knowledge from the rants is a"
" chore."
msgstr ""
"Una guía de palabras e intrincada para la supervivencia en la naturaleza y "
"en la ciudad en el peor de los casos. Aunque lleno de información útil, el "
"loco que escribió esto era un escritor terrible, y recoger conocimientos de "
"las declaraciones es una molestia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Through the Lens"
msgid_plural "copies of Through the Lens"
msgstr[0] "A Través de las Lentes"
msgstr[1] "copias de A Través de las Lentes"

#. ~ Description for Through the Lens
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A colorful digest devoted to backpacking and wilderness photography.  The "
"photos are beautiful, though the terminology in the sections on "
"survivalcraft assume some proficiency."
msgstr ""
"Un colorido compendio acerca de la fotografía de naturaleza y de mochilero. "
"Las fotos son hermosas, aunque la terminología de las secciones sobre el "
"arte de la supervivencia requieren cierta competencia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Alpha Male Quarterly"
msgid_plural "Alpha Male Quarterlies"
msgstr[0] "Macho Alfa Trimestral"
msgstr[1] "Macho Alfa Trimestral"

#. ~ Description for Alpha Male Quarterly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a full-size glossy men's magazine.  There's a brief article about "
"hiking and a list of simple wilderness survival tips somewhere in between "
"the photos of bikini-clad women and the gadget advertisements."
msgstr ""
"Una revista brillante para hombres. Tiene un pequeño artículo sobre "
"excursionismo y una listo de consejos simples para la supervivencia al aire "
"libre, entre fotos de mujeres en bikini y publicidades de artefactos "
"electrónicos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Outdoor Adventures"
msgid_plural "issues of Outdoor Adventures"
msgstr[0] "Aventuras al Aire Libre"
msgstr[1] "ediciones de Aventuras al Aire Libre"

#. ~ Description for Outdoor Adventures
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A glossy magazine about surviving and hunting in the wilderness.  There's an"
" exciting article about a bear attack in the back pages."
msgstr ""
"Una revista brillante acerca de la supervivencia al aire libre y la cacería."
" Tienen un artículo apasionante sobre los ataques de osos en las últimas "
"páginas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Pitching a Tent"
msgid_plural "copies of Pitching a Tent"
msgstr[0] "Montando una tienda de campaña"
msgstr[1] "copias de Montando una tienda de campaña"

#. ~ Description for Pitching a Tent
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A guide detailing the basics of woodsmanship and outdoor survival."
msgstr ""
"Una guía que detalla los fundamentos del trabajador forestal y la "
"supervivencia en la naturaleza."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Pocket Survival Guide"
msgid_plural "copies of Pocket Survival Guide"
msgstr[0] "Guía de Supervivencia de Bolsillo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Guía de Supervivencia de Bolsillo"

#. ~ Description for Pocket Survival Guide
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This pocket-sized leather-bound survival guide combines a wealth of concise "
"information with simple to follow instructions and easy to read "
"illustrations."
msgstr ""
"Está guía de bolsillo encuadernada en cuero sobre supervivencia, combina "
"mucha información concisa con instrucciones fáciles de seguir, e "
"ilustraciones comprensibles."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Autobiography of a Mountain Man"
msgid_plural "copies of Autobiography of a Mountain Man"
msgstr[0] "Autobiografía de un Hombre de la Montaña"
msgstr[1] "copias de la Autobiografía de un Hombre de la Montaña"

#. ~ Description for Autobiography of a Mountain Man
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An amusing historical novel filled with detailed descriptions of surviving "
"in the wild, potentially containing great insights for an experienced "
"outdoorsman."
msgstr ""
"Una divertida novela histórica llena de descripciones detalladas sobre la "
"supervivencia en la naturaleza, y probablemente contenga mucho conocimiento "
"para el amante de la naturaleza."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Outdoor Survival Guide"
msgid_plural "copies of Outdoor Survival Guide"
msgstr[0] "Guía de Supervivencia al Aire Libre"
msgstr[1] "copias de Guía de Supervivencia al Aire Libre"

#. ~ Description for Outdoor Survival Guide
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A thick soft-cover book filled with vital information about surviving in the"
" wild, aimed at the experienced backpacker."
msgstr ""
"Es un libro de tapa blanda resistente con información vital acerca de la "
"supervivencia en la naturaleza, dirigido al mochilero experimentado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Introduction to Plant Biology"
msgid_plural "copies of Introduction to Plant Biology"
msgstr[0] "Introducción a la Biología Vegetal"
msgstr[1] "copias de Introducción a la Biología Vegetal"

#. ~ Description for Introduction to Plant Biology
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A college-level textbook about plants of all shapes and sizes.  Covers a "
"wide range of subjects, from  horticulture to the identification of tropical"
" plants.  As such, it is of limited practical use in your current situation."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de texto de nivel universitario sobre plantas de todas las formas y"
" tamaños. Cubre una amplia gama de temas, desde la horticultura hasta la "
"identificación de plantas tropicales. Como tal, tiene un uso práctico "
"limitado en tu situación actual."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Wonderful World of Arthropodology"
msgid_plural "copies of The Wonderful World of Arthropodology"
msgstr[0] "El Maravilloso Mundo de la Artropodología"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Maravilloso Mundo de la Artropodología"

#. ~ Description for The Wonderful World of Arthropodology
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A three-volume doorstopper introducing the whole breadth of modern "
"arthropodology, beginning with a lengthy section on the comparative anatomy "
"of the described taxa.  The authors somehow manage to maintain a gushingly "
"enthusiastic tone, even as they describe the grisly effects of arthropod "
"venoms or the mating habits of horseshoe crabs.  Given the curious lack of "
"man-sized wasps in the illustrations, you have to wonder how much of the "
"contents is still applicable."
msgstr ""
"Un tope de tres volúmenes que introduce toda la amplitud de la "
"artrópodologia moderna, comenzando con una larga sección sobre la anatomía "
"comparativa de los taxones descritos. Los autores de alguna manera se las "
"arreglan para mantener un tono entusiasta, incluso mientras describen los "
"espeluznantes efectos de los venenos de los artrópodos o los hábitos de "
"apareamiento de los cangrejos herradura. Dada la curiosa falta de avispas de"
" tamaño humano en las ilustraciones, hay que preguntarse qué parte del "
"contenido sigue siendo aplicable."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Natural Remedies of New England"
msgid_plural "copies of Natural Remedies of New England"
msgstr[0] "Remedios Naturales de Nueva Inglaterra"
msgstr[1] "copias de Remedios Naturales de Nueva Inglaterra"

#. ~ Description for Natural Remedies of New England
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A leather bound manuscript, it features native herbal remedies with hand "
"colored illustrations of each plant."
msgstr ""
"Un manuscrito encuadernado en cuero, presenta remedios de hierbas nativas "
"con ilustraciones coloreadas a mano de cada planta."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Swim Planet"
msgid_plural "issues of Swim Planet"
msgstr[0] "Planeta Natación"
msgstr[1] "ediciones de Planeta Natación"

#. ~ Description for Swim Planet
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The world's leading resource about aquatic sports."
msgstr "El recurso líder en el mundo sobre deportes acuáticos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Water Survival Training Field Manual"
msgid_plural "copies of Water Survival Training Field Manual"
msgstr[0] "Manual de Supervivencia en el Agua"
msgstr[1] "copias de Manual de Supervivencia en el Agua"

#. ~ Description for Water Survival Training Field Manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A commercially produced survival guide that details swimming and deep water "
"survival techniques tailored to emergency scenarios."
msgstr ""
"Una guía de supervivencia comercialmente producida que detalla la natación y"
" las técnicas de supervivencia en aguas profundas, perfectas para "
"emergencias."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Boston AnimeCon magazine"
msgid_plural "Boston AnimeCon magazines"
msgstr[0] "revista de la Boston AnimeCon"
msgstr[1] "revistas de la Boston AnimeCon"

#. ~ Description for Boston AnimeCon magazine
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A short magazine printed as an advertisement for the now canceled Boston "
"AnimeCon.  A few costume ideas are intermixed with miscellaneous information"
" about the event."
msgstr ""
"Una breve revista impresa como un anuncio de la ahora cancelada Boston "
"AnimeCon.  Algunas ideas de disfraces son mezcladas con información "
"miscelánea sobre el evento."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Beauty Magazine"
msgid_plural "Beauty Magazines"
msgstr[0] "Revista Belleza"
msgstr[1] "Revista Belleza"

#. ~ Description for Beauty Magazine
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a full-size glossy women's magazine.  There are a few simple "
"patterns and basic sewing tips somewhere in between the fashion photos and "
"the makeup advertisements."
msgstr ""
"Una revista brillante para mujeres. Tiene algunos diseños simples y consejos"
" básicos sobre costura entre las fotos de moda y las publicidades de "
"maquillaje."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Sew Awesome Monthly"
msgid_plural "Sew Awesome Monthlies"
msgstr[0] "Costura Maravillosa Mensual"
msgstr[1] "Costura Maravillosa Mensual"

#. ~ Description for Sew Awesome Monthly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A well presented monthly magazine all about knitting, crocheting, and "
"needlepoint.  Filled with ideas and project patterns."
msgstr ""
"Una revista mensual bien presentada, con información sobre tejido, crochet  "
"y bordado. Lleno de ideas y moldes de proyectos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Sew What? Clothing!"
msgid_plural "copies of Sew What? Clothing!"
msgstr[0] "Coser ¿Qué? ¡Ropa!"
msgstr[1] "copias de Coser ¿Qué? ¡Ropa!"

#. ~ Description for Sew What? Clothing!
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A colorful book about tailoring."
msgstr "Es un libro colorido acerca de costura."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "clothing designer's portfolio"
msgid_plural "clothing designer's portfolios"
msgstr[0] "porfolio de diseñador de ropa"
msgstr[1] "porfolios de diseñador de ropa"

#. ~ Description for clothing designer's portfolio
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A leather bound portfolio that once belonged to a clothing designer.  Filled"
" with sketches and notes, a skilled tailor could learn a lot from this "
"volume."
msgstr ""
"Es un porfolio encuadernado en cuero que alguna vez perteneció a un "
"diseñador de ropa. Lleno de bocetos y notas, un sastre habilidoso podría "
"aprender mucho de este volumen."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Traditional Japanese Kimono"
msgid_plural "copies of Traditional Japanese Kimono"
msgstr[0] "Kimono Tradicional Japonés"
msgstr[1] "copias del Kimono Tradicional Japonés"

#. ~ Description for Traditional Japanese Kimono
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "An illustrated textbook on the crafting of Japanese traditional garb."
msgstr ""
"Es un libro de texto ilustrado acerca de la fabricación de indumentaria "
"clásica japonesa."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Friendly, Humane Fashion"
msgid_plural "copies of Friendly, Humane Fashion"
msgstr[0] "Moda Humana y Amistosa"
msgstr[1] "copias de Moda Humana y Amistosa"

#. ~ Description for Friendly, Humane Fashion
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An educational book detailing the uses of fake fur, as well as its benefits "
"and disadvantages.  The prose is rather passionate, and a disclaimer on the "
"cover proudly states that the book is printed and distributed by the Gryphon"
" Animal Rights Organization."
msgstr ""
"Un libro educativo que detalla el uso de piel falsa, así cómo sus beneficios"
" y desventajas. La prosa es un tanto apasionada, y una nota en la cubierta "
"declara orgullosamente que el libro ha sido impreso y distribuido por la "
"Asociación de Derechos Animales Grifo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Sewing Techniques for Designers"
msgid_plural "copies of Sewing Techniques for Designers"
msgstr[0] "Técnicas de Costura para Diseñadores"
msgstr[1] "copias de Técnicas de Costura para Diseñadores"

#. ~ Description for Sewing Techniques for Designers
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A massive, hardbound book full of a wealth of information for the "
"professional clothing designer."
msgstr ""
"Un masivo libro de tapa dura lleno de mucha información para el diseñador "
"profesional de indumentaria."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Ye Scots Beuk o Tailorin'"
msgid_plural "copies of Ye Scots Beuk o Tailorin'"
msgstr[0] "Ye Scots Beuk o Cuikery"
msgstr[1] "copias de Ye Scots Beuk o Cuikery"

#. ~ Description for Ye Scots Beuk o Tailorin'
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A translated Gaelic book from Scotland.  While boring to read due to its "
"technical tone, it provides insights into Scottish culture and information "
"about tailoring."
msgstr ""
"Un libro gaélico traducido de Escocia. Aunque es aburrido de leer debido a "
"su tono técnico, proporciona una visión de la cultura escocesa e información"
" sobre la sastrería."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Diskobolus"
msgid_plural "issues of Diskobolus"
msgstr[0] "Discóbolo"
msgstr[1] "ediciones del Discóbolo"

#. ~ Description for Diskobolus
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A biannual magazine devoted to the art and science of discus-throwing."
msgstr ""
"Una revista semestral dedicada al arte y la ciencia del lanzamiento de "
"discos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgid_plural "copies of The Complete Guide to Pitching"
msgstr[0] "La Guía Completa de Lanzamiento"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Guía Completa de Lanzamiento"

#. ~ Description for The Complete Guide to Pitching
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A detailed guide for baseball pitchers that combines time-tested techniques "
"and information mixed with a common sense approach to pitching."
msgstr ""
"Una guía detallada para los lanzadores de béisbol que combina técnicas "
"comprobadas e información mezclada con un acercamiento lógico al "
"lanzamiento."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "How to Trap Anything"
msgid_plural "copies of How to Trap Anything"
msgstr[0] "Cómo Atrapar Cualquier Cosa"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cómo Atrapar Cualquier Cosa"

#. ~ Description for How to Trap Anything
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A worn manual that describes how to set and disarm a wide variety of traps."
msgstr ""
"Un manual gastado que describo cómo poner y desarmar una gran variedad de "
"trampas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Trapper's Life"
msgid_plural "issues of Trapper's Life"
msgstr[0] "Vida del Trampero"
msgstr[1] "ediciones de la Vida del Trampero"

#. ~ Description for Trapper's Life
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An in-depth magazine about trapping game.  There are lots of articles and "
"diagrams that explain simple trap designs."
msgstr ""
"Una detallada revista sobre trampas para cazar animales. Tiene un montón de "
"artículos y diagramas que explican el diseño de trampas sencillas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Modern Trapper"
msgid_plural "copies of The Modern Trapper"
msgstr[0] "El Trampero Moderno"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Trampero Moderno"

#. ~ Description for The Modern Trapper
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "An extensive volume that details numerous methods of trapping game."
msgstr ""
"Un volumen extensivo que detalla numerosos métodos para atrapar animales "
"salvajes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations manual"
msgid_plural "copies of FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations manual"
msgstr[0] "Manual de Operaciones de Minas/Contramuros del FM 20-32"
msgstr[1] "copias del Manual de Operaciones de Minas/Contramuros del FM 20-32"

#. ~ Description for FM 20-32 Mine/Countermine Operations manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hefty military field manual about mine-warfare principles, the mechanics "
"of different types of mines/IED's, and countermine operations."
msgstr ""
"Un pesado manual de campo militar sobre los principios de la guerra contra "
"las minas, la mecánica de los diferentes tipos de minas y artefactos "
"explosivos improvisados, y las operaciones de contraminas."

#. ~ The spelling is intentionally archaic, as this form is commonly used in
#. the titles of books.
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Compleat Trapper"
msgid_plural "copies of The Compleat Trapper"
msgstr[0] "El Trampero Completo"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Trampero Completo"

#. ~ Description for The Compleat Trapper
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An in-depth book about trapping game animals, covering methods both modern "
"and ancient."
msgstr ""
"Un libro detallado sobre trampas para cazar animales, que abarca métodos "
"antiguos y modernos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Trapper's Companion"
msgid_plural "copies of The Trapper's Companion"
msgstr[0] "Los Compañeros del Trampero"
msgstr[1] "copias de Los Compañeros del Trampero"

#. ~ Description for The Trapper's Companion
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A folksy guide to trapping wild game using time-tested methods.  A bit in-"
"depth for the beginner, it can provide a wealth of information to a "
"knowledgeable trapper."
msgstr ""
"Una guía rústica para atrapar animales salvajes usando métodos de eficacia "
"comprobada. Un poco complejo para un principiante, pero puede brindar "
"abundante información para un trampero conocedor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Boxing Monthly"
msgid_plural "Boxing Monthlies"
msgstr[0] "Boxeo Mensual"
msgstr[1] "Boxeo Mensual"

#. ~ Description for Boxing Monthly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An exciting monthly magazine about boxing.  There are lots of large, "
"colorful photos of pugilistic exploits."
msgstr ""
"Una entretenida revista mensual sobre boxeo. Tiene muchas fotos grandes y "
"coloridas de proezas pugilísticas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "101 Wrestling Moves"
msgid_plural "copies of 101 Wrestling Moves"
msgstr[0] "Movimientos de Lucha Libre 101 "
msgstr[1] "copias de Movimientos de Lucha Libre 101 "

#. ~ Description for 101 Wrestling Moves
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"It seems to be a wrestling manual, poorly photocopied and released on "
"spiral-bound paper.  Still, there are lots of useful tips for unarmed "
"combat."
msgstr ""
"Parece ser un manual de lucha libre, mal fotocopiado y publicado en papel "
"con espiral. Aún así, hay muchos consejos útiles para el combate sin armas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "children's book"
msgid_plural "children's books"
msgstr[0] "libro infantil"
msgstr[1] "libros infantiles"

#. ~ Description for children's book
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A little book for little readers.  The colorful cartoon characters and sweet"
" stories contained herein belong to a different time, before the dead walked"
" and the world moved on."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño libro para pequeños lectores. Los personajes coloridos y las "
"dulces historias que contiene dentro pertenecen a otro tiempo diferente, "
"antes de que los muertos caminen y el mundo continuó girando."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "book of fairy tales"
msgid_plural "books of fairy tales"
msgstr[0] "libro de cuentos de hadas"
msgstr[1] "libros de cuentos de hadas"

#. ~ Description for book of fairy tales
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An amusing collection of folklore featuring the usual cast of fairies, "
"goblins, and trolls."
msgstr ""
"Una divertida colección de cuentos tradicionales, con la participación de "
"los protagonistas habituales como hadas, goblins y trolls."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This fairy tale is about a wolf who eats so much salted meat she becomes "
"trapped in the butcher's cellar."
msgstr ""
"Este cuento es sobre un lobo que come mucha carne salada y termina atrapado "
"en el sótano de un carnicero."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this traditional story of beastly intrigue a clever fox convinces an "
"elderly lion to kill a derogatory wolf."
msgstr ""
"En esta tradicional historia de intriga bestial, un astuto zorro convence a "
"un anciano león de matar a un lobo despectivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an illustrated fairy tale book about a conversation between a mouse "
"and a cat."
msgstr ""
"Este es un libro de cuento de hadas ilustrado sobre una conversación entre "
"un ratón y un gato."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This illustrated fairy tale relates how a city mouse did visit his cousin in"
" the country, and how each regarded the other's quality of life."
msgstr ""
"Este cuento ilustrado relata cómo un ratón de ciudad visitó a su primo en el"
" campo, y cómo cada uno consideraba la calidad de vida del otro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A fable in which the jackal wins the day via clever foolishness."
msgstr ""
"Una fábula en la que el chacal gana el día a través de una ingeniosa "
"tontería."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A slave mistakenly wanders into a lion's den - thus begins a fable which "
"demonstrates mutual dependence regardless of size or status."
msgstr ""
"Un esclavo se mete por error en la guarida de un león - así comienza una "
"fábula que demuestra la dependencia mutua sin importar el tamaño o el "
"estatus."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An amusing collection of stories featuring \"Goldilocks and The Three "
"Bears\" on the cover."
msgstr ""
"Una divertida colección de historias con \"Ricitos de oro y los tres osos\" "
"en la portada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a well illustrated fairy tale about a war between the birds and the "
"beasts, with particulars on the wartime conduct and eventual fate of the "
"bat."
msgstr ""
"Este es un cuento de hadas bien ilustrado sobre una guerra entre los pájaros"
" y las bestias, con detalles sobre la conducta en tiempo de guerra y el "
"eventual destino del murciélago."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book, titled \"The Rattlesnake's Vengeance\" is a collection of "
"Cherokee myths and legends.  \"285D\" is hand-written in pencil on the title"
" page."
msgstr ""
"Este libro, titulado \"La venganza de la serpiente de cascabel\" es una "
"colección de mitos y leyendas cherokees. \"285D\" está escrito a mano con "
"lápiz en la portada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This fairy tale book is a regional variant of \"Jack and the Beanstalk.\""
msgstr ""
"Este libro de cuentos de hadas es una variante regional de \"Jack y las "
"habichuelas mágicas\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This fairy tale book is entitled \"Little Red Cap\".  It details a red-"
"cloaked child's various encounters with talking wolves."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de cuentos de hadas se titula \"Pequeña gorra roja\". Detalla los"
" diversos encuentros de un niño con capa roja con lobos parlantes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of ghost stories warning about the dangers of stealing from the"
" dead."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de cuentos de hadas se titula \"Pequeña gorra roja\". Detalla una"
" gorra roja..."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An Irish fairy tale in which a Celtic poet marries a princess who has been "
"cursed with the head of a pig."
msgstr ""
"Un cuento de hadas irlandés en el que un poeta celta se casa con una "
"princesa que ha sido maldecida con la cabeza de un cerdo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book of Italian fairy tales translated into English.  The cover features "
"an orange fairy juggling a lemon, a lime, and a tangerine."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de cuentos de hadas italianos traducido al inglés. En la portada "
"aparece un hada naranja haciendo malabares con un limón, una lima y una "
"mandarina."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A book of fables about people who change into birds."
msgstr "Un libro de fábulas sobre gente que se convierte en pájaros."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This compendium of amusing folk tales about the devil is titled \"Hell's "
"Kettle: Legends of the Devil.\""
msgstr ""
"Este compendio de divertidos cuentos populares sobre el diablo se titula "
"\"La tetera del infierno: Leyendas del Diablo\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This charming book of Swedish fables is titled, \"The Glass Mountain and the"
" Princess.\""
msgstr ""
"Este encantador libro de fábulas suecas se titula \"La montaña de cristal y "
"la princesa\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a collection of fairy tale stories warning against the consequences "
"of extreme greed."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de cuentos de hadas que advierten sobre las "
"consecuencias de la avaricia extrema."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This fable book is entitled, \"The Rabbit Herd.\"  Inside are woodcut "
"illustrations of a peasant boy playing his flute for a mob of mischievous "
"hares."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de fábula se titula \"La manada de conejos\". Dentro hay "
"ilustraciones en madera de un niño campesino tocando su flauta para una "
"turba de liebres traviesas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book is titled, \"The Thieving Pot: Folktales of the Arab World.\""
msgstr ""
"Este libro se titula \"La Olla de los Ladrones: Cuentos del Mundo Árabe\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a book of legends collected by Traveller Johnny Cassidy in the "
"1960s."
msgstr ""
"Este es un libro de leyendas recogidas por el viajero Johnny Cassidy en los "
"años 60."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A book by the Brothers Grimm titled, \"Eve's Unequal Children.\""
msgstr "Un libro de los hermanos Grimm titulado \"Los niños desiguales de Eva\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book of fables expands upon the legend of the Seven Sleepers of "
"Ephesus."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de fábulas amplía la leyenda de los Siete Durmientes de Éfeso."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this fairy tale a strong man frightens an ogre by squeezing water out of "
"a stone."
msgstr ""
"En este cuento de hadas un hombre fuerte asusta a un ogro exprimiendo agua "
"de una piedra."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book of rustic folk tales bears the title: \"How to Shout Down the "
"Devil.\""
msgstr ""
"Este libro de cuentos populares rústicos lleva el título: \"Cómo gritar al "
"diablo\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The title of this book is \"Village Folk-tales of Ceylon.\"  It includes "
"fables about logical errors and foolish misjudgements of the Kadambawa men."
msgstr ""
"El título de este libro es \"Cuentos populares de Ceilán\". Incluye fábulas "
"sobre errores lógicos y juicios tontos de los hombres Kadambawa."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book of folk tales is titled, \"The Girl with the Ugly Name, and Other "
"Stories.\""
msgstr ""
"Este libro de cuentos folclóricos se titula \"La chica del nombre feo y "
"otras historias\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Titled \"The Fleeing Pancake\", this collection of silly folk tales is "
"suitable for small children."
msgstr ""
"Titulada \"La tortita que huye\", esta colección de cuentos populares tontos"
" es adecuada para los niños pequeños."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Adorkable Girl"
msgid_plural "copies of Adorkable"
msgstr[0] "La Chica Adorkable"
msgstr[1] "copias de Adorkable"

#. ~ Description for The Adorkable Girl
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When a therapist's daughter transfers to a new school, she decides to change"
" her personality type.  As her social life begins to blossom, can she "
"maintain a healthy boundary between her home life and her public persona?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando la hija de un terapeuta se transfiere a una nueva escuela, decide "
"cambiar su tipo de personalidad. Cuando su vida social comienza a florecer, "
"¿puede mantener un límite saludable entre su vida de hogar y su persona "
"pública?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Becoming Jackson"
msgid_plural "copies of Becoming Jackson"
msgstr[0] "Convirtiéndose en Jackson"
msgstr[1] "copias de Convirtiéndose en Jackson"

#. ~ Description for Becoming Jackson
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When Jackson gains the mystical talent to alter his appearance on command, "
"will he be able to recognize himself in his own mirror?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando Jackson adquiera el talento místico de alterar su apariencia al "
"mando, ¿será capaz de reconocerse en su propio espejo?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Nothing Burned"
msgid_plural "copies of Nothing Burned"
msgstr[0] "Nada se quemó"
msgstr[1] "copias de Nada se quemó"

#. ~ Description for Nothing Burned
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A teenage influencer becomes fast friends with someone who may or may not be"
" an actual demon."
msgstr ""
"Un influencer adolescente se hace amigo íntimo con alguien que puede o no "
"puede ser realmente un demonio."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "High and Low"
msgid_plural "copies of High and Low"
msgstr[0] "Alto y Bajo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Alto y Bajo"

#. ~ Description for High and Low
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this work of adolescent fiction, a young gemini discovers that the "
"astrology section of his small town newspaper is eerily preminiscent.  His "
"efforts to uncover the oracle reveal more than the stars could have "
"predicted."
msgstr ""
"En esta obra de ficción adolescente, un joven géminis descubre que la "
"sección de astrología del periódico de su pequeña ciudad es inquietantemente"
" prematura. Sus esfuerzos por descubrir el oráculo revelan más de lo que las"
" estrellas podrían haber predicho."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Fire When You See My Eyes"
msgid_plural "copies of Fire When"
msgstr[0] "Dispara Cuando Veas Mis Ojos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Dispara Cuando"

#. ~ Description for Fire When You See My Eyes
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In a cataclysmic future, advanced technology gives parents access to video "
"footage of every moment of their teenage children's lives."
msgstr ""
"En un futuro cataclísmico, la tecnología avanzada da a los padres acceso a "
"imágenes de vídeo de cada momento de la vida de sus hijos adolescentes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Peanut Butter Bruised"
msgid_plural "copies of Peanut Butter Bruised"
msgstr[0] "Mantequilla de Cacahuete Estropeada"
msgstr[1] "copias de Mantequilla de Cacahuete Estropeada"

#. ~ Description for Peanut Butter Bruised
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this work of young adult fiction, a woman raised on food stamps falls in "
"love with a young cook.  More importantly, she falls in love with the idea "
"of becoming a professional chef."
msgstr ""
"En esta obra de ficción para jóvenes adultos, una mujer criada con cupones "
"de comida se enamora de una joven cocinera. Más importante aún, se enamora "
"de la idea de convertirse en chef profesional."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Ready When You Are"
msgid_plural "copies of Ready When"
msgstr[0] "Preparado Cuando Tu Lo Estes"
msgstr[1] "copias de Preparado Cuando"

#. ~ Description for Ready When You Are
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When three teenage girls ditch class to drive cross country together they "
"get a strong dose of life lessons on the road.  This work of young adult "
"fiction explores how friendships evolve in early adulthood."
msgstr ""
"Cuando tres adolescentes abandonan la clase para conducir juntos a través "
"del país, reciben una fuerte dosis de lecciones de vida en la carretera. "
"Esta obra de ficción para jóvenes adultos explora cómo se desarrollan las "
"amistades en la edad adulta temprana."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Study of a Boy"
msgid_plural "copies of \"Study of a Boy\""
msgstr[0] "Estudio De Un Niño"
msgstr[1] "copias de Estudio De Un Niño"

#. ~ Description for Study of a Boy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A high school sophomore's personal journal is stolen and then leaked on "
"social media.  When it goes viral he is forced simultaneously to contend "
"with both fame and betrayal."
msgstr ""
"El diario personal de un estudiante de segundo año es robado y luego "
"filtrado en los medios sociales. Cuando se hace viral, se ve obligado a "
"luchar simultáneamente con la fama y la traición."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Summer Variables"
msgid_plural "copies of Summer Variables"
msgstr[0] "Variables de Verano"
msgstr[1] "copias de Variables de Verano"

#. ~ Description for Summer Variables
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In this book written primarily for young adults, a woman's modest summer "
"internship results in an incredible discovery that attracts the attention of"
" unsavory elements."
msgstr ""
"En este libro escrito principalmente para adultos jóvenes, la modesta "
"pasantía de verano de una mujer resulta en un increíble descubrimiento que "
"atrae la atención de elementos desagradables."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "In a Dark Place"
msgid_plural "copies of Dark Place"
msgstr[0] "En Un Lugar Oscuro"
msgstr[1] "copias de Lugar Oscuro"

#. ~ Description for In a Dark Place
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Markia dreams about the future.  Theo longs for the past.  Together can they"
" find a way to live in the now?"
msgstr ""
"Markia sueña con el futuro. Theo anhela el pasado. ¿Juntos pueden encontrar "
"una forma de vivir en el ahora?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Betrayal Takes Two"
msgid_plural "copies of Betrayal"
msgstr[0] "La Traición Toma a Dos"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Traición"

#. ~ Description for Betrayal Takes Two
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hard cover book for older teens.  The two main characters pull a "
"cruel prank on their classmates, and are brought together both by their "
"frantic efforts to avoid being caught and their shared sense of guilt."
msgstr ""
"Este es un libro de tapa dura para adolescentes mayores. Los dos personajes "
"principales le gastan una broma cruel a sus compañeros de clase, y se unen "
"por sus frenéticos esfuerzos para evitar ser atrapados y su sentimiento de "
"culpa compartido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "coming of age novel"
msgid_plural "coming of age novels"
msgstr[0] "novela de iniciación"
msgstr[1] "novelas de iniciación"

#. ~ Description for coming of age novel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A classic tale about growing up, portraying one young man's funny and "
"poignant experiences with life, love, and sex."
msgstr ""
"Una clásica historia sobre madurar, narra las emotivas y divertidas "
"experiencias de un joven sobre la vida, el amor y el sexo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Pantheon: The Story of an Iranian Youth"
msgid_plural "copies of Pantheon"
msgstr[0] "Panteón: La Historia de Una Joven Iraní"
msgstr[1] "copias de Panteón"

#. ~ Description for Pantheon: The Story of an Iranian Youth
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hard cover graphic novel about a young girl living in Iran during the "
"1980's, seeing the world change around her as Iraq invaded her country."
msgstr ""
"Una novela gráfica de tapa dura sobre una joven que vivía en Irán durante "
"los años 80, viendo cómo el mundo cambiaba a su alrededor cuando Irak "
"invadía su país."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "original copy of Housefly"
msgid_plural "original copies of Housefly"
msgstr[0] "copia original de Mosca"
msgstr[1] "copias originales de Mosca"

#. ~ Description for original copy of Housefly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The only copy of Housefly in existence - a long book about three individuals"
" drawn together by fate in the early 1800s to save their English town of "
"Victoria from a mysterious threat.  You never got to publish it, but reading"
" it lets you forget the horrors of the Cataclysm, if only for a moment."
msgstr ""
"La única copia de Mosca que existe: un largo libro acerca de tres individuos"
" unidos por el destino a principios del siglo XIX para salvar Victoria, su "
"pueblo inglés, de una amenaza misteriosa. Nunca llegaste a publicarlo, pero "
"leerlo te hace olvidar los horrores del Cataclismo, aunque sea solo por un "
"momento."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia no autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 1"

#. ~ Description for Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Welcome to Frozen Hell, an unofficial history of Salus IV by Bette Lapin.  "
"Salus IV was founded in the early days of the Hyperspace Era by the "
"interstellar Soviet community.  At its height several hundred years ago "
"Salus IV had just over one billion sentient citizens, but that population "
"had begun to decline even before the Discontinuity as people migrated to "
"planets that while more hostile to life during the earliest colonization "
"phases than Salus IV were much simpler to terraform into a place more "
"enjoyable by human and uplift citizens."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenido al Infierno Congelado, la historia no autorizada de Salus IV "
"escrita por Bette Lapin. Salus IV fue fundada en los primeros días de la Era"
" Hiperespacial por la comunidad Interestelar Soviética. En su apogeo, hace "
"varios cientos de años, Salus IV tenía poco más de mil millones de "
"ciudadanos conscientes, pero la población habia empezado a declinar incluso "
"antes de la Discontinuidad cuando las personas migraron a planetas que "
"aunque eran más hostiles a la vida durante las primeras fases de la "
"colonización que Salus IV, eran mucho más simples de terraformar  en un "
"lugar más agradable para los humanos y ciudadanos ascendidos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 2"

#. ~ Description for Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Even during the Discontinuity Salus IV's population continued to drop as "
"there were easier places to live even in the Salus system, from honeycombed "
"asteroid habitats, to domed cities with gorgeous views.  As with many other "
"governments during the Discontinuity the Interstellar Soviet collapsed into "
"a vipers pit of microstates, solar corporations and other forms of self "
"governance.  During this time Mercurial Genomics a corporation specializing "
"in Uplifts successfully laid claim to Salus IV in the court system set up by"
" ESCA.  The Whately family, which runs Mercurial Genomics begins leasing "
"development and exploitation permits and allows the establishment of minor "
"UICA outposts within Salus IV.  There is an official citizen count of less "
"than fifty thousand sentient beings mostly in orbit of Salus IV.  It is "
"believed however that there are at least that many non-citizen sentients "
"spread amongst squatter, smuggler, pirate, and feral uplift communities."
msgstr ""
"Incluso durante la Discontinuidad, la población de Salus IV continuó "
"disminuyendo ya que había lugares más fáciles donde vivir en el sistema "
"Salus, desde asteroides colmena hasta ciudades con cupulas y paisajes "
"hermosos. Como muchos otros gobiernos durante al Discontinuidad, la "
"Interestelar Soviética colapsó en un nido de víboras de microestados, "
"corporaciones solares y otras formas de autogobiernos. Durante este tiempo, "
"Génomica Mercurial, una corporación especializada en Ascendidos, reclamó "
"Salus IV en el sistema judicial establecido por ESCA. La familia Whately, la"
" cual controla Genómica Mercurial, comienza a alquilar permisos para "
"desarrollo y explotación y permite que se establezcan puestos de avanzadas "
"menores de UICA dentro de Salus IV. Hay un censo oficial de menos de "
"cincuenta mil seres conscientes, encontrándose la mayoría en la órbita de "
"Salus IV. Sin embargo, se sospecha que hay por al menos esa misma cantidad "
"de no ciudadanos conscientes entre ocupantes ilegales, contrabandistas, "
"piratas y comunidades salvajes de ascendidos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 3"

#. ~ Description for Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Salus system is what is called a hinge system for the new FTL travels.  "
"This system contains a number of easy exit points to star systems that have "
"no other easy way to travel to each other than through a series of systems "
"with low to zero civilization in them.  Salus at minimum has several "
"interstellar refueling points.  These stations are often blind to each other"
" as the planets and other objects rotate around the sun.  Mercurial seems to"
" have no interest in managing or protecting the traffic that flows through "
"the Salus system or in neighboring systems beyond the bare minimum effort "
"required by UICA.  As a result of this neglect; victims of pirate attacks, "
"engine failure and other critical issues regularly limp to whatever safety "
"they can find in the Salus system.  Unfortunately for many of them they will"
" crash land on Salus IV where there are few regular shuttles between its "
"scattered ports and the outside universe.  As the locals are fond of saying "
"'Getting to Salus IV is hard, getting off may be impossible'."
msgstr ""
"El sistema Salus es lo que se llama un sistema bisagra para los nuevos "
"viajes FTL(Faster than light). Este sistema contiene varias puntos de salida"
" fáciles para sistemas de estrellas que no poseen otra manera fácil de "
"viajar entre ellos que no sea a través de una serie de sistemas con poca o "
"ninguna civilización. Salus tiene como mínimo varios puntos de "
"reabastecimiento interestelar. Estas estaciones a menudo no son visibles  "
"entre ellas ya que planetas y otros objetos rotan alrededor del sol. "
"Mercurial parece no tener interés en gestionar o proteger el tráfico que "
"fluye a través del sistema Salus o en sistemas vecinos, más allá del mínimo "
"requerido por la UICA. Como resultado de esta negligencia, las víctimas de "
"ataques piratas, fallas de motores o otros asuntos críticos restan a la "
"seguridad que se puede encontrar en el sistema Salus. Lamentablemente muchos"
" de ellos, se estrellarán en Salus IV donde hay pocos transbordadores entre "
"sus puertos dispersos y el universo exterior. Como dice el dicho: 'Llegar a "
"Salus IV es difícil, salir imposible.'"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Nuclear Physics Made Easy"
msgid_plural "copies of Nuclear Physics Made Easy"
msgstr[0] "Física Nuclear Hecha Fácil"
msgstr[1] "copias de Física Nuclear Hecha Fácil"

#. ~ Description for Nuclear Physics Made Easy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book detailing the workings of state of the art atomic technology, and the"
" physics behind it."
msgstr ""
"Un libro que detalla el funcionamiento del arte de la tecnología atómica, y "
"la física detrás de ella."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "mealworm farm logbook"
msgid_plural "mealworm farm logbooks"
msgstr[0] "Registro de La Granja del Gusano de la Harina"
msgstr[1] "Libros de Registro de La Granja del Gusano de la Harina"

#. ~ Description for mealworm farm logbook
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A binder containing detailed production logs from an industrial mealworm "
"farm.  You could use its recordings to start your own farming operations."
msgstr ""
"Un archivador que contiene registros detallados de producción de una granja "
"industrial de gusanos de harina. Podrías usar sus grabaciones para iniciar "
"tus propias operaciones agrícolas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "diamond press schematics"
msgid_plural "diamond press schematics"
msgstr[0] "esquema de la prensa de diamantes"
msgstr[1] "esquemas de la prensa de diamantes"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'diamond press schematics'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Bearing the logo of Matrioshka Fabritechnics, those are assembly plans, "
"design specs, and technical drawings for the diamond press.  Most of this is"
" useless to you, but you could use the assembly plans to re-assemble the "
"robot from salvaged parts."
msgstr ""
"Con el logo de Matrioshka Fabritechnics, son planos de montaje, "
"especificaciones de diseño y dibujos técnicos para la prensa de diamantes. "
"La mayoría de esto es inútil para ti, pero podrías usar los planos de "
"ensamblaje para reensamblar el robot a partir de las piezas recuperadas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "nano forge schematics"
msgid_plural "nano forge schematics"
msgstr[0] "esquema de nanoforja"
msgstr[1] "esquemas de nanoforja"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'nano forge schematics'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Bearing the logo of Matrioshka Fabritechnics, those are assembly plans, "
"design specs, and technical drawings for the nano forge.  Most of this is "
"useless to you, but you could use the assembly plans to re-assemble the "
"robot from salvaged parts."
msgstr ""
"Con el logo de Matrioshka Fabritechnics, son planos de montaje, "
"especificaciones de diseño y dibujos técnicos para la nanoforja. La mayoría "
"de esto es inútil para ti, pero podrías usar los planos de ensamblaje para "
"reensamblar el robot a partir de las piezas recuperadas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "landfall survival manual"
msgid_plural "landfall survival manuals"
msgstr[0] "manual de supervivencia de aterrizaje en tierra"
msgstr[1] "manuales de supervivencia de aterrizaje en tierra"

#. ~ Description for landfall survival manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small folio indicating how to best utilize the equipment of your landfall "
"survival kit during an emergency.  Its first page urges you to remain calm, "
"and to consult your escape pod's control console for further instructions."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño folio que indica cómo utilizar mejor el equipo de tu kit de "
"supervivencia de aterrizaje durante una emergencia. Su primera página le "
"insta a mantener la calma y a consultar la consola de control de su cápsula "
"de escape para obtener más instrucciones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Cyrus Whateley's Notes on Repurposing mi-go victims"
msgid_plural "copies of Cyrus Whateley's Notes"
msgstr[0] ""
"Notas de Cyrus Whateley Sobre La Reconversión de las víctimas de mi-go"
msgstr[1] "copias de Notas de Cyrus Whateley"

#. ~ Description for Cyrus Whateley's Notes on Repurposing mi-go victims
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A folio of notes written by a madman.  They seem to suggest ways to re-"
"animate the dead and create various affronts to the natural order."
msgstr ""
"Un folio de notas escritas por un loco. Parecen sugerir formas de reanimar a"
" los muertos y crear diversas afrentas al orden natural."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Dr Moreau and You"
msgid_plural "copies of Dr Moreau and You"
msgstr[0] "Dr Moreau y Tu"
msgstr[1] "copias de Dr Moreau y Tu"

#. ~ Description for Dr Moreau and You
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"In what many considered a stunning example of poor taste and others "
"considered overt speciesism this text on the creation of Uplifted Animals "
"references a story about sapient animals killing their creator.  Otherwise a"
" dry text about genetic modification."
msgstr ""
"En lo que muchos consideraron un ejemplo impresionante de mal gusto y otros "
"consideraron un especismo manifiesto, este texto sobre la creación de "
"Animales Ascendidos hace referencia a una historia sobre animales sapientes "
"que matan a su creador. Por lo demás, un texto seco sobre la modificación "
"genética."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Millyficent's Diary"
msgid_plural "copies of Millyficent's Diary"
msgstr[0] "El Diario de Millyficent"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Diario de Millyficent"

#. ~ Description for Millyficent's Diary
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pocket-sized book filled to the margins with cramped handwriting and notes"
" on the biology of Mi-Go and other musings.  It's hard to understand and "
"quite gruesome in some places and written in a shorthand or cipher in "
"others."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de bolsillo lleno hasta los márgenes con una escritura apretada y "
"notas sobre la biología de Mi-Go y otras reflexiones. Es difícil de entender"
" y bastante espantoso en algunos lugares y escrito en taquigrafía o cifrado "
"en otros."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "useful recipes for resistance"
msgid_plural "copies of useful recipes for resistance"
msgstr[0] "Recetas Útiles Para Resistencia"
msgstr[1] "copias de Recetas Útiles Para Resistencia"

#. ~ Description for useful recipes for resistance
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Recipes for Resistance is a collection of tales, strategies and recipes for "
"working against corporate rule.  Very simple language is used in the recipes"
" but it drags out the explanations."
msgstr ""
"Recetas Para la Resistencia es una colección de cuentos, estrategias y "
"recetas para trabajar en contra de las reglas corporativas. Se utiliza un "
"lenguaje muy simple en las recetas, pero alarga las explicaciones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Working in Boreal Conditions and beyond"
msgid_plural "copies of Working in Boreal Conditions and beyond"
msgstr[0] "Trabajando en Condiciones Boreales y Más Allá"
msgstr[1] "copias de Trabajando en Condiciones Boreales y Más Allá"

#. ~ Description for Working in Boreal Conditions and beyond
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A corporate manual for conditions of inhospitable cold.  It includes "
"instructions for building devices and substances that will aid in survival "
"in extreme weather or even the lack thereof."
msgstr ""
"Un manual corporativo para condiciones de frío inhóspito. Incluye "
"instrucciones para la construcción de dispositivos y sustancias que ayudan a"
" la supervivencia en condiciones climáticas extremas o incluso la falta de "
"ellas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Unusual Ammunitions of the Corporations"
msgid_plural "copies of Unusual Ammunitions of the Corporations"
msgstr[0] "Municiones Inusuales de las Corporaciones"
msgstr[1] "copias de Municiones Inusuales de las Corporaciones"

#. ~ Description for Unusual Ammunitions of the Corporations
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lab book dedicated to reverse engineering various ammunitions found "
"throughout the solar system.  Written in a format to allow barely trained "
"technicians to *safely* replicate these rounds."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de laboratorio dedicado a la ingeniería inversa de varias "
"municiones encontradas en todo el sistema solar. Escrito en un formato que "
"permite a los técnicos apenas entrenados a *seguramente* replicar estas "
"municiones."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Applications of Salus IV Lichen"
msgid_plural "copies of Applications of Salus IV Lichen"
msgstr[0] "Aplicaciones del Liquen de Salus IV"
msgstr[1] "copias de Aplicaciones del Liquen de Salus IV"

#. ~ Description for Applications of Salus IV Lichen
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sheaf of notes detailing some species of lichen.  Most of the information "
"is useless to you except for the fact that the majority of Salus IV "
"lifeform's metabolism rely on a macronutrient that acts like a neurotoxin "
"for humans.  One useful note is a detailed procedure to neutralize said "
"neurotoxin."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de notas que detallan algunas especies de líquenes. La mayor parte"
" de la información es inútil para usted excepto por el hecho de que la "
"mayoría del metabolismo de la forma de vida de Salus IV depende de un "
"macronutriente que actúa como una neurotoxina para los humanos. Una nota "
"útil es un procedimiento detallado para neutralizar dicha neurotoxina."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "USMC M1014 technical manual"
msgid_plural "USMC M1014 technical manuals"
msgstr[0] "Manual Técnico USMC M1014 "
msgstr[1] "Manuales Técnicos USMC M1014 "

#. ~ Description for USMC M1014 technical manual
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pocket-sized book printed in 2000 by the United States Marine Corps for "
"official use.  It describes the operation, repair, and cleaning of the "
"Benilli M1014 shotgun.  Though specific to the M4, it can provide a wealth "
"of information to the trained eye."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de bolsillo impreso en 2000 por el Cuerpo de Marines de los Estados"
" Unidos para uso oficial. Describe la operación, reparación y limpieza de la"
" escopeta Benilli M1014. Aunque es específica para la M4, puede proporcionar"
" una gran cantidad de información al ojo entrenado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Black Powder to Berettas"
msgid_plural "copies of Black Powder to Berettas"
msgstr[0] "Pólvora Negra para Berettas"
msgstr[1] "copias de Pólvora Negra para Berettas"

#. ~ Description for Black Powder to Berettas
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hardcover book, aimed at the gun nut, provides an illustrated, concise "
"history of the handgun throughout history, including technical "
"specifications and use techniques.  It's difficult to follow without a "
"passing knowledge in pistols, but an experienced handgun user could glean "
"much from it."
msgstr ""
"Este libro de tapa dura, dirigido al entendido de las armas, proporciona una"
" historia ilustrada y concisa de las armas de fuego a lo largo de la "
"historia, incluyendo especificaciones técnicas y técnicas de uso. Es difícil"
" de seguir sin un conocimiento previo de las pistolas, pero un usuario "
"experimentado de arma de fuego podría sacar mucho de él."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "America's Rifle"
msgid_plural "copies of America's Rifle"
msgstr[0] "copia de El Rifle de Estados Unidos"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Rifle de Estados Unidos"

#. ~ Description for America's Rifle
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A history book penned by an anonymous author.  Starting from its design by "
"John Garand and ending with the Vietnam War, it provides a detailed run-down"
" of the M1 Garand rifle's use throughout history as well as its design and "
"quirks with the weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un libro de historia escrito por un autor anónimo. Comenzando con su diseño "
"por John Garand y terminando con la Guerra de Vietnam, proporciona un "
"detallado resumen del uso del rifle M1 Garand a lo largo de la historia, así"
" como su diseño y las peculiaridades del arma."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Jane's Flamethrowers and Firestarters"
msgid_plural "copies of Jane's Flamethrowers and Firestarters"
msgstr[0] "El Lanzallamas De Jane Y Los Encendedores De Fuego."
msgstr[1] "copias de El Lanzallamas De Jane Y Los Encendedores De Fuego."

#. ~ Description for Jane's Flamethrowers and Firestarters
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A detailed, full-colored guide to flamethrowers, incendiary weapons, and "
"napalm.  It builds off of information provided in its sister book, Jane's "
"Mortars and Rocket Launchers, and so it's mostly incomprehensible to anyone "
"without prior knowledge."
msgstr ""
"Una detallada guía a todo color de lanzallamas, armas incendiarias y napalm."
" Se basa en la información proporcionada en su libro hermano, Los Morteros "
"de Jane y los Lanzacohetes, y por lo tanto es mayormente incomprensible para"
" cualquiera sin conocimiento previo."

#. ~ Description for children's book
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A little book for little readers.  The colorful cartoon characters and sweet"
" stories contained herein belong to a different time, before the sky grew "
"dark and the aliens arrived."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño libro para pequeños lectores. Los coloridos personajes de dibujos"
" animados y las dulces historias que contiene pertenecen a otra época, antes"
" de que el cielo se oscureciera y llegaran los extraterrestres."

#. ~ Description for TIME magazine
#. ~ Description for US Weekly
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Current events concerning a bunch of people who're all dead now - or working"
" for them."
msgstr ""
"Eventos actuales acerca de un montón de gente que ahora esta muertos o "
"trabajando en ello."

#. ~ Description for Zombie Survival Guide
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"While this seems like it would be at least partially useful in this "
"situation, the sheer amount of speculative fiction present makes it "
"practically useless.  What the hell is a mi-go?  Aren't triffids from some "
"ancient movie?"
msgstr ""
"Aunque parece que sería al menos parcialmente útil en esta situación, la "
"gran cantidad de ficción especulativa presente la hace prácticamente inútil."
" ¿Qué demonios es un mi-go? ¿No son los trífidos de alguna película antigua?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Kiernan's notes"
msgid_plural "copies of Kiernan's notes"
msgstr[0] "notas de Kiernan"
msgstr[1] "copias de notas de Kiernan"

#. ~ Description for Kiernan's notes
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The voluminous notes of an obviously talented paleontologist, dedicated "
"biologist, and amateur author.  These notes jump from such topics as fossil "
"digs, science fiction stories, also strangely enough notes on dinosaur "
"biology and potential hybridization efforts."
msgstr ""
"Las voluminosas notas de un paleontólogo de evidente talento, dedicado "
"biólogo y autor amateur. Estas notas saltan de temas tales como excavaciones"
" de fósiles, historias de ciencia ficción, también curiosamente notas sobre "
"la biología de los dinosaurios y los posibles esfuerzos de hibridación."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scorching Sirocco"
msgid_plural "Scorching Sirocco"
msgstr[0] "Siroco Abrasador"
msgstr[1] "Siroco Abrasador"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Scorching Sirocco'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Desert Wind discipline."
msgstr ""
"Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina Viento del Desierto."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Perfect Clarity of Mind and Body"
msgid_plural "Perfect Clarity of Mind and Body"
msgstr[0] "Claridad Perfecta de la Mente y Cuerpo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Claridad Perfecta de la Mente y Cuerpo"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Perfect Clarity of Mind and Body'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Diamond Mind discipline."
msgstr ""
"Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina de la Mente de Diamante."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Book of Mudora"
msgid_plural "The Book of Mudora"
msgstr[0] "El Libro de Mudora"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Libro de Mudora"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'The Book of Mudora'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of ancient Hylian lore and stories.  A section on historic "
"battles is bookmarked."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de antiguas tradiciones e historias de Hylian. Una sección de "
"batallas históricas está marcada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Stormguard Warrior"
msgid_plural "Stormguard Warrior"
msgstr[0] "Guerrero GuardiaTormenta"
msgstr[1] "Guerrero GuardiaTormenta"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Stormguard Warrior'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Iron Heart discipline."
msgstr ""
"Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina del Corazón de Hierro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Life and Work of Tiger Sauer"
msgid_plural "The Life and Work of Tiger Sauer"
msgstr[0] "La Vida y la Obra de Tiger Sauer"
msgstr[1] "copias de La Vida y la Obra de Tiger Sauer"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'The Life and Work of Tiger Sauer'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A biography of a combat cyborg agent detailing his philosophy and martial "
"art."
msgstr ""
"Una biografía de un agente cibernético de combate que detalla su filosofía y"
" su arte marcial."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Pocket Monster Encyclopedia"
msgid_plural "Pocket Monster Encyclopedia"
msgstr[0] "Enciclopedia de Monstruos de Bolsillo"
msgstr[1] "copias de Enciclopedia de Monstruos de Bolsillo"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Pocket Monster Encyclopedia'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This encyclopedia contains a detailed listing of the strengths and "
"techniques of various fictional monsters and how to apply them the in a real"
" fight."
msgstr ""
"Esta enciclopedia contiene una lista detallada de los puntos fuertes y las "
"técnicas de varios monstruos ficticios y cómo aplicarlos en una lucha real."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Distant Horizon"
msgid_plural "Distant Horizon"
msgstr[0] "Horizonte Distante"
msgstr[1] "copias de Horizonte Distante"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Distant Horizon'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Setting Sun discipline."
msgstr "Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina del Sol Poniente."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Jedi Holocrons: Form I"
msgid_plural "Jedi Holocrons: Form I"
msgstr[0] "Holocrón Jedi: Forma 1"
msgstr[1] "Holocrones Jedi: Forma 1"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Jedi Holocrons: Form I'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This device contains the teachings of the first form of Jedi lightsaber "
"combat: Shii-Cho."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo contiene las enseñanzas de la primera forma de combate con "
"sable láser Jedi: Shii-Cho."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Shards of Granite"
msgid_plural "Shards of Granite"
msgstr[0] " Esquirlas de Granito"
msgstr[1] "copias de Esquirlas de Granito"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Shards of Granite'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Stone Dragon discipline."
msgstr ""
"Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina del Dragón de Piedra."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Reaping Talons"
msgid_plural "Reaping Talons"
msgstr[0] "Cosechando Zarpas"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cosechando Zarpas"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Reaping Talons'}
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This book contains the teaching of the Tiger Claw discipline."
msgstr ""
"Este libro contiene la enseñanza de la disciplina de la Garra del Tigre."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Spellcraft Theory"
msgid_plural "copies of Spellcraft Theory"
msgstr[0] "Teoría de la Hechicería"
msgstr[1] "copias de la Teoría de la Hechicería"

#. ~ Description for Spellcraft Theory
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A intermediate textbook on magical theories."
msgstr "Un libro de texto intermedio sobre teorías mágicas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Basic Spellcraft Theory"
msgid_plural "copies of Basic Spellcraft Theory"
msgstr[0] "Teoría Básica de Hechicería"
msgstr[1] "copias de Teoría Básica de Hechicería"

#. ~ Description for Basic Spellcraft Theory
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A beginner textbook on magical theories."
msgstr "Un libro de texto para principiantes sobre teorías mágicas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Black Dragons: Swamp Ruins"
msgid_plural "copies of Black Dragons: Swamp Ruins"
msgstr[0] "Dragones Negros: Ruinas de Pantanos"
msgstr[1] "copias de Dragones Negros: Ruinas de Pantanos"

#. ~ Description for Black Dragons: Swamp Ruins
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book details black dragons: The most evil of dragons, who live in ruins"
" generally in swamps.  Immune to acid and breathe acid.  The book also "
"details how to prepare its hide and craft various armors that make use of "
"some of its acid resistance."
msgstr ""
"Este libro detalla los dragones negros: El más malvado de los dragones, que "
"viven en ruinas generalmente en pantanos. Son inmunes al ácido y respiran "
"ácido. El libro también detalla cómo preparar su pellejo y fabricar varias "
"armaduras que utilizan parte de su resistencia al ácido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A Comprehensive Analysis on Black Dragons"
msgid_plural "copies of A Comprehensive Analysis on Black Dragons"
msgstr[0] "Un Análisis Exhaustivo Sobre los Dragones Negros"
msgstr[1] "copias de Un Análisis Exhaustivo Sobre los Dragones Negros"

#. ~ Description for A Comprehensive Analysis on Black Dragons
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This book painstakingly delves into the history of black dragons, gruesomely"
" detailing their acts, the cults that worship them, and those that oppose "
"them.  In its pages are some alchemical formulae that can be concocted using"
" the remains of dead black dragons."
msgstr ""
"Este libro profundiza en la historia de los dragones negros, detallando "
"terriblemente sus actos, los cultos que los adoran y los que se oponen a "
"ellos. En sus páginas se encuentran algunas fórmulas alquímicas que pueden "
"ser elaboradas usando los restos de dragones negros muertos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A Beginner's Guide to Alchemy"
msgid_plural "copies of A Beginner's Guide to Alchemy"
msgstr[0] "Una Guía de Alquimia para Principiantes"
msgstr[1] "copias de Una Guía de Alquimia para Principiantes"

#. ~ Description for A Beginner's Guide to Alchemy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A paperback tome for the art of liquid magic, alcohol not included."
msgstr "Un tomo de bolsillo para el arte de la magia líquida, sin alcohol."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A Soulbinder's Guide to Necromancy"
msgid_plural "copies of A Soulbinder's Guide to Necromancy"
msgstr[0] "Una Guía de Nigromancia Para el Alma"
msgstr[1] "copias de Una Guía de Nigromancia Para el Alma"

#. ~ Description for A Soulbinder's Guide to Necromancy
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A paperback tome for the art of binding undead creatures' souls to dolls, "
"along with emulating their healing factor."
msgstr ""
"Un tomo de bolsillo para el arte de atar las almas de las criaturas no "
"muertas a las muñecas, junto con la emulación de su factor de curación."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Magitek Illustrated"
msgid_plural "copies of Magitek Illustrated"
msgstr[0] "Magitek Ilustrado"
msgstr[1] "copias de Magitek Ilustrado"

#. ~ Description for Magitek Illustrated
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A paperback tome for the art of combining modern technology with magic.  "
"There is a disclaimer on the back: `Cannith Industries bears no "
"responsibility for malfunctions or accidents for any products mentioned "
"herein`."
msgstr ""
"Un tomo de bolsillo para el arte de combinar la tecnología moderna con la "
"magia. Hay una cláusula de exención de responsabilidad en el reverso: "
"\"Industrias Cannith no se hace responsable de los fallos de funcionamiento "
"o accidentes de los productos aquí mencionados\"."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The Weapons of Asgard and Beyond"
msgid_plural "copies of The Weapons of Asgard and Beyond"
msgstr[0] "Las Armas de Asgard y Más Allá"
msgstr[1] "copias de Las Armas de Asgard y Más Allá"

#. ~ Description for The Weapons of Asgard and Beyond
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ornate book which appears to be written in Norse runes.  Based on the "
"detailed illustrations, it appears to contain information about crafting "
"numerous weapons used by various Gods."
msgstr ""
"Un libro ornamentado que parece estar escrito en runas nórdicas. Basado en "
"las detalladas ilustraciones, parece contener información sobre la "
"fabricación de numerosas armas usadas por varios dioses."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Cooking with Poison"
msgid_plural "copies of Cooking with Poison"
msgstr[0] "Cocinar Con Veneno"
msgstr[1] "copias de Cocinar Con Veneno"

#. ~ Description for Cooking with Poison
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A leatherbound book with an embossed cauldron on the cover.  Inside it "
"describes ways to purify food magically."
msgstr ""
"Un libro encuadernado en cuero con un caldero en relieve en la portada. En "
"su interior describe formas de purificar la comida de forma mágica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Metals of Legend"
msgid_plural "copies of Metals of Legend"
msgstr[0] "Metales de Leyenda"
msgstr[1] "copias de Metales de Leyenda"

#. ~ Description for Metals of Legend
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A book with a brass coverplate.  It professes to teach one how to make "
"magical metals such as Orichalcum.  It is dry reading even for an alchemical"
" tome."
msgstr ""
"Un libro con una cubierta de latón. Profesa enseñar a uno a hacer metales "
"mágicos como el Oricalco. Es una lectura aburrida incluso para un tomo de "
"alquimia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Protection from Magical Beasts"
msgid_plural "copies of Protection from Magical Beasts"
msgstr[0] "Protección Contra las Bestias Mágicas"
msgstr[1] "copias de Protección Contra las Bestias Mágicas"

#. ~ Description for Protection from Magical Beasts
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A leatherbound book with a picture of a shield holding back dragonfire on "
"the cover.  There are many ways to turn monster skins and hides into "
"protective equipment inside."
msgstr ""
"Un libro encuadernado en cuero con una imagen de un escudo que contiene "
"fuego de dragón en la portada. Hay muchas maneras de convertir los pellejos "
"y los cueros de los monstruos en equipos de protección interior."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "The art of Enchantment"
msgid_plural "copies of The art of Enchantment"
msgstr[0] "El Arte del Encantamiento"
msgstr[1] "copias de El Arte del Encantamiento"

#. ~ Description for The art of Enchantment
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "A paperback tome on the art of imbuing items with magic properties."
msgstr ""
"Un tomo de bolsillo para el arte del imbuido de objetos con propiedades "
"mágicas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Spell Scroll"
msgid_plural "Spell Scrolls"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Hechizo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Hechizo"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Crystallize Mana"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Crystallize Mana"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Cristalización de Maná"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Cristalización de Maná"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Crystallize Mana
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A proper wizard is always prepared, crystallize your mana for the future!"
msgstr ""
"Un mago apropiado siempre está preparado, ¡cristaliza tu maná para el "
"futuro!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Dark Sight"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Dark Sight"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Visión Oscura"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Visión Oscura"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Dark Sight
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The darkness holds no secrets for the arcane.  Adjust your sight to see in "
"perfect darkness!"
msgstr ""
"La oscuridad no tiene secretos para el arcano. ¡Ajusta tu vista para ver en "
"la oscuridad perfecta!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Invisibility"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Invisibility"
msgstr[0] "Pergaminosde Invisibilidad"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invisibilidad"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Invisibility
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The light can not interact with you unless you want it to.  Become "
"invisible!"
msgstr ""
"La luz no puede interactuar con usted a menos que usted lo desee. "
"¡Conviértete en invisible!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Obfuscated Body"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Obfuscated Body"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino del Cuerpo Ofuscado"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos del Cuerpo Ofuscado"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Obfuscated Body
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A magical aura distorts light around your body, making it easier to dodge "
"enemy attacks."
msgstr ""
"Un aura mágica distorsiona la luz alrededor de tu cuerpo, haciendo más fácil"
" esquivar los ataques enemigos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Holographic Transposition"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Holographic Transposition"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Transposición Holográfica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Transposición Holográfica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Holographic Transposition
#. ~ Description for Holographic Transposition
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Allows you to swap places with a previously existing holographic image of "
"yourself.  If the universe itself can't tell you apart, who could?"
msgstr ""
"Le permite intercambiar lugares con una imagen holográfica de sí mismo "
"previamente existente. Si el propio universo no puede diferenciarte, ¿quién "
"podría?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Smite"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Smite"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Golpe"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Golpe"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Smite
#. ~ Description for Smite
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Evil has become pervasive throughout the world.  Let your power be the light"
" that shines in the darkness!"
msgstr ""
"El mal se ha vuelto omnipresente en todo el mundo. ¡Deja que tu poder sea la"
" luz que brilla en la oscuridad!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Life Conversion"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Life Conversion"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Conversión de Vida"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Conversión de Vida"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Life Conversion
#. ~ Description for Life Conversion
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You channel your life force itself into your spiritual energy.  You spend hp"
" to regain mana."
msgstr ""
"Canalizas tu fuerza vital en tu energía espiritual. Gastas energía para "
"recuperar el maná."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Mind Over Pain"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Mind Over Pain"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Mente Sobre el Cuerpo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de la Mente Sobre el Cuerpo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Mind Over Pain
#. ~ Description for Mind over Pain
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"With an intense ritual that resembles crossfit, you manage to put some of "
"your pain at bay."
msgstr ""
"Con un intenso ritual que se asemeja al crossfit, te las arreglas para poner"
" algo de tu dolor a raya."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Baleful Polymorph"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Baleful Polymorph"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Poliformia Malévola"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Poliformia Malévola"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Baleful Polymorph
#. ~ Description for Baleful Polymorph
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Transform your enemies into frogs."
msgstr "Transforma a tus enemigos en ranas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Summon Zombie"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Summon Zombie"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Invocar Zombi"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invocar Zombi"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Summon Zombie
#. ~ Description for Summon Zombie
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ethereal-looking zombie rises from the depths of the earth to fight for "
"you.  You may be able to summon more with a higher level in this spell."
msgstr ""
"Un zombi de aspecto etéreo se levanta de las profundidades de la tierra para"
" luchar por ti. Podrás invocar más con un nivel más alto en este hechizo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Summon Skeleton"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Summon Skeleton"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Invocar Esqueleto"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invocar Esqueletos"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Summon Skeleton
#. ~ Description for Summon Skeleton
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A ghostly skeleton rises from the depths of the earth to fight for you.  You"
" may be able to summon more with a higher level in this spell."
msgstr ""
"Un esqueleto fantasmagórico se levanta de las profundidades de la tierra "
"para luchar por ti. Podrás invocar más con un nivel más alto en este "
"hechizo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Summon Floating Disk"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Summon Floating Disk"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Invocar Disco"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invocar Disco"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Summon Floating Disk
#. ~ Description for Summon floating disk
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Summons a floating disk that is sworn to carry your burdens."
msgstr "Invoca un disco flotante que se ha prometido llevar tus cosas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Summon Decayed Pouncer"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Summon Decayed Pouncer"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Invocar Asaltante Pútrido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invocar Asaltante Pútrido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Summon Decayed Pouncer
#. ~ Description for Summon Decayed Pouncer
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A decrepit looking large cat rises from the depths of the earth to fight for"
" you.  You may be able to summon more with a higher level in this spell."
msgstr ""
"Un gato grande decrépito se levanta de las profundidades de la tierra para "
"luchar por ti. Podrás invocar más con un nivel más alto en este hechizo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Cure Light Wounds"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Cure Light Wounds"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Curar Heridas Leves"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Curar Heridas Leves"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Cure Light Wounds
#. ~ Description for Cure Light Wounds
#. ~ Description for Jury Rig
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Heals a little bit of damage on the target."
msgstr "Cura un poco de daño en el objetivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Pain Split"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Pain Split"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Dolor Dividido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Dolor Dividido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Pain Split
#. ~ Description for Pain Split
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Evens out damage among your limbs."
msgstr "Empareja el daño entre tus extremidades."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Vicious Tentacle"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Vicious Tentacle"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tentáculo Vicioso"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tentáculo Vicioso"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Vicious Tentacle
#. ~ Description for Vicious Tentacle
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell extrudes a long nasty whiplike tentacle of sharp bones and oozing"
" acid from your body, it has a long reach attack and vicious damage."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo extrae de tu cuerpo un largo y desagradable tentáculo en forma "
"de latigazo de huesos afilados y ácido rezumante, tiene un ataque de largo "
"alcance y un daño feroz."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Grotesque Enhancement"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Grotesque Enhancement"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Mejora Grotesca"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Mejora Grotesca"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Grotesque Enhancement
#. ~ Description for Grotesque Enhancement
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A spell that warps your body in alien ways to increase your physical "
"abilities and strength."
msgstr ""
"Un hechizo que modifica tu cuerpo en formas alienígenas para incrementar tu "
"fuerza y habilidades físicas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Acidic Spray"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Acidic Spray"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rocío Ácido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rocío Ácido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Acidic Spray
#. ~ Description for Acidic Spray
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"When cast, the mage opens his mouth and sprays acid in a wide cone to "
"dissolve his foes into goo.  Just imagine what he'll do with the goo."
msgstr ""
"Cuando es lanzado, el mago abre su boca y rocía ácido en un cono ancho para "
"disolver a sus enemigos en la sustancia viscosa. Imagina lo que hará con la "
"sustancia viscosa."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Flesh Pouch"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Flesh Pouch"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Bolsa de Carne"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Bolsa de Carne"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Flesh Pouch
#. ~ Description for Flesh Pouch
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell grows a large pouch out of your skin on your back, allowing you "
"to store your gear in it."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo hace crecer una gran bolsa de su piel en la espalda, "
"permitiéndole almacenar su equipo en ella."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Conjure Bonespear"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Conjure Bonespear"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Conjurar Lanza de Hueso"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Conjurar Lanza de Hueso"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Conjure Bonespear
#. ~ Description for Conjure Bonespear
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell creates a long shaft of bone with a wicked point and blades along"
" its length."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo crea un largo eje de hueso con una punta malvada y cuchillas a "
"lo largo de su longitud."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Megablast"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Megablast"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de MegaImpacto"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de MegaImpacto"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Megablast
#. ~ Description for Megablast
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You always wanted to fire energy beams like in the animes you watched as a "
"kid.  Now you can!"
msgstr ""
"Siempre quisiste disparar rayos de energía como en los animes que veías de "
"niño. ¡Ahora puedes!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Magical Light"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Magical Light"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Luz Mágica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Luz Mágica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Magical Light
#. ~ Description for Magical Light
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Creates a magical light."
msgstr "Crea una luz mágica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Blinding Flash"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Blinding Flash"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Flash Cegador"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Flash Cegador"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Blinding Flash
#. ~ Description for Blinding Flash
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Blind enemies for a short time with a sudden, dazzling light.  Higher levels"
" deal slightly higher damage."
msgstr ""
"Ciega a los enemigos por un corto tiempo con una repentina y deslumbrante "
"luz. Los niveles más altos causan un daño ligeramente mayor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ethereal Grasp"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ethereal Grasp"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Agarre Etéreo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Agarre Etéreo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ethereal Grasp
#. ~ Description for Ethereal Grasp
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A mass of spectral hands emerge from the ground, slowing everything in "
"range.  Higher levels allow a bigger AoE, and longer effect."
msgstr ""
"Una masa de manos espectrales emergen del suelo, frenando todo lo que está a"
" su alcance. Los niveles más altos permiten un mayor área de efecto, y un "
"efecto más largo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Aura of Protection"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Aura of Protection"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Aura de Protección"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Aura de Protección"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Aura of Protection
#. ~ Description for Aura of Protection
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Encases your whole body in a magical aura that protects you from the "
"environment."
msgstr "Envuelve todo tu cuerpo en un aura mágica que te protege del entorno."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Vegetative Grasp"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Vegetative Grasp"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Agarre Vegetativo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Agarre Vegetativo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Vegetative Grasp
#. ~ Description for Vegetative Grasp
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell causes roots and vines to burst forth from the ground and grab "
"your foes, slowing them and doing a small amount of damage as they dig in."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo hace que las raíces y las enredaderas broten del suelo y se "
"agarren a tus enemigos, ralentizándolos y causando una pequeña cantidad de "
"daño mientras cavan."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Root Strike"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Root Strike"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Golpe de Raíz"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos del Golpe de Raíz"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Root Strike
#. ~ Description for Root Strike
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell causes roots to spear out the ground and stab into your foes in "
"an arc, impaling them."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo hace que las raíces salgan del suelo y apuñalen a sus enemigos "
"en un arco, empalándolos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Wooden Shaft"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Wooden Shaft"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Asta de Madera"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos del Asta de Madera"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Wooden Shaft
#. ~ Description for Wooden Shaft
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell creates a projectile of hardwood that shoots forth from the "
"caster's hand at high speed to stab into an enemy."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo crea un proyectil de madera dura que sale disparado de la mano "
"del lanzador a gran velocidad para apuñalar a un enemigo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Nature's Bow"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Nature's Bow"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Arco de la Naturaleza"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Arco de la Naturaleza"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Nature's Bow
#. ~ Description for Nature's Bow
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell conjures a magical wooden recurve bow that fires endless arrows "
"for as long as it lasts."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo conjura un mágico arco curvo de madera que dispara infinitas "
"flechas mientras dure."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Nature's Trance"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Nature's Trance"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Trance de la Naturaleza"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Trance de la Naturaleza"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Nature's Trance
#. ~ Description for Nature's Trance
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Your connection to living things allows you to go into a magical trance.  "
"This allows you to recover fatigue quickly in exchange for mana."
msgstr ""
"Tu conexión con los seres vivos te permite entrar en un trance mágico. Esto "
"te permite recuperarte de la fatiga rápidamente a cambio de maná."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Bag of Cats"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Bag of Cats"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Bolsa de Gatos"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Bolsa de Gatos"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Bag of Cats
#. ~ Description for Bag of Cats
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Are you the crazy cat lady?"
msgstr "¿Eres la señora loca de los gatos?"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Summon Wolf"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Summon Wolf"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Invocar Lobo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Invocar Lobo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Summon Wolf
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Call to the wild for aid from some wolves."
msgstr "Llama a la naturaleza para pedir ayuda a algunos lobos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Stonefist"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Stonefist"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Puño de Piedra"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Puño de Piedra"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Stonefist
#. ~ Description for Stonefist
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Encases your arms and hands in a sheath of magical stone, you can punch and "
"defend yourself with it in melee combat."
msgstr ""
"Encierra tus brazos y manos en una vaina de piedra mágica, puedes golpear y "
"defenderte con ella en el combate cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Seismic Stomp"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Seismic Stomp"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Pisotón Sísmico"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Pisotón Sísmico"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Seismic Stomp
#. ~ Description for Seismic Stomp
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Focusing mana into your leg, you stomp your foot and send out a shockwave, "
"knocking enemies around you onto the ground."
msgstr ""
"Al concentrar el maná en tu pierna, pisas a fondo y envías una onda "
"expansiva que hace caer al suelo a los enemigos que te rodean."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Stone's Endurance"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Stone's Endurance"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Resistencia de Piedra"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Resistencia de Piedra"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Stone's Endurance
#. ~ Description for Stone's Endurance
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You focus on the stones beneath you and draw from their agelessness.  Your "
"mana is converted to stamina."
msgstr ""
"Te concentras en las piedras que están debajo de ti y extraes de su "
"intemporalidad. Tu maná se convierte en vigor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Shardspray"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Shardspray"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rocio de Esquirlas"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rocio de Esquirlas"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Shardspray
#. ~ Description for Shardspray
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell projects a wide spray of sharp metal shards, cutting into your "
"foes and friends alike."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo proyecta un amplio rocío de afilados fragmentos de metal, "
"cortando a tus enemigos y amigos por igual."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Piercing Bolt"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Piercing Bolt"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Saeta Perforante"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Saeta Perforante"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Piercing Bolt
#. ~ Description for Piercing Bolt
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell projects a piercing rod of conjured iron at those that dare "
"oppose you."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo proyecta una varilla de hierro conjurado a aquellos que se "
"atrevan a oponerse a ti."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Shardstorm"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Shardstorm"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tormenta de Esquirlas"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tormenta de Esquirlas"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Shardstorm
#. ~ Description for Shardstorm
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Creates an omnidirectional spray of razor sharp metal shards all around you."
msgstr ""
"Crea un rocío omnidireccional de fragmentos metálicos afilados a tu "
"alrededor."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Rockbolt"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Rockbolt"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rayo Pétreo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rayo Pétreo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Rockbolt
#. ~ Description for Rockbolt
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Fires a conjured stone projectile at high velocity."
msgstr "Dispara un proyectil de piedra conjurado a alta velocidad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Point Flare"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Point Flare"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Punto de Inflamación"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Punto de Inflamación"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Point Flare
#. ~ Description for Point Flare
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Causes an intense heat at the location, damaging the target."
msgstr "Causa un intenso calor en el lugar, dañando el objetivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Finger Firelighter"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Finger Firelighter"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Mechero de Dedo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Mechero de Dedo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Finger Firelighter
#. ~ Description for Finger Firelighter
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Summons a small flame that does not burn you, but you can use it to light "
"things on fire.  It seems to need you to have some intent to light things on"
" fire, because you are able to put it in your pocket with no issue."
msgstr ""
"Invoca una pequeña llama que no te quema, pero puedes usarla para prender "
"cosas. Parece que necesita que tengas alguna intención de encender cosas con"
" fuego, porque eres capaz de ponerla en tu bolsillo sin problemas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ice Spike"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ice Spike"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Pua de Hielo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Pua de Hielo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ice Spike
#. ~ Description for Ice Spike
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Causes jagged icicles to form in the air above the target, falling and "
"damaging it."
msgstr ""
"Hace que se formen carámbanos irregulares en el aire por encima del "
"objetivo, cayendo y dañándolo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Fireball"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Fireball"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Bola de Fuego"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Bola de Fuego"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Fireball
#. ~ Description for Fireball
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You hurl a pea-sized glowing orb that when reaches its target or an obstacle"
" produces a pressure-less blast of searing heat."
msgstr ""
"Lanzas un orbe brillante del tamaño de un guisante que al llegar a su "
"objetivo o a un obstáculo produce una ráfaga sin presión de calor abrasador."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Cone of Cold"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Cone of Cold"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Cono de Frío"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Cono de Frío"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Cone of Cold
#. ~ Description for Cryokinetic blast
#. ~ Description for Cone of Cold
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You blast a cone of frigid air toward the target."
msgstr "Se lanza un cono de aire gélido hacia el objetivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Burning Hands"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Burning Hands"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Manos Ardientes"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Manos Ardientes"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Burning Hands
#. ~ Description for Burning Hands
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You're pretty sure you saw this in a game somewhere.  You fire a short-range"
" cone of fire."
msgstr ""
"Estás bastante seguro de que viste esto en un juego en alguna parte. "
"Disparas un cono de fuego de corto alcance."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Frost Spray"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Frost Spray"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rocío de Escarcha"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rocío de Escarcha"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Frost Spray
#. ~ Description for Frost Spray
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You're pretty sure you saw this in a game somewhere.  You fire a short-range"
" cone of ice and cold."
msgstr ""
"Estás bastante seguro de que viste esto en un juego en alguna parte. "
"Disparas un cono de corto alcance de hielo y frío."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Chilling Touch"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Chilling Touch"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Toque Gélido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Toque Gélido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Chilling Touch
#. ~ Description for Chilling Touch
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Freezes the touched target with intense cold."
msgstr "Congela el objetivo tocado con un frío intenso."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Glide on Ice"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Glide on Ice"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Deslizamiento sobre Hielo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Deslizamiento sobre Hielo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Glide on Ice
#. ~ Description for Glide on Ice
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Encases your feet in a magical coating of ice, allowing you to glide along "
"smooth surfaces faster."
msgstr ""
"Encierra los pies en una mágica capa de hielo, permitiéndote deslizarse por "
"superficies lisas más rápido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Hoary Blast"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Hoary Blast"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Explosión de Escarcha"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Explosión de Escarcha"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Hoary Blast
#. ~ Description for Hoary Blast
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You project a glowing white crystal of ice and it explodes on impact into a "
"blossom of shattering cold."
msgstr ""
"Proyectas un brillante cristal blanco de hielo y explota al impactar en un "
"brote de frío desgarrador."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ice Shield"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ice Shield"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Escudo de Hielo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Escudo de Hielo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ice Shield
#. ~ Description for Ice Shield
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Creates a magical shield of ice on your arm, you can defend yourself with it"
" in melee combat and use it to bash."
msgstr ""
"Crea un escudo mágico de hielo en tu brazo, puedes defenderte con él en el "
"combate cuerpo a cuerpo y usarlo para golpear."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Frost Armor"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Frost Armor"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Armadura de Hielo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Armadura de Hielo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Frost Armor
#. ~ Description for Frost Armor
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Covers you in a thin layer of magical ice to protect you from harm."
msgstr ""
"Te cubre en una fina capa de hielo mágico para protegerte de los daños."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Shadow Field"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Shadow Field"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Campo Sombra"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Campo Sombra"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Shadow Field
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Cast a field of shadows."
msgstr "Lanza un campo de sombras."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Magic Missile"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Magic Missile"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Misil Mágico"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Misil Mágico"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Magic Missile
#. ~ Description for Magic Missile
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "I cast Magic Missile at the darkness!"
msgstr "Lanza un misil mágico a un objetivo que es capaz de atravesar muros. "

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Phase Door"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Phase Door"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Puerta de Fase"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Puerta de Fase"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Phase Door
#. ~ Description for Phase Door
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Teleports you in a random direction a short distance."
msgstr "Te teletransporta en una dirección aleatoria a una distancia corta."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Gravity Well"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Gravity Well"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Pozo de Gravedad"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Pozo de Gravedad"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Gravity Well
#. ~ Description for Gravity Well
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Summons a well of gravity with the epicenter at the location.  Deals bashing"
" damage to all creatures in the affected area."
msgstr ""
"Invoca un pozo de gravedad. Hace daño de impacto a todas las criaturas en el"
" área afectada."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Mana Blast"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Mana Blast"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Explosión Mana"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Explosión Mana"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Mana Blast
#. ~ Description for Mana Blast
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "A blast of concentrated magical power that obliterates a large area."
msgstr "Una explosión de poder mágico concentrado que destruye una gran área."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Mana Bolt"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Mana Bolt"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Saeta de Maná"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Saeta de Maná"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Mana Bolt
#. ~ Description for Mana Bolt
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "A bolt of magical power that only damages your foes."
msgstr "Un rayo de poder mágico que sólo daña a tus enemigos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Haste"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Haste"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Velocidad"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Velocidad"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Haste
#. ~ Description for Haste
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell gives you an enormous boost of speed lasting a short period of "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo te da un enorme impulso de velocidad que dura un corto período "
"de tiempo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Mana Beam"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Mana Beam"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rayo de Mana"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rayo de Mana"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Mana Beam
#. ~ Description for Mana Beam
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "A beam of focused magical power that damages any foes in its path."
msgstr ""
"Un rayo de poder mágico enfocado que daña a cualquier enemigo en su camino."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Escape"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Escape"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Escape"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Escape"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Escape
#. ~ Description for Escape
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Teleports you in a random direction a medium distance, to help escape your "
"foes in dangerous situations."
msgstr ""
"Te teletransporta en una dirección aleatoria a media distancia, para ayudar "
"a escapar de tus enemigos en situaciones peligrosas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Cat's Grace"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Cat's Grace"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Gracia de Gato"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Gracia de Gato"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Cat's Grace
#. ~ Description for Cat's Grace
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You become more graceful, agile, and coordinated."
msgstr "Te vuelves más grácil, ágil y coordinado."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Eagle's Sight"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Eagle's Sight"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Vista de Águila"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Vista de Águila"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Eagle's Sight
#. ~ Description for Eagle's Sight
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You gain the perception of an eagle."
msgstr "Se obtiene la percepción de un águila."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ogre's Strength"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ogre's Strength"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Fuerza del Ogro"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Fuerza del Ogro"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ogre's Strength
#. ~ Description for Ogre's Strength
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You gain the strength of an ogre."
msgstr "Se gana la fuerza de un ogro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Fox's Cunning"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Fox's Cunning"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Astucia de Zorro"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Astucia de Zorro"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Fox's Cunning
#. ~ Description for Fox's Cunning
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You become wily like a fox."
msgstr "Te vuelves astuto como un zorro."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Shocking Lash"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Shocking Lash"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Azote Eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Azote Eléctrico"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Shocking Lash
#. ~ Description for Shocking Lash
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A quick burst of electricity strikes a target and possibly one other nearby."
msgstr ""
"Una rápida ráfaga de electricidad golpea a un objetivo y posiblemente a otro"
" cercano."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Jolt"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Jolt"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Sacudida"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Sacudida"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Jolt
#. ~ Description for Jolt
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "A short-ranged fan of electricity shoots from your fingers."
msgstr ""
"Un ventilador de corto alcance de electricidad se dispara desde tus dedos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lightning Bolt"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lightning Bolt"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rayo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rayo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lightning Bolt
#. ~ Description for Lightning Bolt
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The goto spell for many Stormshapers, this iconic spell does just what you "
"expect: you shoot lightning from your fingertips.  However, this lightning "
"is more directed than most lightning, and travels in a line through most "
"non-solid targets."
msgstr ""
"El hechizo básico para muchos Moldeadores de Tormentas, este icónico hechizo"
" hace justo lo que esperas: disparas rayos con la punta de los dedos. Sin "
"embargo, este rayo está más dirigido que la mayoría de los rayos, y viaja en"
" línea a través de la mayoría de los objetivos no sólidos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Windstrike"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Windstrike"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Golpe de Viento"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Golpe de Viento"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Windstrike
#. ~ Description for Windstrike
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A powerful blast of wind slams into anything in front of your outstretched "
"hand."
msgstr ""
"Una poderosa ráfaga de viento golpea cualquier cosa frente a tu mano "
"extendida."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Windrunning"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Windrunning"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Corredor de Viento"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Corredor de Viento"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Windrunning
#. ~ Description for Windrunning
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A magical wind pushes you forward as you move, easing your movements and "
"increasing speed."
msgstr ""
"Un viento mágico te empuja hacia adelante a medida que te mueves, "
"facilitando tus movimientos y aumentando la velocidad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Call Stormhammer"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Call Stormhammer"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Llamada De Martillo de Tormenta"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Llamada De Martillo de Tormenta"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Call Stormhammer
#. ~ Description for Call Stormhammer
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Creates a crackling magical warhammer full of lightning to smite your foes "
"with, and of course, smash things to bits!"
msgstr ""
"Crea un crepitante martillo mágico lleno de relámpagos para golpear a tus "
"enemigos y, por supuesto, ¡hacer añicos las cosas!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Bless"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Bless"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Bendición"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Bendición"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Bless
#. ~ Description for Bless
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "A spell of blessing that gives you energy and boosts your abilities."
msgstr "Un hechizo de bendición que te da energía y aumenta tus habilidades."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Holy Blade"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Holy Blade"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Espada Sagrada"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Espada Sagrada"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Holy Blade
#. ~ Description for Holy Blade
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "This blade of light will cut through any evil it makes contact with!"
msgstr "¡Esta hoja de luz cortará cualquier mal con el que entre en contacto!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Spiritual Armor"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Spiritual Armor"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Armadura Espiritual"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Armadura Espiritual"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Spiritual Armor
#. ~ Description for Spiritual Armor
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Evil will not make it through your defenses if your faith is strong enough!"
msgstr ""
"¡El mal no logrará atravesar sus defensas si su fe es lo suficientemente "
"fuerte!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lamp"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lamp"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Lámpara"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Lámpara"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lamp
#. ~ Description for Lamp
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Creates a magical lamp."
msgstr "Crea una lámpara mágica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Manatricity"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Manatricity"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Manatricidad"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Manatricidad"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Manatricity
#. ~ Description for Manatricity
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You have found a way to convert your spiritual energy into power you can use"
" for your bionics."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una forma de convertir tu energía espiritual en un poder que "
"puedes usar para tu biónica."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Taze"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Taze"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Taser"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Taser"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Taze
#. ~ Description for Taze
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell creates a very short range bolt of electricity to shock your "
"foes."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo crea un rayo de electricidad de muy corto alcance para impactar"
" a tus enemigos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lesser Quantum Tunnel"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lesser Quantum Tunnel"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Túnel Cuántico Menor"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Túnel Cuántico Menor"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lesser Quantum Tunnel
#. ~ Description for Lesser Quantum Tunnel
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell manipulates some quantum something or other to tunnel you through"
" a short distance of space, and even matter, unfortunately there's that "
"whole uncertainty thing as to where you come out.  It leaves you a little "
"dazed on the other side as you reorient yourself."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo manipula algo cuántico para hacerte un túnel a través de una "
"corta distancia del espacio, e incluso de la materia, desafortunadamente hay"
" toda esa incertidumbre de dónde sales. Te deja un poco aturdido en el otro "
"lado mientras te reorientas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Synaptic Stimulation"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Synaptic Stimulation"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Estimulación Sináptica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Estimulación Sináptica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Synaptic Stimulation
#. ~ Description for Synaptic Stimulation
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell stimulates the synapses in your brain beyond normal processing "
"speeds, giving you a large boost in mental processing capability, including "
"enhancing your reflexes, speed, and raw intellectual power.  Use "
"responsibly!"
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo estimula la sinapsis en tu cerebro más allá de las velocidades "
"de procesamiento normal, dándote un gran impulso en la capacidad de "
"procesamiento mental, incluyendo la mejora de tus reflejos, velocidad y el "
"poder intelectual en bruto. ¡Úsalo responsablemente!"

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Laze"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Laze"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Pereza"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Pereza"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Laze
#. ~ Description for Laze
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You concentrate and release a focused beam of photons at a target, also "
"known as a laser."
msgstr ""
"Te concentras y liberas un rayo de fotones enfocados en un objetivo, también"
" conocido como láser."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Animated Blade"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Animated Blade"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Espada Animada"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Espada Animada"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Animated Blade
#. ~ Description for Animated Blade
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell conjures flying animated blades that will cut your enemies down "
"to size.  Into small pieces that is."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo conjura espadas voladoras animadas que cortarán a tus enemigos "
"a medida. En pequeños trozos quiero decir."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Mirror Image"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Mirror Image"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Imagen Espejo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Imagen Espejo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Mirror Image
#. ~ Description for Mirror Image
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This spell manipulates light into barely tangible duplicates of a living "
"being, a magical hologram in short."
msgstr ""
"Este hechizo manipula la luz para crear duplicados poco reales de un ser "
"vivo, un holograma mágico en definitiva."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lightning Blast"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lightning Blast"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Bomba Eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Bomba Eléctrica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lightning Blast
#. ~ Description for Lightning Blast
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You fire a small concentrated ball of lightning at the target.  The "
"electricity diffuses quickly, so it doesn't do much damage, but you're able "
"to fire off several quick ones in a row."
msgstr ""
"Disparas una pequeña bola concentrada de rayos al objetivo. La electricidad "
"se difunde rápidamente, así que no hace mucho daño, pero puedes disparar "
"varias veces seguidas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Necrotic Gaze"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Necrotic Gaze"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Mirada Necrótica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Mirada Necrótica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Necrotic Gaze
#. ~ Description for Necrotic Gaze
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You use the power of your own blood to imbue necrotic energy into your gaze,"
" damaging the target you look at."
msgstr ""
"Utilizas el poder de tu propia sangre para impregnar la energía necrótica en"
" tu mirada, dañando el objetivo que miras."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Purification Seed"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Purification Seed"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Semilla de Purificación"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Semilla de Purificación"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Purification Seed
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You summon a gift of the earth which will purify water.  Greater levels "
"yield greater numbers of seeds."
msgstr ""
"Invoca una semilla de la tierra que purificará el agua. Los niveles más "
"altos producen un mayor número de semillas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of X-ray Vision"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of X-ray Vision"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Visión de Rayos X"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Visión de Rayos X"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of X-ray Vision
#. ~ Description for X-ray Vision
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You fire a cone of X-rays that magically allow you to see that area for a "
"short time."
msgstr ""
"Disparas un cono de rayos X que mágicamente te permite ver esa área por un "
"corto tiempo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Optical Sneeze Beam"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Optical Sneeze Beam"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Rayo Óptico"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Rayo Óptico"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Optical Sneeze Beam
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You overcharge your internal batteries to send a semi-directed beam from "
"your face."
msgstr ""
"Sobrecargas tus baterías internas para enviar un rayo semi-direccional desde"
" tu cara."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Clairvoyance"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Clairvoyance"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Clarividencia"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Clarividencia"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Clairvoyance
#. ~ Description for Clairvoyance
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "You close your eyes and the earth surrenders its secrets to you."
msgstr "Cierras los ojos y la tierra te entrega sus secretos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Bleed"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Bleed"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Sangrado"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Sangrado"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Bleed
#. ~ Description for Bleed
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"With a shout and a gesture, the target starts bleeding from old wounds."
msgstr ""
"Con un grito y un gesto, el objetivo empieza a sangrar por viejas heridas."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lesser Banishment"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lesser Banishment"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Destierro Menor"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Destierro Menor"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lesser Banishment
#. ~ Description for Lesser Banishment
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Banish a monster to the lesser-known nether dimension.  If a monster is more"
" powerful than you can handle, the spell drains your life force to make up "
"the difference."
msgstr ""
"Destierra a un monstruo a la dimensión inferior menos conocida. Si un "
"monstruo es más poderoso de lo que puedes manejar, el hechizo drena tu "
"fuerza vital para compensar la diferencia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Acid Resistance"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Acid Resistance"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Resistencia al Ácido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Resistencia al Ácido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Acid Resistance
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "This spell creates an invisible aura to protect you from acid."
msgstr "Este hechizo crea un aura invisible para protegerte del ácido."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Lightning Storm"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Lightning Storm"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tormenta Eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tormenta Eléctrica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Lightning Storm
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This scroll details how a spell called 'Lightning Blast' which is commonly "
"used among Stormshapers can be altered to become much more powerful, at a "
"much higher mana cost."
msgstr ""
"Este pergamino detalla cómo un hechizo llamado \"Explosión del Relámpago\" "
"que se utiliza comúnmente entre los Moldeadores de Tormentas puede ser "
"alterado para ser mucho más poderoso, a un costo de maná mucho más alto."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Sacrificial Regrowth"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Sacrificial Regrowth"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Recrecimiento Sacrificado"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Recrecimiento Sacrificado"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Sacrificial Regrowth
#. ~ Description for Sacrificial Regrowth
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Through giving of one's own life force, you restore withered and barren "
"plant life nearby.  What remains will need time to regrow its full strength."
msgstr ""
"A través de la entrega de la propia fuerza de vida, se restaura la vida "
"vegetal seca y estéril cercana. Lo que queda necesitará tiempo para "
"recuperar toda su fuerza."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Sacrificial Healing"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Sacrificial Healing"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Curación por Sacrificio"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Curación por Sacrificio"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Sacrificial Healing
#. ~ Description for Sacrificial Healing
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Channels some of the user's own life force into healing energy, for the sake"
" of ones allies."
msgstr ""
"Canalizar parte de la fuerza vital del usuario en energía curativa, por el "
"bien de sus aliados."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Stoneskin"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Stoneskin"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Piel de Piedra"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Piel de Piedra"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Stoneskin
#. ~ Description for Stoneskin
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Envelops your entire body in armor formed from living rock, encumbering yet "
"protective."
msgstr ""
"Envuelve todo el cuerpo en una armadura formada por roca viva, que es a la "
"vez gravosa y protectora."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Pillar of Stone"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Pillar of Stone"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Pilar de Piedra"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Pilar de Piedra"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Pillar of Stone
#. ~ Description for Pillar of Stone
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Drawing upon the surrounding earth, you form a pillar of solid rock.  "
"Experience will make the task easier, and less disruptive to the surrounding"
" area."
msgstr ""
"Dibujando sobre la tierra circundante, se forma un pilar de roca sólida. La "
"experiencia hará la tarea más fácil, y menos perturbadora para el área "
"circundante."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Paralytic Dart"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Paralytic Dart"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Dardo Paralízante"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Dardo Paralízante"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Paralytic Dart
#. ~ Description for Paralytic Dart
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Spits a warped needle of sinew and bone, carrying with it a sting that slows"
" your victim."
msgstr ""
"Escupe una aguja deformada de tendón y hueso, llevando consigo un aguijón "
"que ralentiza a su víctima."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Visceral Projection"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Visceral Projection"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Proyección Visceral"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Proyección Visceral"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Visceral Projection
#. ~ Description for Visceral Projection
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Projects a spray of acrid blood and gore all around you, growing to ensnare "
"your prey in in a field of twitching poisonous tendrils."
msgstr ""
"Proyecta un rocío de sangre acre a tu alrededor, creciendo para atrapar a tu"
" presa en un campo de zarcillos venenosos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Coagulant Weave"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Coagulant Weave"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tejido Coagulante"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tejido Coagulante"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Coagulant Weave
#. ~ Description for Coagulant Weave
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Turns your biological mastery inwards, medically enhancing your flesh.  "
"Rather than strength of healing, it staves off blood loss and purges wounds "
"before they can turn septic, at the cost of increased hunger and thirst."
msgstr ""
"Vuelve tu dominio biológico hacia adentro, mejorando médicamente tu carne. "
"En lugar de la fuerza de curación, evita la pérdida de sangre y purga las "
"heridas antes de que se vuelvan sépticas, a costa del aumento del hambre y "
"la sed."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ionization"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ionization"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Ionización"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Ionización"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ionization
#. ~ Description for Ionization
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"By manipulating the charge in the air, you can conjure a sharp snap of "
"lightning over a wide area.  While its destructive potential is a far cry "
"from natural lightning, the light and thunderclap produced will leave your "
"foes reeling."
msgstr ""
"Manipulando la carga en el aire, se puede conjurar un chasquido agudo de un "
"rayo sobre una amplia área. Aunque su potencial destructivo está muy lejos "
"del de los relámpagos naturales, la luz y el trueno producidos dejarán a tus"
" enemigos tambaleándose."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Ignus Fatuus"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Ignus Fatuus"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Ignífugo Fatuo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Ignífugo Fatuo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Ignus Fatuus
#. ~ Description for Ignus Fatuus
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Summons ghostly foxfire worked from living marsh vapor, to lead your enemies"
" astray.  With more experience, this spell can conjure multiple ghost "
"lights."
msgstr ""
"Invoca un fantasmal fuego fatuo del vapor de pantano, para extraviar a tus "
"enemigos. Con más experiencia, este hechizo puede conjurar múltiples luces "
"fantasmales."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Wall of Fog"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Wall of Fog"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Muro de Niebla"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Muro de Niebla"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Wall of Fog
#. ~ Description for Wall of Fog
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Draws forth a broad wall of thick fog.  While the sudden force of air "
"pressure will floor any enemies caught in it, the conjuration is otherwise "
"harmless."
msgstr ""
"Dibuja una amplia pared de niebla espesa. Mientras que la repentina fuerza "
"de la presión del aire derribará a cualquier enemigo atrapado en ella, el "
"conjuro es por lo demás inofensivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Knock"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Knock"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Toque de Puerta"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Toque de Puerta"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Knock
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You can channel magical energy to open locked wooden doors from a short "
"range away."
msgstr ""
"Puedes canalizar la energía mágica para abrir puertas de madera cerradas a "
"corta distancia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Improved Knock"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Improved Knock"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Toque de Puerta Mejorado"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Toque de Puerta Mejorado"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Improved Knock
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You can channel magical energy to open any locked door from a short range "
"away."
msgstr ""
"Puedes canalizar la energía mágica para abrir cualquier puerta cerrada a "
"corta distancia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Repelling Arc"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Repelling Arc"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Arco Repelente"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Arco Repelente"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Repelling Arc
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You manifest an aura of crackling electricity around you to strike attackers"
" with baleful lightning."
msgstr ""
"Manifiestas un aura de electricidad crepitante a tu alrededor para golpear a"
" los atacantes con un relámpago maligno."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Sappy Scroll"
msgid_plural "Sappy Scrolls"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino con Savia"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos con Savia"

#. ~ Description for Sappy Scroll
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This scroll is covered in sap and rose thorns.  You can still make out some "
"of the writings, but it probably won't work the same."
msgstr ""
"Este pergamino está cubierto de savia y espinas de rosa. Todavía puedes ver "
"algunos de los escritos, pero probablemente no funcionará igual."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Feral Form"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Feral Form"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Forma Salvaje"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Forma Salvaje"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Feral Form
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Unleash your inner beast by snapping a fur-covered bone, becoming beastly."
msgstr ""
"Libera tu bestia interior rompiendo un hueso cubierto de piel, "
"convirtiéndote en bestia."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Flamesword"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Flamesword"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Espada Flamígera"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Espada Flamígera"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Flamesword
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Ignite a wooden sword to create a flaming saber."
msgstr "Encender una espada de madera para crear un sable llameante."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Flamebreath"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Flamebreath"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Aliento de Llama"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Aliento de Llama"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Flamebreath
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pocketful of combustible powder is ignited, creating a cone of flame with "
"ashes that stick to those in its path."
msgstr ""
"Un paquete lleno de polvo combustible se enciende, creando un cono de fuego "
"con cenizas que se pegan a los que se encuentran a su paso."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Caustic Aura"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Caustic Aura"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Aura Cáustica"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Aura Cáustica"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Caustic Aura
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Animate a layer of acid around you, burning attackers and increasing your "
"melee damage."
msgstr ""
"Anima una capa de ácido a tu alrededor, quemando a los atacantes e "
"incrementando tu daño en el combate cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Decaying Boneclub"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Decaying Boneclub"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Garrote de Hueso Pútrido"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Garrote de Hueso Pútrido"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Decaying Boneclub
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Link your live blood to dead blood and bones, creating a club eager to "
"harvest the living."
msgstr ""
"Vincula tu sangre viva con la sangre y los huesos muertos, creando un "
"garrote ansioso por cosechar a los vivos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Impact Sling"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Impact Sling"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Honda de Impacto"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Honda de Impacto"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Impact Sling
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Infuse a sling with excess energy, delivering devastating throws before it "
"tears itself apart."
msgstr ""
"Infunde una honda con un exceso de energía, entregando lanzamientos "
"devastadores antes de que se rompa en partes."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Knifeshot"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Knifeshot"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tiro Cuchillo"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tiro Cuchillo"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Knifeshot
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Emulate a railgun, launching a knife at high speed."
msgstr "Emula una cañón de riel, lanzando un cuchillo a alta velocidad."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "MICE(R) blueprint"
msgid_plural "MICE(R) blueprints"
msgstr[0] "esquema MICE(R)"
msgstr[1] "esquemas MICE(R)"

#. ~ Description for MICE(R) blueprint
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Manafied Infernal Combustion Engine (Rideable)\n"
"Detailed schematics for a motorcycle, that are somehow simultaneously obviously impossible and yet intriguingly intuitive.\n"
"In one margin, the word 'Mojocycle' has been scrawled in a flowing hand."
msgstr ""
"Motor de Combustión Infernal Manificado (Manejable)\n"
"Esquemas detallados para una motocicleta, que de alguna manera obviamente es simultáneamente imposible y sin embargo intrigantemente intuitiva.\n"
"En un margen, la palabra \"Mojocicleta\" ha sido garabateada en una mano fluida."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Nova Flare"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Nova Flare"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Nova de Llamas"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Nova de Llamas"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Nova Flare
#. ~ Description for Nova Flare
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid "Causes an intense heat at the location, greatly damaging the target."
msgstr ""
"Provoca un intenso calor en el lugar, dañando enormemente al objetivo."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Jar of Force"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Jar of Force"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Tarro de la Fuerza"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Tarro de la Fuerza"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Jar of Force
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Summon a jar of force you can use to store liquids in."
msgstr ""
"Invoca un tarro de fuerza que puedas utilizar para almacenar líquidos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of freezing touch"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of freezing touch"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Toque Congelante"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Toque Congelante"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of freezing touch
#. ~ Description for Freezing Touch
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py lang/json/SPELL_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Your hands freeze anything they touch at temperatures so cold it slows down "
"your foes."
msgstr ""
"Tus manos congelan todo lo que tocan a temperaturas tan frías que ralentizan"
" a tus enemigos."

#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid "Scroll of Nature's Commune"
msgid_plural "Scrolls of Nature's Commune"
msgstr[0] "Pergamino de Comunión con la Naturaleza"
msgstr[1] "Pergaminos de Comunión con la Naturaleza"

#. ~ Description for Scroll of Nature's Commune
#: lang/json/BOOK_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Your connection with nature allows you to become one with it; you revitalize"
" your body while in communion with the flora and fauna around you."
msgstr ""
"Tu conexión con la naturaleza te permite ser uno con ella; revitalizas tu "
