"This spoon is covered in cartoon dogs and a logo that reads 'Paw Patrol'."
msgstr ""
"Esta cuchara está cubierta de perros de dibujos animados y un logo que dice "
"\"Patrulla Canina\"."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "There is a cute cartoon bear on the handle of this spoon."
msgstr "Hay un lindo oso de caricatura en el mango de esta cuchara."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "There are cartoon cats all over this spoon."
msgstr "Hay gatos de dibujos animados por toda la cuchara."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This spoon has a silhouette of a giraffe going down the handle."
msgstr "Esta cuchara tiene la silueta de una jirafa bajando por el mango."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "butter knife"
msgid_plural "butter knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo para mantequilla"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos para mantequilla"

#. ~ Description for butter knife
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A dull knife, absolutely worthless in combat.  Excellent for spreading soft "
"things on bread."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo sin filo, absolutamente inútil en combate. Excelente para untar "
"cosas blandas en el pan."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "plastic knife"
msgid_plural "plastic knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de plástico"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de plástico"

#. ~ Description for plastic knife
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A plastic butter knife.  It's actually a bit sharper than its metal "
"counterpart, but that doesn't make it any more effective as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de mantequilla de plástico. Es un poco más afilado que el de "
"metal, pero eso no lo hace más efectivo como arma."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "plastic straw"
msgid_plural "plastic straws"
msgstr[0] "pajita de plástico"
msgstr[1] "pajitas de plástico"

#. ~ Description for plastic straw
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A plastic straw, for drinking things and making litter"
msgstr "Una pajilla de plástico, para beber y hacer basura."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "corkscrew"
msgid_plural "corkscrews"
msgstr[0] "sacacorchos"
msgstr[1] "sacacorchos"

#. ~ Description for corkscrew
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Many a pleasant date has been ruined by forgetting this important tool."
msgstr ""
"Muchas citas agradables se han arruinado al olvidar esta importante "
"herramienta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "vegetable peeler"
msgid_plural "vegetable peelers"
msgstr[0] "pelador de vegetales"
msgstr[1] "peladores de vegetales"

#. ~ Description for vegetable peeler
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a simple tool for peeling the outer skin off fruit and veggies "
"without stabbing yourself."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta sencilla para pelar la piel exterior de las frutas y "
"verduras sin apuñalarse."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bottle opener"
msgid_plural "bottle openers"
msgstr[0] "abridor de botellas"
msgstr[1] "abridores de botellas"

#. ~ Description for bottle opener
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A simple lever for popping open bottles."
msgstr "Una simple palanca para abrir botellas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This bottle opener is shaped like a zombie head, the mouth pops open the "
"bottle."
msgstr ""
"Este abridor de botellas tiene la forma de una cabeza de zombi, la boca abre"
" la botella."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This bottle opener is shaped like a lightsaber."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas tiene la forma de un sable láser."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This bottle opener is shaped like a revolver."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas tiene forma de revólver."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This bottle opener is engraved with the words 'I'll die before I give you my"
" beer'."
msgstr ""
"Este abridor está grabado con las palabras \"Moriré antes de darte mi "
"cerveza\"."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This bottle opener is emblazoned with a logo for an HVAC contracting "
"company."
msgstr ""
"Este abridor de botellas tiene el logo de una empresa contratante de HVAC."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This bottle opener reads 'Corporate Team Building Exercise 1999'."
msgstr ""
"Este abridor de botellas dice: \"Ejercicio de construcción de equipo "
"corporativo 1999\"."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This bottle opener reads 'I'd rather be drinking whiskey'."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas dice: \"Preferiría estar bebiendo whisky\"."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This bottle opener is shaped like a phaser."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas tiene la forma de un fáser."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This novelty bottle opener is designed to look like a hobo clown."
msgstr ""
"Este novedoso abridor de botellas está diseñado para parecerse a un payaso "
"vagabundo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "spork"
msgid_plural "sporks"
msgstr[0] "cuchador"
msgstr[1] "cuchadores"

#. ~ Description for spork
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The bastardized hybrid of a spoon and fork, with all the power and "
"capabilities of both in a more annoying to use package."
msgstr ""
"El híbrido bastardo de una cuchara y un tenedor, con todo el poder y las "
"capacidades de ambos en un paquete más molesto de usar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "foon"
msgid_plural "foons"
msgstr[0] "tenuchara"
msgstr[1] "tenucharas"

#. ~ Description for foon
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Clearly the superior instrument.  Sporks are just imitators."
msgstr ""
"Obviamente, el mejor instrumento. Los cuchadores son tristes imitaciones."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "chopsticks"
msgid_plural "pairs of chopsticks"
msgstr[0] "par de palitos chinos"
msgstr[1] "pares de palitos chinos"

#. ~ Description for chopsticks
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"One of the most popular eating utensils in the world.  Does double duty as a"
" way of dealing with especially fragile vampires."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los utensilios para comer más populares del mundo. Hace doble turno "
"como una forma de tratar con vampiros especialmente frágiles."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ladle"
msgid_plural "ladles"
msgstr[0] "cucharón"
msgstr[1] "cucharones"

#. ~ Description for ladle
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "When you need to scoop some soup, this is the utensil for you."
msgstr "Cuando necesites servir sopa, este es el utensilio para ti."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "whisk"
msgid_plural "whisks"
msgstr[0] "batidora"
msgstr[1] "batidoras"

#. ~ Description for whisk
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Also known as a 'wire whip', this is a less effective weapon than it sounds."
msgstr ""
"También conocido como \"látigo de alambre\", es un arma menos efectiva de lo"
" que parece."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "potato masher"
msgid_plural "potato mashers"
msgstr[0] "machacador de patatas"
msgstr[1] "machacadores de patatas"

#. ~ Description for potato masher
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This tool can mash potatoes and soft root vegetables; it cannot do the "
"twist."
msgstr ""
"Esta herramienta puede hacer puré de papas y vegetales de raíz suave; no "
"puede hacer el giro."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "garlic press"
msgid_plural "garlic presses"
msgstr[0] "prensa de ajo"
msgstr[1] "prensas de ajo"

#. ~ Description for garlic press
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This tool can squash a clove or two of garlic into a fine paste."
msgstr ""
"Esta herramienta puede aplastar uno o dos dientes de ajo en una fina pasta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "can opener"
msgid_plural "can openers"
msgstr[0] "abridor de latas"
msgstr[1] "abridores de latas"

#. ~ Description for can opener
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "It's not hard to open cans without this, but it's way messier."
msgstr "No es difícil abrir latas sin esto, pero es mucho más complicado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "carving fork"
msgid_plural "carving forks"
msgstr[0] "tenedor de trinchar"
msgstr[1] "tenedores de trinchar"

#. ~ Description for carving fork
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"It's like a tiny pitchfork, or a very large dinner fork.  You use it to hold"
" meat still while you slice it."
msgstr ""
"Es como una pequeña horquilla, o un gran tenedor para la cena. Lo usas para "
"mantener la carne quieta mientras la cortas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "spatula"
msgid_plural "spatulas"
msgstr[0] "espátula"
msgstr[1] "espátulas"

#. ~ Description for spatula
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A rubber scraper for making sure you get every last scrap of cookie dough."
msgstr ""
"Un raspador de goma para asegurarte de que recibes hasta el último resto de "
"masa de galletas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "rolling pin"
msgid_plural "rolling pins"
msgstr[0] "rodillo de cocina"
msgstr[1] "rodillos de cocina"

#. ~ Description for rolling pin
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout piece of hardwood, turned and sanded smooth, with rounded handles at"
" the ends.  This timeless kitchen tool also doubles as a very effective "
"club."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza robusta de madera dura, torneada y lijada suavemente, con mangos "
"redondeados en los extremos. Este intemporal utensilio de cocina también es "
"un garrote muy efectivo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pot"
msgid_plural "pots"
msgstr[0] "olla"
msgstr[1] "ollas"

#. ~ Description for pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Useful for boiling water when cooking spaghetti and more."
msgstr "Útil para hervir agua cuando se cocinan espaghetis y otras cosas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cast-iron pot"
msgid_plural "cast-iron pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de hierro fundido"
msgstr[1] "ollas de hierro fundido"

#. ~ Description for cast-iron pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hefty black pot is made from cast iron and coated in a sturdy enamel."
msgstr ""
"Esta pesada olla negra está hecha de hierro fundido y recubierta de un "
"robusto esmalte."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "copper pot"
msgid_plural "copper pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de cobre"
msgstr[1] "ollas de cobre"

#. ~ Description for copper pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Useful for boiling water when cooking spaghetti and more.  Made from copper,"
" with a lining of tin to prevent metal from leaching into acidic foods."
msgstr ""
"Útil para hervir agua cuando cocinas fideos y otras cosas. Está hecha de "
"cobre, con un revestimiento de estaño para prevenir que el metal se filtre "
"en las comidas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "casserole"
msgid_plural "casseroles"
msgstr[0] "cazuela"
msgstr[1] "cazuelas"

#. ~ Description for casserole
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A ceramic pot made for both cooking and serving, particularly one-pot "
"dinners."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de cerámica hecha tanto para cocinar como para servir, "
"especialmente para cenas de una sola olla."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "stock pot"
msgid_plural "stock pots"
msgstr[0] "marmita"
msgstr[1] "marmitas"

#. ~ Description for stock pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large pot for making soup stocks.  You could fit a whole turkey in there, "
"with a bit of shoving."
msgstr ""
"Una gran olla para hacer caldos. Podrías meter un pavo entero ahí, con un "
"poco de empuje."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "canning pot"
msgid_plural "canning pots"
msgstr[0] "bote de conserva"
msgstr[1] "botes de conserva"

#. ~ Description for canning pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A very large 25 liter pot, primarily meant for canning food in glass jars "
"via the water bath method, though it can cook normal foods just as well.  "
"Canning foods with it will require a lot of water.  If you're only canning a"
" couple of jars at a time, you'd fill it up with rocks or something to "
"displace the water above the lids."
msgstr ""
"Una olla muy grande de 25 litros, destinada principalmente a enlatar "
"alimentos en tarros de cristal mediante el método de baño de agua, aunque "
"también puede cocinar alimentos normales. El enlatado de alimentos con ella "
"requerirá mucha agua. Si sólo se enlatan un par de frascos a la vez, se "
"llenaría con piedras o algo para desplazar el agua por encima de las tapas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cast-iron frying pan"
msgid_plural "cast-iron frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de hierro fundido"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de hierro fundido"

#. ~ Description for cast-iron frying pan
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cast-iron pan.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de hierro fundido. Sirve como arma de cuerpo a cuerpo, y es útil "
"para cocinar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "steel frying pan"
msgid_plural "steel frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de acero"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de acero"

#. ~ Description for steel frying pan
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A steel frying pan.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una sartén de acero. Es un arma cuerpo a cuerpo decente y se usa para "
"cocinar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "copper frying pan"
msgid_plural "copper frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de cobre"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de cobre"

#. ~ Description for copper frying pan
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A copper frying pan, coated in a thin layer of tin.  Makes a decent melee "
"weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una sartén de cobre, recubierta con una fina capa de estaño. Es un arma "
"cuerpo a cuerpo decente y se usa para cocinar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift pot"
msgid_plural "makeshift pots"
msgstr[0] "olla improvisada"
msgstr[1] "ollas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description for makeshift pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sheet of metal crudely hammered into a cooking pot.  Good enough to cook "
"food and boil water, but not as useful as proper cookware."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de metal burdamente martillada para darle forma de olla. Es "
"suficiente para cocinar comida y hervir agua, pero no tan útil como un "
"utensilio adecuado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift copper pot"
msgid_plural "makeshift copper pots"
msgstr[0] "olla improvisada de cobre"
msgstr[1] "ollas improvisadas de cobre"

#. ~ Description for makeshift copper pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cooking pot crudely hammered out of copper.  Good enough to cook food and "
"boil water, but not as useful as proper cookware."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de cocina burdamente martillada a partir de cobre. Suficiente para "
"cocinar comida y hervir agua, pero no tan útil como un utensilio de cocina "
"adecuado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "kettle"
msgid_plural "kettles"
msgstr[0] "tetera"
msgstr[1] "teteras"

#. ~ Description for kettle
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stovetop kettle for boiling water."
msgstr "Una tetera para hervir agua."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "mesh colander"
msgid_plural "mesh colanders"
msgstr[0] "colador de malla"
msgstr[1] "coladores de malla"

#. ~ Description for mesh colander
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stainless steel mesh colander, for washing rice, vegetables or straining "
"liquid off from noodles or other foods."
msgstr ""
"Un colador de malla de acero inoxidable, para lavar el arroz, las verduras o"
" colar el líquido de los fideos u otros alimentos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "splatter guard"
msgid_plural "splatter guards"
msgstr[0] "protector contra salpicaduras"
msgstr[1] "protectores contra salpicaduras"

#. ~ Description for splatter guard
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stainless steel mesh screen for preventing flying oil from getting all "
"over your nice counters (or you) when frying."
msgstr ""
"Una pantalla de malla de acero inoxidable para evitar que el aceite volador "
"se desparrame sobre sus bonitos mostradores (o sobre usted) cuando se fríe."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cutting board"
msgid_plural "cutting boards"
msgstr[0] "tabla para cortar"
msgstr[1] "tablas para cortar"

#. ~ Description for cutting board
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large flat piece of wood for chopping vegetables on without ruining your "
"knife or your countertop."
msgstr ""
"Un gran trozo plano de madera para cortar verduras sin arruinar el cuchillo "
"o la encimera."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "meal tray"
msgid_plural "meal trays"
msgstr[0] "bandeja de comida"
msgstr[1] "bandejas de comida"

#. ~ Description for meal tray
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stainless steel tray used for serving food in cafeterias, mess halls, or "
"similar places."
msgstr ""
"Una bandeja de acero inoxidable usada para servir comida en cafeterías, "
"comedores o lugares similares."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pizza cutter"
msgid_plural "pizza cutters"
msgstr[0] "cortador de pizza"
msgstr[1] "cortadores de pizza"

#. ~ Description for pizza cutter
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A utensil used for cutting pizza.  Practically useless in combat."
msgstr ""
"Un utensilio usado para cortar la pizza. Prácticamente inútil en combate."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "icecream scoop"
msgid_plural "icecream scoops"
msgstr[0] "cuchara de helado"
msgstr[1] "cucharas de helado"

#. ~ Description for icecream scoop
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A utensil used for scooping icecream into bowls.  It has a spring powered "
"lever to assist."
msgstr ""
"Un utensilio usado para servir helado en tazones. Tiene una palanca "
"accionada por resorte para ayudar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cheese grater"
msgid_plural "cheese graters"
msgstr[0] "rayador de queso"
msgstr[1] "rayadores de queso"

#. ~ Description for cheese grater
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stainless steel cheese grater with a plastic grip.  It is used to shred "
"cheese."
msgstr ""
"Un rallador de queso de acero inoxidable con mango de plástico. Se utiliza "
"para rallar queso."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "XLR cable"
msgid_plural "XLR cables"
msgstr[0] "cable XLR"
msgstr[1] "cables XLR"

#. ~ Description for XLR cable
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A balanced cable used for sending audio signal.  The connectors have three "
"prongs."
msgstr ""
"Un cable balanceado usado para enviar la señal de audio. Los conectores "
"tienen tres puntas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "speaker cable"
msgid_plural "speaker cables"
msgstr[0] "cable de altavoz"
msgstr[1] "cables de altavoz"

#. ~ Description for speaker cable
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This audio cable connects one speaker to a powered head, or one speaker to "
"another."
msgstr ""
"Este cable de audio conecta un altavoz a un cabezal motorizado, o un altavoz"
" a otro."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "instrument cable"
msgid_plural "instrument cables"
msgstr[0] "cable de instrumento"
msgstr[1] "cables de instrumentos"

#. ~ Description for instrument cable
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Known as an instrument cable because it is usually used to connect a guitar "
"to a powered amp, it is an unbalanced cable with 1/4\" male connectors on "
"each side."
msgstr ""
"Conocido como un cable para instrumentos porque se usa normalmente para "
"conectar una guitarra a un amplificador alimentado, es un cable "
"desbalanceado con conectores macho de 1/4 de pulgada a cada lado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "headphones"
msgid_plural "headphones"
msgstr[0] "auricular"
msgstr[1] "auriculares"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'headphones'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Typical headphones that cover your ears.  A well-known brand that is very "
"high quality, with a detachable 1/8\" cable.  Comes with a 1/8\" to 1/4\" "
"adaptor."
msgstr ""
"Típicos auriculares que cubren los oídos. Una marca conocida de muy alta "
"calidad, con un cable desmontable de 1/8\". Viene con un adaptador de 1/8\" "
"a 1/4\"."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "XLR microphone"
msgid_plural "XLR microphones"
msgstr[0] "micrófono XLR"
msgstr[1] "micrófonos XLR"

#. ~ Description for XLR microphone
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A typical microphone used to record or amplify voice.  Comes with a clip.  "
"Has a 3-pin XLR connector on the bottom in order to connect to an amp."
msgstr ""
"Un típico micrófono usado para grabar o amplificar la voz. Viene con un "
"clip. Tiene un conector XLR de 3 pines en la parte inferior para conectar a "
"un amplificador."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "microphone stand"
msgid_plural "microphone stands"
msgstr[0] "soporte de micrófono"
msgstr[1] "soportes de micrófono"

#. ~ Description for microphone stand
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight telescoping boom stand made of aluminum and painted black.  "
"About 6' tall when full extended, or 3' when closed fully.  Has threads for "
"a mic clip on one end."
msgstr ""
"Un soporte telescópico ligero de aluminio pintado de negro. Alrededor de 6 "
"pies de altura cuando está completamente extendido, o 3 pies cuando está "
"completamente cerrado. Tiene hilos para un clip de micrófono en un extremo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "guitar stand"
msgid_plural "guitar stands"
msgstr[0] "soporte de guitarra"
msgstr[1] "soportes de guitarra"

#. ~ Description for guitar stand
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small, oddly shaped piece of aluminum hardware with three legs.  When "
"placed on the ground, this can support one guitar in an upright position."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña y extraña pieza de aluminio con tres patas. Cuando se coloca en "
"el suelo, puede soportar una guitarra en posición vertical."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "plectrum"
msgid_plural "plectra"
msgstr[0] "plectro"
msgstr[1] "plectros"

#. ~ Description for plectrum
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A flat piece of plastic with a pointed tip, designed for plucking the "
"strings of a guitar or mandolin."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza plana de plástico con una punta afilada, diseñada para tocar las "
"cuerdas de una guitarra o mandolina."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "mixer"
msgid_plural "mixers"
msgstr[0] "mezcladora"
msgstr[1] "mezcladoras"

#. ~ Description for mixer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A device with faders, switches, and knobs that mixes input signal and sends "
"it to two output XLR cables.  (left and right)"
msgstr ""
"Un dispositivo con controles de nivel, interruptores y perillas que mezcla "
"la señal de entrada y la envía a dos cables XLR de salida. (izquierda y "
"derecha)"

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "spare parts"
msgid_plural "spare parts"
msgstr[0] "pieza de repuesto"
msgstr[1] "piezas de repuesto"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'spare parts'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Items with are not themselves useful but are instead requirements for "
"crafting or repairs"
msgstr ""
"Son objetos que no son útiles así sueltos pero pueden ser necesarios para "
"algunas fabricaciones o reparaciones."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "drive belt"
msgid_plural "drive belts"
msgstr[0] "correa de transmisión"
msgstr[1] "correas de transmisión"

#. ~ Description for drive belt
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A synthetic rubber V-belt with steel reinforcement fibers commonly fitted to"
" engines or other industrial equipment."
msgstr ""
"Es una cinta de goma sintética en V con fibras de acero reforzado que se "
"utiliza normalmente en motores u otros equipos industriales."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift drive belt"
msgid_plural "makeshift drive belts"
msgstr[0] "correa improvisada de transmisión"
msgstr[1] "correas improvisadas de transmisión"

#. ~ Description for makeshift drive belt
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An improvised belt useful for repairing engines or other industrial "
"equipment when no better alternative is available."
msgstr ""
"Es una correa improvisada que sirve para arreglar motores u otros equipos "
"industriales cuando no encuentras una mejor alternativa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "air filter"
msgid_plural "air filters"
msgstr[0] "filtro de aire"
msgstr[1] "filtros de aire"

#. ~ Description for air filter
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A plastic box containing creped paper used to filter the air supply for "
"combustion engines or other industrial equipment."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de plástico que contiene papel arrugado utilizado para filtrar el "
"suministro de aire de los motores de combustión u otros equipos "
"industriales."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift air filter"
msgid_plural "makeshift air filters"
msgstr[0] "filtro de aire improvisado"
msgstr[1] "filtros de aire improvisados"

#. ~ Description for makeshift air filter
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An improvised air filter useful for repairing engines or other industrial "
"equipment when no better alternative is available."
msgstr ""
"Es un filtro de aire improvisado que sirve para arreglar motores u otros "
"equipos industriales cuando no encuentras una mejor alternativa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "automotive filter"
msgid_plural "automotive filters"
msgstr[0] "filtro automotor"
msgstr[1] "filtros automotores"

#. ~ Description for automotive filter
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A steel can containing filter paper designed for automotive use."
msgstr ""
"Es una lata de acero que tiene papel de filtro diseñado para utilizar en "
"automotores."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift automotive filter"
msgid_plural "makeshift automotive filters"
msgstr[0] "filtro automotor improvisado"
msgstr[1] "filtros automotores improvisados"

#. ~ Description for makeshift automotive filter
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An improvised automotive filter useful for repairing engines or other "
"industrial equipment when no better alternative is available."
msgstr ""
"Es un filtro automotor improvisado que sirve para arreglar motores u otros "
"equipos industriales cuando no encuentras una mejor alternativa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "glow plug"
msgid_plural "glow plugs"
msgstr[0] "bujía de precalentamiento"
msgstr[1] "bujías de precalentamiento"

#. ~ Description for glow plug
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cylindrical heating device designed to be screwed in to a diesel engine to"
" aid starting in cold weather."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo cilíndrico de calentamiento diseñado para ser atornillado "
"en un motor diésel para ayudar el arranque bajo climas fríos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "high-pressure pump"
msgid_plural "high-pressure pumps"
msgstr[0] "bomba de alta presión"
msgstr[1] "bombas de alta presión"

#. ~ Description for high-pressure pump
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A complex mechanical pump capable of achieving high pressures.  Far beyond "
"anything you could reasonably improvise."
msgstr ""
"Una compleja bomba mecánica capaz de alcanzar presiones altas. Mucho más "
"allá de lo que se podría razonablemente improvisar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "mechanical pump"
msgid_plural "mechanical pumps"
msgstr[0] "bomba mecánica"
msgstr[1] "bombas mecánicos"

#. ~ Description for mechanical pump
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A simple cast iron mechanical impeller pump.  It's not good for much of "
"anything on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un simple surtidor mecánico de hierro fundido. No sirve para nada por sí "
"solo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "set of pipe fittings"
msgid_plural "sets of pipe fittings"
msgstr[0] "conjunto de encajes de tuberias"
msgstr[1] "conjuntos de encajes de tuberias"

#. ~ Description for set of pipe fittings
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A loose assortment of metal pipe fittings - end caps, pipe junctions, and "
"similar items.  They can be used in a variety of projects."
msgstr ""
"Un surtido suelto de accesorios de tuberías de metal - tapas finales, "
"uniones de tuberías y artículos similares. Pueden ser usados en una variedad"
" de proyectos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short cordage piece"
msgid_plural "short cordage pieces"
msgstr[0] "cordaje corto"
msgstr[1] "cordajes cortos"

#. ~ Description for short cordage piece
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 6-inch (or about 15 cm) long piece of natural cordage.  Useful for some "
"purposes, but not as strong or flexible as proper string."
msgstr ""
"Un cordaje natural de 6 pulgadas (sobre 15 cm) de largo. Útil para algunos "
"propósitos, pero no tan fuerte o flexible como una cuerda."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long cordage piece"
msgid_plural "long cordage pieces"
msgstr[0] "cordaje largo"
msgstr[1] "cordajes largos"

#. ~ Description for long cordage piece
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 3-foot (or about 90 cm) long piece of natural cordage.  Useful for some "
"purposes, but not as strong or flexible as proper string."
msgstr ""
"Un cordaje natural de 3 pies (sobre 90 cm) de largo. Útil para algunos "
"propósitos, pero no tan fuerte o flexible como una cuerda."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short string"
msgid_plural "short strings"
msgstr[0] "cuerda corta"
msgstr[1] "cuerdas cortas"

#. ~ Description for short string
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A 6-inch (or about 15 cm) long piece of cotton string."
msgstr "Una cuerda de algodón de 6 pulgadas (sobre 15 cm) de largo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long string"
msgid_plural "long strings"
msgstr[0] "cuerda larga"
msgstr[1] "cuerdas largas"

#. ~ Description for long string
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A 3-foot (or about 90 cm) long piece of cotton string."
msgstr "Una cuerda de algodón de 3 pies (sobre 90 cm) de largo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short rope"
msgid_plural "short ropes"
msgstr[0] "soga corta"
msgstr[1] "sogas cortas"

#. ~ Use action holster_msg for short rope.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid "You use an elaborate knot to tie your %s to your %s"
msgstr "Usas un nudo elaborado para atar tu %s a tu  %s"

#. ~ Use action holster_prompt for short rope.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Tie what to the rope?"
msgstr " ¿Qué atar a la soga?"

#. ~ Description for short rope
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 6-foot (or about 180 cm) long piece of rope.  Wear it over a shoulder and "
"tie items to it as a temporary carrying solution."
msgstr ""
"Un soga de 6 pies (sobre 180 cm) de largo. Llévala sobre un hombro y ata "
"objetos a ella como una solución de transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long rope"
msgid_plural "long ropes"
msgstr[0] "soga larga"
msgstr[1] "sogas largas"

#. ~ Description for long rope
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 30-foot (or about 9 m) long rope.  Useful for keeping yourself safe from "
"falls.  Wear it over a shoulder and tie items to it as a temporary carrying "
"solution."
msgstr ""
"Una soga de 30 pies (sobre 9 m) de largo. Útil para mantenerte a salvo de "
"caídas. Llévala sobre un hombro y ata objetos a ella como solución de "
"transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short vine"
msgid_plural "short vines"
msgstr[0] "enredadera corta"
msgstr[1] "enredaderas cortas"

#. ~ Description for short vine
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sturdy 6-foot (or about 180 cm) long vine.  Wear it over a shoulder and "
"tie items to it as a temporary carrying solution."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta enredadera de 6 pies (sobre 180 cm) de largo. Llévala sobre un "
"hombro y ata objetos a ella como solución de transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long vine"
msgid_plural "long vines"
msgstr[0] "enredadera larga"
msgstr[1] "enredaderas largas"

#. ~ Description for long vine
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sturdy 30-foot (or about 9 m) long vine.  Could easily be used as a rope."
"  Strong enough to suspend a large corpse for butchering.  Wear it over a "
"shoulder and tie items to it as a temporary carrying solution."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta enredadera de 6 pies (sobre 180 cm) de largo. Podría usarse "
"fácilmente como soga. Lo suficientemente fuerte como para suspender un gran "
"cadáver para su descuartizamiento. Llévala sobre un hombro y ata objetos a "
"ella como solución de transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short cordage rope"
msgid_plural "short cordage ropes"
msgstr[0] "soga de cordajes cortos"
msgstr[1] "sogas de cordajes cortos"

#. ~ Description for short cordage rope
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 6-foot (or about 180 cm) long piece of rough rope, woven from natural "
"cordage.  Useful for some purposes, but not as strong or flexible as proper "
"rope.  Wear it over a shoulder and tie items to it as a temporary carrying "
"solution."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo de soga áspera de 6 pies (o unos 180 cm) de largo, tejida con "
"cordajes naturales. Útil para algunos propósitos, pero no tan fuerte o "
"flexible como una soga apropiada. Llévalo sobre un hombro y ata objetos a "
"ella como solución de transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long cordage rope"
msgid_plural "long cordage ropes"
msgstr[0] "soga de cordajes largos"
msgstr[1] "sogas de cordajes largos"

#. ~ Description for long cordage rope
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 30-foot (or about 9 m) long rough rope, woven from natural cordage.  Not "
"strong enough to hold up to falls, but still useful for some things, such as"
" suspending large corpses for butchering.  Wear it over a shoulder and tie "
"items to it as a temporary carrying solution."
msgstr ""
"Una soga áspera de 30 pies (o unos 9 m) de largo, tejida con cordajes "
"naturales. No es lo suficientemente fuerte para soportar caídas, pero aún "
"así es útil para algunas cosas, como suspender grandes cadáveres para su "
"carnicería. Llévalo sobre un hombro y ata objetos a ella como solución de "
"transporte temporal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "badminton shuttlecock"
msgid_plural "shuttlecocks"
msgstr[0] "volante de badminton"
msgstr[1] "volantes de badminton"

#. ~ Description for badminton shuttlecock
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A high-drag projectile used in the sport of badminton."
msgstr "Un proyectil de alta resistencia usado en el deporte del bádminton."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "golf tee"
msgid_plural "golf tees"
msgstr[0] "tee"
msgstr[1] "tees"

#. ~ Description for golf tee
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pin shaped piece of wood meant for holding a golf ball slightly off the "
"ground."
msgstr ""
"Un pieza de madera con forma de alfiler, que se usa para sostener una pelota"
" de golf levantada del suelo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "golf ball"
msgid_plural "golf balls"
msgstr[0] "bola de golf"
msgstr[1] "bolas de golf"

#. ~ Description for golf ball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A small ball with round indentations on it."
msgstr "Una pequeña bola con hollitos redondos en su superficie."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pool ball"
msgid_plural "pool balls"
msgstr[0] "bola de billar"
msgstr[1] "bolas de billar"

#. ~ Description for pool ball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A colorful, hard ball.  Essentially a rock."
msgstr "Una bola dura, colorida. Es casi una piedra."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bowling ball"
msgid_plural "bowling balls"
msgstr[0] "bola de bolos"
msgstr[1] "bolas de bolos"

#. ~ Description for bowling ball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large, heavy ball.  Before the apocalypse, its main purpose was to be "
"rolled along waxed floors."
msgstr ""
"Una bola grande y pesada. Antes del cataclismo, su principal propósito era "
"rodar por pisos encerados."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "baseball"
msgid_plural "baseballs"
msgstr[0] "pelota de béisbol"
msgstr[1] "pelotas de béisbol"

#. ~ Description for baseball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A baseball, good for throwing at enemies.  Getting hit with one of these "
"hurts a lot more than you might think."
msgstr ""
"Una pelota de béisbol, sirve para tirarle a los enemigos. Si te pegan con "
"una de estas, te va a doler mucho más de lo que te imaginás."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "football"
msgid_plural "footballs"
msgstr[0] "pelota de fútbol americano"
msgstr[1] "pelotas de fútbol americano"

#. ~ Description for football
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An oval made of leather and string, it's easily thrown but does little "
"damage.  You could take it apart into leather if you wanted."
msgstr ""
"Un óvalo hecho de cuero y cuerda, fácil de lanzar pero hace poco daño. La "
"puedes desmontar para recuperar el cuero, si lo necesitas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "basketball"
msgid_plural "basketballs"
msgstr[0] "balón de baloncesto"
msgstr[1] "balones de baloncesto"

#. ~ Description for basketball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A high-quality indoor basketball.  You may throw it at zombies."
msgstr ""
"Un balón de baloncesto de alta calidad. Se la puedes lanzar a los zombis."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "volleyball"
msgid_plural "volleyballs"
msgstr[0] "pelota de volleyball"
msgstr[1] "pelotas de volleyball"

#. ~ Description for volleyball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A standard regulation volleyball."
msgstr "Una pelota de volleyball de regulación estándar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "beach volleyball"
msgid_plural "volleyballs"
msgstr[0] "pelota de volleyball playa"
msgstr[1] "pelotas de volleyball playa"

#. ~ Description for beach volleyball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A brightly colored beach volleyball.  It is slightly larger than a regular "
"white one."
msgstr ""
"Una colorida pelota de volleyball playa. Es ligeramente más grande que una "
"pelota de volleyball blanca normal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "hockey puck"
msgid_plural "hockey pucks"
msgstr[0] "disco de hockey"
msgstr[1] "discos de hockey"

#. ~ Description for hockey puck
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A heavy circular block of solid rubber, normally used for playing hockey.  "
"You can throw it to cause some serious harm."
msgstr ""
"Es un disco pesado de goma sólida, normalmente utilizado para jugar al "
"hockey sobre hielo. Se lo puedes lanzar a un enemigo para causar daño "
"bastante serio."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift bayonet"
msgid_plural "makeshift bayonets"
msgstr[0] "bayoneta improvisada"
msgstr[1] "bayonetas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description for makeshift bayonet
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A makeshift version of a bayonet that consists of a mere spike with some "
"string."
msgstr ""
"Una versión improvisada de una bayoneta que consiste en una mera punta con "
"alguna cadena."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "war flail"
msgid_plural "war flails"
msgstr[0] "mayal de guerra"
msgstr[1] "mayales de guerra"

#. ~ Description for war flail
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a stout pole with a large steel flanged mace head on a short chain "
"attached to it, based on the peasant flail agricultural tool except now with"
" a metal head and made to thresh people in metal armor rather than grain."
msgstr ""
"Este es un poste robusto con una gran cabeza de maza con bridas de acero en "
"una cadena corta unida a él, basado en la herramienta agrícola de azotador "
"campesino excepto ahora con una cabeza de metal y hecho para trillar a la "
"gente con armadura de metal en lugar de grano."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "peasant flail"
msgid_plural "peasant flails"
msgstr[0] "mayal de arma"
msgstr[1] "mayal de armas"

#. ~ Description for peasant flail
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a stout pole with a wooden club on a leather cord attached to it, "
"this is a tool used to thresh wheat and occasionally people when the "
"peasants got angry at their feudal lords."
msgstr ""
"Este es un poste robusto con un palo de madera sobre un cordón de cuero "
"unido a él, esta es una herramienta utilizada para trillar el trigo y "
"ocasionalmente a la gente cuando los campesinos se enfadaban con sus señores"
" feudales."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "baseball bat"
msgid_plural "baseball bats"
msgstr[0] "bate de béisbol"
msgstr[1] "bates de béisbol"

#. ~ Description for baseball bat
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A sturdy wood bat.  Makes a great melee weapon."
msgstr "Un robusto bate de madera. Es muy buena arma para el cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "aluminum bat"
msgid_plural "aluminum bats"
msgstr[0] "bate de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "bates de aluminio"

#. ~ Description for aluminum bat
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An aluminum baseball bat, lighter than a wooden bat and a little easier to "
"swing as a result."
msgstr ""
"Un bate de béisbol de aluminio, más ligero que el de madera y un poco más "
"fácil para usar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "foam rubber bat"
msgid_plural "foam rubber bats"
msgstr[0] "murciélago de gomaespuma"
msgstr[1] "murciélagos de gomaespuma"

#. ~ Description for foam rubber bat
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A baseball bat made out of foam rubber with a plastic handle.  Light, well-"
"balanced, and easy to wield, but almost completely ineffective."
msgstr ""
"Un bate de béisbol hecho de goma espuma con un mango de plástico. Ligero, "
"bien equilibrado y fácil de manejar, pero casi completamente ineficaz."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "expandable baton"
msgid_plural "expandable batons"
msgstr[0] "garrote extendible"
msgstr[1] "garrotes extendibles"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for expandable baton.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Expand"
msgstr "Expandir"

#. ~ Use action msg for expandable baton.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "You snap open your baton."
msgstr "Abres bruscamente tu garrote."

#. ~ Description for expandable baton
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton that collapses for easy storage.  Makes an excellent "
"melee weapon.  Activate to expand."
msgstr ""
"Es un garrote telescópico que se cierra sobre sí mismo para ser fácil de "
"guardar. Una excelente arma de cuerpo a cuerpo. Activalo para extenderlo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "expandable baton (extended)"
msgid_plural "expandable batons (extended)"
msgstr[0] "garrote extendible (extendido)"
msgstr[1] "garrotes extendibles (extendidos)"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for expandable baton (extended).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Collapse"
msgstr "Colapsar"

#. ~ Use action msg for expandable baton (extended).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "You collapse your baton."
msgstr "Cierras tu garrote."

#. ~ Description for expandable baton (extended)
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton that collapses for easy storage.  Makes an excellent "
"melee weapon.  Activate to collapse."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón telescópico que se colapsa para facilitar el almacenamiento. Es "
"una excelente arma de combate cuerpo a cuerpo. Activar para colapsar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "battle axe"
msgid_plural "battle axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de guerra"
msgstr[1] "hachas de guerra"

#. ~ Description for battle axe
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply made replica of a massive axe designed for warfare."
msgstr ""
"Es una réplica berreta sin filo de un hacha enorme diseñada para la guerra."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "blackjack"
msgid_plural "blackjacks"
msgstr[0] "blackjack(arma)"
msgstr[1] "blackjacks(armas)"

#. ~ Description for blackjack
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a short, easily concealed bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight "
"embedded at the end of a short leather shaft.  Formerly used by law "
"enforcement, this weapon is meant to stun or knock out the subject, although"
" head strikes have a high risk of causing a permanent, disabling brain "
"injury or being fatal."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma corta y fácil de ocultar que consiste en un peso incrustado "
"en el extremo de un mango corto de cuero. Anteriormente utilizada por las "
"fuerzas del orden, esta arma tiene por objeto aturdir o noquear al sujeto, "
"aunque los golpes en la cabeza tienen un alto riesgo de causar una lesión "
"cerebral permanente e incapacitante o de ser mortales."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bokken"
msgid_plural "bokken"
msgstr[0] "bokken"
msgstr[1] "bokkens"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bokken'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a solid wood 'training' katana, exactingly crafted to mimic the "
"weight and balance of the real thing.  Despite its lack of a sharp metal "
"edge, it's still quite capable of inflicting deadly wounds."
msgstr ""
"Es una katana de madera de entrenamiento, estrictamente fabricada para ser "
"igual en peso y balance a la verdadera. Más allá de su falta de filo de "
"metal, igual es capaz de infligir heridas mortales."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bokken'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a solid wood 'training' katana, but feels far too light to make an "
"effective weapon."
msgstr ""
"Es una buena katana de madera de entrenamiento, pero se siente demasiado "
"liviana como para actuar efectivamente como arma."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bokken'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a solid wood 'training' katana, but it looks to be mass-produced, "
"and not quite as effective as the real deal."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una katana de entrenamiento de madera sólida, pero parece ser "
"producida en masa, y no tan efectiva como la real."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "The 7-10 Split"
msgid_plural "7-10 Splits"
msgstr[0] "The 7-10 Split"
msgstr[1] "7-10 Splits"

#. ~ Description for The 7-10 Split
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An improvised weapon, made from two spikes attached to a bowling pin in the "
"shape of a 'T'."
msgstr ""
"Es una arma improvisada hecha con dos puntas adheridas a un bolo formando "
"una 'T'. Llamado así por los bolos 7 y 10 que son los de las puntas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bowling pin"
msgid_plural "bowling pins"
msgstr[0] "bolo"
msgstr[1] "bolos"

#. ~ Description for bowling pin
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A blunt bowling pin.  Makes a decent melee weapon, if somewhat short."
msgstr ""
"Un romo bolo. Es un arma decente para el cuerpo a cuerpo, aunque un poco "
"corto."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "barbed wire bat"
msgid_plural "barbed wire bats"
msgstr[0] "bate con alambre de púas"
msgstr[1] "bates con alambre de púas"

#. ~ Description for barbed wire bat
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A baseball bat wrapped with barbed wire.  A brutal melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Es un bate de béisbol envuelto con alambre de púas. Un arma brutal para el "
"cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "walking cane"
msgid_plural "walking canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón"
msgstr[1] "bastones"

#. ~ Description for walking cane
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Handicapped or not, you always walk in style.  Consisting of a metal "
"headpiece and a wooden body, this makes a great bashing weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Discapacitado o no, con esto siempre caminas con estilo. Consiste en un "
"cabezal de metal en un cuerpo de madera. Es una arma golpeante muy buena si "
"la necesitas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cudgel"
msgid_plural "cudgels"
msgstr[0] "porra"
msgstr[1] "porras"

#. ~ Description for cudgel
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A slender long rod of wood, while traditionally intended as a training tool "
"for many dueling moves, it still makes a good melee weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo fino y largo de madera, que aunque tradicionalmente se lo ve como"
" una herramienta de entrenamiento, es también una buena arma de cuerpo a "
"cuerpo, de ser necesario."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift macuahuitl"
msgid_plural "makeshift macuahuitls"
msgstr[0] "macuahuitl improvisado"
msgstr[1] "macuahuitl improvisados"

#. ~ Description for makeshift macuahuitl
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A flat wooden club with sharpened pieces of stone sticking to both of its "
"sides."
msgstr ""
"Un garrote plano de madera con fragmentos afilados de piedra sobresaliendo "
"de los dos lados."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "glass shiv"
msgid_plural "glass shivs"
msgstr[0] "navaja carcelaria de cristal"
msgstr[1] "navajas carcelarias de cristal"

#. ~ Description for glass shiv
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A glass shard with wrapping at one end so it can be safely wielded."
msgstr ""
"Un fragmento de cristal con una punta envuelta con un trapo para que pueda "
"ser empuñado fácilmente."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "golf club"
msgid_plural "golf clubs"
msgstr[0] "palo de golf"
msgstr[1] "palos de golf"

#. ~ Description for golf club
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A long handle with a big metal head, flat on one side, for driving golf "
"balls.  Fore!"
msgstr ""
"Un mango largo con un cabezal grande de metal, chato de un lado, hecho para "
"golpear pelotas de golf. ¡Fore!"

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena"
msgstr[1] "almádenas"

#. ~ Description for sledge hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large, heavy hammer.  Makes an acceptable melee weapon for the very "
"strong, but is nearly useless in the hands of the weak."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo grande y pesado. Sirve bastante bien como arma de cuerpo a "
"cuerpo para los que tengan fuerza, pero es casi inservible en las manos de "
"alguien débil."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "short sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "short sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena corta"
msgstr[1] "almádenas cortas"

#. ~ Description for short sledge hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A shorter sledge hammer, still as weighty, however, due to the same steel "
"head.  Worse as a melee weapon but is a more portable tool."
msgstr ""
"Una almádena más corta, pero igual de pesada, debido a la misma cabeza de "
"acero. Peor como arma de combate cuerpo a cuerpo pero una herramienta más "
"portátil."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "engineer's hammer"
msgid_plural "engineer's hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de ingeniería"
msgstr[1] "martillos de ingeniería"

#. ~ Description for engineer's hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout and hefty hammer, more akin to a sledge than a typical ball-peen.  "
"Useful for portable demolition work, but is very unwieldy as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un robusto y fuerte martillo, más parecido a un trineo que a una típica "
"pelota. Útil para trabajos de demolición portátil, pero muy difícil de "
"manejar como arma."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "heavy sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "heavy sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena pesada"
msgstr[1] "almádenas pesadas"

#. ~ Description for heavy sledge hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large sledge hammer with a massive, heavy head.  This unwieldy tool is "
"meant to break concrete, rock, brick, anything really."
msgstr ""
"Una gran almádena con una enorme y pesada cabeza. Esta herramienta poco "
"manejable está hecha para romper hormigón, roca, ladrillos, en realidad "
"cualquier cosa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "hockey stick"
msgid_plural "hockey sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo de hockey"
msgstr[1] "palos de hockey"

#. ~ Description for hockey stick
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A curved wooden stick with a wide and flat end.  Commonly used by hockey "
"players."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo curvado de madera con una punta ancha y plana. Es comúnmente "
"utilizado por los jugadores de hockey."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "homewrecker"
msgid_plural "homewreckers"
msgstr[0] "rompehogar"
msgstr[1] "rompehogares"

#. ~ Description for homewrecker
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A long piece of wood with several chunks of steel firmly tied to it.  The "
"resulting weapon is unwieldy and slow but very heavy hitting."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza grande de madera con varios trozos de acero atados firmemente. El "
"arma resultante es difícil de manejar y lenta pero con un golpe muy pesado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ironshod quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "ironshod quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "vara larga con calzas de hierro"
msgstr[1] "varas largas con calzas de hierro"

#. ~ Description for ironshod quarterstaff
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A smooth and sturdy staff with a leather-wrapped grip, which has been "
"reinforced with metal bands and caps.  Durable and well-balanced, it is "
"surprisingly easy to handle."
msgstr ""
"Una vara fuerte y lisa con cuero enrollado como mango, que ha sido reforzada"
" con franjas y capuchas de metal. Duradera y bien balanceada, es "
"sorprendentemente fácil de usar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "lucerne hammer"
msgid_plural "lucerne hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de lucerne"
msgstr[1] "martillos de lucerne"

#. ~ Description for lucerne hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a versatile polearm with a spiked hammer head, a spike, and a hook "
"attached to a beefy wooden pole."
msgstr ""
"Este es un arma de asta versátil con una cabeza de martillo con púas, un "
"pico y un gancho unido a un palo largo."

#. ~ Description for lucerne hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a cheap piece of crap imitation of a versatile polearm with a spiked"
" hammer head, probably used for LARPing"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una barata mierda de imitación de una versátil arma de asta con una "
"cabeza de martillo con púas, probablemente utilizado para LARPing"

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "mace"
msgid_plural "maces"
msgstr[0] "maza"
msgstr[1] "mazas"

#. ~ Description for mace
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy iron end.  It is "
"heavy and slow, but its crushing damage is devastating."
msgstr ""
"Es un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera con una punta de "
"hierro pesado. Es lenta y pesada, pero su golpe aplastante es devastador."

#. ~ Description for mace
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy iron end."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica ligera y barata de un arma medieval que normalmente consistiría "
"en un mango de madera con un pesado extremo de hierro."

#. ~ Description for mace
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy iron end.  That "
"iron end feels a bit loose."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un mango de madera con un pesado extremo de"
" hierro. Ese extremo de hierro se siente un poco suelto."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift sap"
msgid_plural "makeshift saps"
msgstr[0] "porra improvisada"
msgstr[1] "porras improvisadas"

#. ~ Description for makeshift sap
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an improvised sap, also known as a cosh, slapjack and slapper.  A "
"short and flat bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded between "
"two patches of leather."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una porra improvisada, también conocida como cachiporra, slapjack y "
"slapper. Un arma corta y plana que consiste en un peso incrustado entre dos "
"parches de cuero."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Mjölnir"
msgid_plural "Mjölnirs"
msgstr[0] "Mjölnir"
msgstr[1] "Mjölnirs"

#. ~ Description for Mjölnir
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large hammer, forged from the heart of a dying star.  It bears the inscription:\n"
"\n"
"Whosoever holds this hammer,\n"
"If he be worthy,\n"
"Shall possess the power to…\n"
"CRUSH!'"
msgstr ""
"Un gran martillo, forjado en el corazón de una estrella moribunda. Lleva la inscripción:\n"
"\n"
"Quienquiera que sostenga este martillo,\n"
"Si es digno,\n"
"Tendrá el poder de...\n"
"¡APLASTAR!'."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "morningstar"
msgid_plural "morningstars"
msgstr[0] "maza de armas"
msgstr[1] "mazas de armas"

#. ~ Description for morningstar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked iron ball"
" on the end.  It deals devastating crushing damage, with a small amount of "
"piercing to boot."
msgstr ""
"Es un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera con una bola pesada y "
"con púas en la punta. Causa un daño aplastante devastador, con una pequeña "
"cantidad de daño penetrante."

#. ~ Description for morningstar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked iron ball on the end."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica ligera y barata de un arma medieval que normalmente consistiría "
"en un mango de madera con una pesada bola de hierro con púas en el extremo."

#. ~ Description for morningstar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked iron ball"
" on the end.  That end feels lighter than it should."
msgstr ""
"Es un arma medieval que consiste en un mango de madera con una bola pesada "
"de hierro con púas en la punta. Esa bola se siente un poco más liviana de lo"
" que debería."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "nail bat"
msgid_plural "nail bats"
msgstr[0] "bate con clavos"
msgstr[1] "bates con clavos"

#. ~ Description for nail bat
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A baseball bat with several nails driven through it, an excellent melee "
"weapon."
msgstr ""
"Es un bate de béisbol con varios clavos atravesándolo. Es una excelente arma"
" de cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "nailboard"
msgid_plural "nailboards"
msgstr[0] "tabla con clavos"
msgstr[1] "tablas con clavos"

#. ~ Description for nailboard
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A long piece of wood with several nails through one end; essentially a "
"simple mace.  Makes an acceptable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una tabla grande de madera con varios clavos en una punta. Esencialmente, es"
" un maza simple. Es una arma aceptable para el cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pool cue"
msgid_plural "pool cues"
msgstr[0] "palo de billar"
msgstr[1] "palos de billar"

#. ~ Description for pool cue
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hard-wood stick designed for hitting colorful balls around a felt table.  "
"Truly, the coolest of sports."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo de madera dura diseñado para golpear pelotas coloridas en una "
"mesa de fieltro. La verdad, el mejor de los deportes."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "PR-24 baton (extended)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (extended)"
msgstr[0] "garrote PR-24 (extendido)"
msgstr[1] "garrotes PR-24 (extendidos)"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for PR-24 baton (extended).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Retract"
msgstr "Retraer"

#. ~ Use action msg for PR-24 baton (extended).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "You collapse your PR-24 baton."
msgstr "Cierras tu garrote PR-24."

#. ~ Description for PR-24 baton (extended)
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to retract."
msgstr ""
"El bastón Monadnock PR-24 es un bastón plegable, ligero, con mango lateral, "
"utilizado por las fuerzas del orden de todo el mundo. Se rumorea que la "
"designación PR significa Relaciones Públicas. Activar para retraerse."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (retracted)"
msgstr[0] "garrote PR-24 (retraído)"
msgstr[1] "garrotes PR-24 (retraídos)"

#. ~ Use action menu_text for PR-24 baton (retracted).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Extend"
msgstr "Extender"

#. ~ Use action msg for PR-24 baton (retracted).
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "You snap open your PR-24 baton."
msgstr "Abres bruscamente tu garrote PR-24."

#. ~ Description for PR-24 baton (retracted)
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to extend."
msgstr ""
"El bastón Monadnock PR-24 es un bastón plegable, ligero, con mango lateral, "
"utilizado por las fuerzas del orden de todo el mundo. Se rumorea que la "
"designación PR significa Relaciones Públicas. Activar para extender."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "vara larga"
msgstr[1] "varas largas"

#. ~ Description for quarterstaff
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A smooth and sturdy staff.  Light and well-balanced, it is surprisingly easy"
" to handle."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón suave y robusto. Ligero y bien equilibrado, es sorprendentemente "
"fácil de manejar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "rock in a sock"
msgid_plural "rocks in socks"
msgstr[0] "piedra en una calcetín"
msgstr[1] "piedras en calcetines"

#. ~ Description for rock in a sock
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A pair of nested socks filled with a stone.  A true weapon of despair."
msgstr ""
"Un par de calcetines anidados llenos de una piedra. Una verdadera arma de "
"desesperación."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "plastic shank"
msgid_plural "plastic shanks"
msgstr[0] "asta de plástico"
msgstr[1] "astas de plástico"

#. ~ Description for plastic shank
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An oblong plastic trinket with the far end ground down into a stabbing "
"point."
msgstr ""
"Una baratija de plástico oblonga con el extremo lejano molido en un punto "
"para apuñalar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "shillelagh"
msgid_plural "shillelaghs"
msgstr[0] "shillelagh(bastón maza)"
msgstr[1] "shillelaghs(bastón maza)"

#. ~ Description for shillelagh
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure"
" in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally "
"used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto y nudoso con un gran pomo en la parte superior que se ha "
"dejado curar en una chimenea. Un arma tradicional irlandesa, el shillelagh "
"se usaba originalmente para resolver disputas de manera caballerosa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "loaded stick"
msgid_plural "loaded sticks"
msgstr[0] " palo cargado"
msgstr[1] " palos cargados"

#. ~ Description for loaded stick
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure"
" in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally "
"used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner.  The knob has been "
"hollowed and filled with molten heavy metal to pack more of a punch."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto y nudoso con un gran pomo en la parte superior que se ha "
"dejado curar en una chimenea. Un arma tradicional irlandesa, el shillelagh "
"se usaba originalmente para resolver disputas de manera caballerosa. El pomo"
" ha sido ahuecado y rellenado con metal pesado fundido para dar un mayor "
"golpe."

#. ~ Description for shillelagh
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A fake shillelagh massproduced as a souvenir for tourists.  This knotty "
"stick has not been cured in a chimney like a traditional shillelagh but has "
"had fake black soot painted on."
msgstr ""
"Un falso shillelagh masivo producido como recuerdo para los turistas. Este "
"palo nudoso no ha sido curado en una chimenea como un shillelagh tradicional"
" sino que tiene pintado hollín negro falso."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "tonfa"
msgid_plural "tonfas"
msgstr[0] "tonfa"
msgstr[1] "tonfas"

#. ~ Description for tonfa
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hard plastic truncheon commonly employed by police.  Originally an "
"Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached"
" a third of the way down its length."
msgstr ""
"Es una cachiporra de plástico duro comúnmente utilizada por la policía. "
"Originalmente, es un arma de Okinawa que consiste en un palo con un mango "
"perpendicular cerca de uno de sus extremos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "wooden tonfa"
msgid_plural "wooden tonfas"
msgstr[0] "tonfa de madera"
msgstr[1] "tonfas de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden tonfa
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout wooden truncheon of the sort commonly employed by police.  "
"Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular "
"handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr ""
"Es una cachiporra de madera resistente parecida a la utilizada por la "
"policía. Originalmente, es un arma de Okinawa que consiste en un palo con un"
" mango perpendicular cerca de uno de sus extremos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "war hammer"
msgid_plural "war hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de guerra"
msgstr[1] "martillos de guerra"

#. ~ Description for war hammer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medieval hammer made for battle.  Its odd shape and balance make it an "
"excellent weapon, but an ineffective tool."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo medieval hecho para el combate. Su extraña forma y balance lo "
"hace una excelente arma, pero una herramienta ineficaz."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bionic claws"
msgid_plural "bionic claws"
msgstr[0] "garras biónicas"
msgstr[1] "garras biónicas"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'bionic claws'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Short and sharp claws made from a high-tech metal."
msgstr "Garras cortas y afiladas hechas de un metal de alta tecnología."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "monomolecular blade"
msgid_plural "monomolecular blades"
msgstr[0] "cuchilla monomolecular"
msgstr[1] "cuchillas monomoleculares"

#. ~ Description for monomolecular blade
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A foot-long blade made from high-tech alloy and edged with bonded "
"nanocrystals."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla de 30 cm de aleación de alta tecnología, y el borde con "
"nanocristales unidos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bullwhip"
msgid_plural "bullwhips"
msgstr[0] "látigo"
msgstr[1] "látigos"

#. ~ Description for bullwhip
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A long strip of braided leather with a handle on one end.  Originally "
"developed to settle disagreements with cattle, it's better used now for "
"flaying the rotten flesh off of walking corpses.  Great for when a problem "
"comes along."
msgstr ""
"Una larga correa de cuero trenzado con un mango en un extremo. Originalmente"
" diseñado para ordenar el ganado, ahora es mejor usada para despellejar la "
"carne podrida de los cadáveres ambulantes. Muy útil cuando se te vienen los "
"problemas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "scourge"
msgid_plural "scourges"
msgstr[0] "cilicio"
msgstr[1] "cilicios"

#. ~ Description for scourge
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The \"cat 'o nine tails\", a handle with nine short leather whips, each "
"sporting a razor-sharp metal tip.  This ancient instrument of torture causes"
" massive bleeding, but by design is inefficient as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"El \"gato de las nueve colas\", un mango con nueve látigos cortos de cuero, "
"cada uno con una punta de metal afilada. Este antiguo instrumento de tortura"
" provoca hemorragias masivas, pero por su diseño es ineficiente como arma."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "lobotomizer"
msgid_plural "lobotomizers"
msgstr[0] "lobotomizador"
msgstr[1] "lobotomizadores"

#. ~ Description for lobotomizer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a hand-forged collapsible tool that has two axe heads and a sharp "
"shovel-like tip on one end.  It can be used as a shovel, or you could chop "
"some zombies with it instead."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una herramienta plegable forjada a mano que tiene dos cabezas de "
"hacha y una punta afilada en forma de pala en un extremo. Puede usarse como "
"pala o, en su lugar, puedes cortar algunos zombis con ella."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pitchfork"
msgid_plural "pitchforks"
msgstr[0] "horca"
msgstr[1] "horcas"

#. ~ Description for pitchfork
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An agricultural tool with long wooden shaft and four spikes.  Is used to "
"lift hay."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta para la agricultura. Es un palo lago con cuatro puntas, y"
" se utiliza para levantar heno."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pointy stick"
msgid_plural "pointy sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo con punta"
msgstr[1] "palos con punta"

#. ~ Description for pointy stick
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A simple wood pole with one end sharpened."
msgstr "Un simple palo de madera con una lado afilado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "wooden spear"
msgid_plural "wooden spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de madera"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stout pole with a fire-hardened point."
msgstr "Un poste robusto con una punta endurecida por el fuego."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "simple makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "simple makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja simple improvisada"
msgstr[1] "gujas simples improvisadas"

#. ~ Description for simple makeshift glaive
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large blade attached to a stout section of tree branch.  It could "
"do a considerable amount of damage."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran hoja unida a una sección robusta de la rama de un árbol. "
"Podría hacer una cantidad considerable de daño."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja improvisada"
msgstr[1] "gujas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description for makeshift glaive
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout tree branch that has been carefully split and reinforced.  At the "
"split point, a sharp blade has been bolted into place and reinforced with "
"layers of sturdy wrapped bindings."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta rama de árbol que ha sido cuidadosamente dividida y reforzada. "
"En el punto de división, se ha atornillado una hoja afilada en su lugar y se"
" ha reforzado con capas de resistentes ataduras envueltas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "forked spear"
msgid_plural "forked spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza tridente"
msgstr[1] "lanzas tridente"

#. ~ Description for forked spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wooden pole with three spikes tied to it.  It's specialized for catching "
"weapons, and not intended for extended use in combat."
msgstr ""
"Un palo de madera con tres púas atadas a él. Está especializado en la "
"captura de armas, y no está destinado a un uso prolongado en el combate."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "copper spear"
msgid_plural "copper spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de cobre"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de cobre"

#. ~ Description for copper spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a spearhead worked from copper."
msgstr "Es un palo grueso de madera con una punta afilada de cobre."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "steel spear"
msgid_plural "steel spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de acero"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de acero"

#. ~ Description for steel spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a hand-forged steel spearhead."
msgstr "Un palo de madera robusto con una punta de acero forjado a mano."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pipe spear"
msgid_plural "pipe spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de tubo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de tubo"

#. ~ Description for pipe spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stout metal pole with a sharp point."
msgstr "Es un palo grueso de metal con una punta afilada."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sharpened rebar"
msgid_plural "sharpened rebars"
msgstr[0] "varilla corrugada afilada"
msgstr[1] "varillas corrugadas afiladas"

#. ~ Description for sharpened rebar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A somewhat sharpened piece of rebar."
msgstr "Una barra de acero corrugado afilada de alguna forma."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "qiang"
msgid_plural "qiang"
msgstr[0] "qiang"
msgstr[1] "qiangs"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'qiang'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ancient Chinese spear, typically with a tassel just below the spearhead."
"  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, jian "
"sword, and gun staff."
msgstr ""
"Es una antigua lanza china, típicamente posee una borla justo debajo de la "
"punta. Una de las cuatro armas principales de su tradición, junto con el "
"sable dao, la espada jian y el bastón gun."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "halberd"
msgid_plural "halberds"
msgstr[0] "alabarda"
msgstr[1] "alabardas"

#. ~ Description for halberd
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a versatile polearm with an axe blade, a spike, and other fun things"
" attached to a long sturdy stick."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma de asta versátil con una cuchilla de hacha, una púa, y otras"
" cosas divertidas agregadas a un palo largo."

#. ~ Description for halberd
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply made replica of a polearm with an axe blade, a "
"spike, and other fun things attached to a thick pole."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una aburrida y barata réplica de un arma de asta con una hoja de "
"hacha, un pico y otras cosas divertidas unidas a un grueso palo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "glaive"
msgid_plural "glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja"
msgstr[1] "gujas"

#. ~ Description for glaive
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A sturdy polearm with a sizable, single-edged blade on the end."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta arma de asta con una considerable cuchilla de un solo filo en la"
" punta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "naginata"
msgid_plural "naginata"
msgstr[0] "naginata"
msgstr[1] "naginata"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'naginata'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  Occasionally used by samurai in early periods, "
"or by their wives in defense of the household."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta arma de asta con una cuchilla curva, hecha a la manera de la "
"katana y otras espadas japonesas. Ocasionalmente era utilizada por los "
"samurai en los primeros tiempos, o por sus esposas en defensa de su hogar."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'naginata'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  This one has a bit of wiggle to its blade and "
"feels a bit shoddily made."
msgstr ""
"Un robust arma de asta con una hoja curva, hecho de la misma manera que la "
"katana y otras hojas japonesas. Este tiene un poco de movimiento en su hoja "
"y se siente un poco mal hecho."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'naginata'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, slightly floppy replica of a Japanese polearm with a curved "
"blade.  With a little difficulty, you could use it administer a solid slap "
"from a distance."
msgstr ""
"Es una réplica sin filo y medio floja de un arma de asta japonesa con una "
"cuchilla curva. Con un poco de dificultad, podrías usarla para administrar "
"una buen golpe a distancia."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "survivor naginata"
msgid_plural "survivor naginata"
msgstr[0] "naginata de superviviente"
msgstr[1] "naginatas de superviviente"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'survivor naginata'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This sturdy steel shaft with a sword blade at the end is good for both "
"slashing and stabbing."
msgstr ""
"Esta robusta vara de acero con una hoja de espada en la punta, es buena "
"tanto para cortar como para apuñalar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "wooden javelin"
msgid_plural "wooden javelins"
msgstr[0] "jabalina de madera"
msgstr[1] "jabalinas de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden javelin
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A fire-hardened wooden spear honed to a sharper point."
msgstr ""
"Una lanza de madera endurecida por el fuego, afilada a una punta más "
"afilada."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "iron javelin"
msgid_plural "iron javelins"
msgstr[0] "jabalina de hierro"
msgstr[1] "jabalinas de hierro"

#. ~ Description for iron javelin
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "An iron-tipped wooden throwing spear."
msgstr "Una lanza de madera con punta de hierro."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "wooden pike"
msgid_plural "wooden pikes"
msgstr[0] "pica de madera"
msgstr[1] "picas de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden pike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a medieval weapon consisting of a wood shaft with a fire hardened "
"point."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma medieval que consiste en un eje de madera con una punta "
"endurecida al fuego."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "copper pike"
msgid_plural "copper pikes"
msgstr[0] "pica de cobre"
msgstr[1] "picas de cobre"

#. ~ Description for copper pike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a medieval weapon consisting of a wood shaft tipped with a copper "
"spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma medieval que consiste en un eje de madera con una punta de "
"cobre."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "pike"
msgid_plural "pikes"
msgstr[0] "lucio"
msgstr[1] "lucios"

#. ~ Description for pike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a medieval weapon consisting of a wood shaft tipped with an iron "
"spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma medieval que consiste en un eje de madera con una punta de "
"hierro."

#. ~ Description for pike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply made replica of a medieval weapon consisting of a "
"wood shaft tipped with an iron spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de un arma medieval que consiste en un"
" eje de madera con una punta de hierro."

#. ~ Description for pike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a medieval weapon consisting of a wood shaft tipped with an iron "
"spearhead.  The head seems to be pretty dull, and the whole thing feels "
"poorly made."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un arma medieval que consiste en un eje de madera con una punta de "
"hierro. La cabeza parece ser bastante aburrida, y todo el conjunto se siente"
" mal hecho."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "war scythe"
msgid_plural "war scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña de guerra"
msgstr[1] "guadañas de guerra"

#. ~ Description for war scythe
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pole weapon with a curving single-edged blade.  Its blade bears some "
"superficial resemblance to that of an agricultural scythe from which it "
"likely evolved."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta con una hoja curva de un solo filo. Su hoja tiene un cierto "
"parecido superficial con la de una guadaña agrícola de la que probablemente "
"evolucionó."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "dory"
msgid_plural "dories"
msgstr[0] "dory"
msgstr[1] "dorus"

#. ~ Description for dory
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A well-made spear with a bronze head, Greek in origin."
msgstr ""
"Una lanza de buena construcción con la punta de bronce. De origen griego."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "poleaxe"
msgid_plural "poleaxes"
msgstr[0] "alabarda"
msgstr[1] "alabardas"

#. ~ Description for poleaxe
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a polearm with an axe head, a small hammer on the back, and a short "
"dagger-like spike on top.  It's less heavy than most polearms and has a "
"smaller head, making it slightly quicker."
msgstr ""
"Este es un arma de asta con una cabeza de hacha, un pequeño martillo en la "
"espalda, y un pico corto como una daga en la parte superior. Es menos pesado"
" que la mayoría de las armas de fuego y tiene una cabeza más pequeña, lo que"
" la hace ligeramente más rápida."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ji"
msgid_plural "ji"
msgstr[0] "ji"
msgstr[1] "ji"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'ji'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a bronze polearm that originated in the Shang dynasty of China, if "
"not earlier.  It combines a spear head with the perpendicular blade of the "
"earlier ge or dagger-axe."
msgstr ""
"Es un arma de asta de bronce con origen en la dinastía Shang de China, "
"aunque tal vez antes. Combina una punta de lanza con la cuchilla "
"perpendicular del ge o una daga-hacha."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "stone spear"
msgid_plural "stone spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de piedra"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de piedra"

#. ~ Description for stone spear
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a sharp stone spearhead."
msgstr "Es un palo grueso de madera con una piedra afilada en la punta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "2-by-sword"
msgid_plural "2-by-swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de madera"
msgstr[1] "espadas de madera"

#. ~ Description for 2-by-sword
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A plank with a crossguard and whittled-down point; not much for slashing, "
"but much better than your bare hands."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón con una guardia cruzada y una punta cortada; no es mucho para "
"cortar, pero es mucho mejor que tus manos desnudas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "nord"
msgid_plural "nords"
msgstr[0] "clavespada"
msgstr[1] "clavespadas"

#. ~ Description for nord
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The nail sword, or nord for short.  This wooden sword has a dozen nails "
"sticking at jagged angles from edge of the blade, making it much better at "
"chopping than slashing."
msgstr ""
"Una espada de clavos, o clavespada para hacerla corta. Esta espada de madera"
" tiene una docena de clavos sobresaliendo como dientes del filo de la hoja, "
"lo que la hace mucho mejor para golpear que para cortar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "crude sword"
msgid_plural "crude swords"
msgstr[0] "espada primitiva"
msgstr[1] "espadas primitivas"

#. ~ Description for crude sword
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Several bits of thin scrap metal crudely beat into the semblance of an edge "
"over a wooden sword.  The added weight is unbalanced, but the jagged edge "
"offers a good bit of slashing power."
msgstr ""
"Varios trocitos de chatarra fina golpeados para darle un parecido de filo a "
"una espada de madera. El peso agregado está desbalanceado, pero el filo "
"dentado brinda una buena cantidad daño cortante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "jian"
msgid_plural "jian"
msgstr[0] "jian"
msgstr[1] "jian"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'jian'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of an ancient Chinese doubled-edged "
"straight sword, with an ornate guard."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una aburrida y barata réplica de una antigua espada recta china de "
"doble filo, con una guardia ornamentada."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "scimitar"
msgid_plural "scimitars"
msgstr[0] "cimitarra"
msgstr[1] "cimitarras"

#. ~ Description for scimitar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a curved sword, associated with "
"various Middle Eastern and Central Asian countries."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de una réplica aburrida y barata de una espada curva, asociada a "
"varios países de Oriente Medio y Asia Central."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "estoc"
msgid_plural "estocs"
msgstr[0] "estoque"
msgstr[1] "estoques"

#. ~ Description for estoc
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a thin thrusting sword, a sort of predecessor to the rapier.  It "
"requires a larger baldric or scabbard, compared to smaller swords."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una fina espada de empuje, una especie de predecesora de la espada "
"ropera. Requiere una vaina más grande, comparada con espadas más pequeñas."

#. ~ Description for estoc
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a thin thrusting sword, a sort of predecessor to the rapier.  It "
"requires a larger baldric or scabbard, compared to smaller swords.  It seems"
" a bit too bendy."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una fina espada de empuje, una especie de predecesora de la espada "
"ropera. Requiere una vaina más grande, comparada con espadas más pequeñas. "
"Parece un poco demasiado flexible."

#. ~ Description for estoc
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a thin thrusting sword predating the"
" rapier.  It requires a larger baldric or scabbard, compared to smaller "
"swords."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de una delgada espada de empuje "
"anterior a la espada ropera. Requiere una vaina más grande, comparada con "
"espadas más pequeñas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "longsword"
msgid_plural "longswords"
msgstr[0] "espada larga"
msgstr[1] "espadas largas"

#. ~ Description for longsword
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of the classic medieval longsword.  It "
"requires a larger baldric or scabbard, compared to smaller swords."
msgstr ""
"Es una réplica berreta de la clásica espada larga medieval. Necesita un gran"
" tahalí o una vaina, a diferencia de otras espadas más pequeñas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "arming sword"
msgid_plural "arming swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de caballero"
msgstr[1] "espadas de caballero"

#. ~ Description for arming sword
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a classic medieval sword, just the "
"right size to use one-handed."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una aburrida y barata réplica de una espada medieval clásica, del "
"tamaño adecuado para usar con una sola mano."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "tanto"
msgid_plural "tanto"
msgstr[0] "tantō"
msgstr[1] "tantōs"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'tanto'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a long Japanese knife, typically "
"used as a samurai's backup weapon."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de un largo cuchillo japonés, "
"típicamente usado como arma de respaldo de un samurai."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'tanto'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Long Japanese knives like this more-modern remake were the samurai's backup "
"weapon, before the advent of the larger wakizashi.  This one doesn't feel "
"well-balanced."
msgstr ""
"Largos cuchillos japoneses como este remake más moderno fueron el arma de "
"respaldo del samurai, antes del advenimiento del wakizashi más grande. Este "
"no se siente bien equilibrado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "nodachi"
msgid_plural "nodachi"
msgstr[0] "nodachi"
msgstr[1] "nodachi"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'nodachi'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a huge, curved, two-handed sword "
"from Japan.  It is surprisingly light for its size."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de una enorme espada curva de dos "
"manos de Japón. Es sorprendentemente ligera para su tamaño."

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'nodachi'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a huge, curved, two-handed sword from Japan.  It is surprisingly "
"light for its size, but also much bendier than a sword should be."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una enorme espada curva de dos manos de Japón. Es sorprendentemente "
"liviana para su tamaño, pero también mucho más curvada de lo que debería ser"
" una espada."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "fencing foil"
msgid_plural "fencing foils"
msgstr[0] "florete de esgrima"
msgstr[1] "floretes de esgrima"

#. ~ Description for fencing foil
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  Unfortunately, a "
"fencing foil is rather useless as a weapon, due to its flexible shaft and "
"dull tip."
msgstr ""
"Un arma utilizada en el esgrima, el más noble de todos los deportes. "
"Lamentablemente, un florete de esgrima es bastante inútil como arma, debido "
"a su hoja flexible y punta sin filo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "fencing épée"
msgid_plural "fencing épées"
msgstr[0] "espada de esgrima"
msgstr[1] "espadas de esgrima"

#. ~ Description for fencing épée
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  The épée is the "
"heaviest and stiffest of the fencing weapons, and therefore perhaps the most"
" useful."
msgstr ""
"Un arma usada para la esgrima, el más noble de todos los deportes. La espada"
" es la más pesada y rígida de las armas de esgrima, y por lo tanto quizás la"
" más útil."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "fencing saber"
msgid_plural "fencing sabers"
msgstr[0] "sable de esgrima"
msgstr[1] "sables de esgrima"

#. ~ Description for fencing saber
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  The fencing saber "
"is marginally shorter than the foil and épée, but no less effective."
msgstr ""
"Un arma usada para la esgrima, el más noble de todos los deportes. El sable "
"de esgrima es ligeramente más corto que el florete y la espada, pero no "
"menos efectivo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sharpened foil"
msgid_plural "sharpened foils"
msgstr[0] "hoja afilada"
msgstr[1] "hojas afiladas"

#. ~ Description for sharpened foil
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"What was once a mostly-harmless fencing foil has had its electrical plunger "
"assembly removed and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still"
" lacks a cutting edge, it is now somewhat more lethal, yet still familiar to"
" the practiced fencer."
msgstr ""
"Lo que una vez fue una hoja de esgrima mayormente inofensiva ha sido "
"removida de su ensamblaje de émbolo eléctrico y ha sido crudamente afilada "
"hasta cierto punto. Aunque todavía carece de un borde cortante, ahora es "
"algo más letal, pero aún familiar para el esgrimista practicante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sharpened épée"
msgid_plural "sharpened épées"
msgstr[0] "espada de esgrima afilada"
msgstr[1] "espadas de esgrimas afiladas"

#. ~ Description for sharpened épée
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"What was once a mostly-harmless fencing épée has had its electrical plunger "
"assembly removed and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still"
" lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still "
"familiar to the practiced fencer."
msgstr ""
"Lo que una vez fue una espada mayormente inofensiva se le ha quitado el "
"ensamblaje del émbolo eléctrico y ha sido crudamente afilado hasta cierto "
"punto. Aunque todavía carece de un borde cortante, ahora es "
"considerablemente más letal, aunque todavía es familiar para el esgrimista "
"practicante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sharpened saber"
msgid_plural "sharpened sabers"
msgstr[0] "sable afilado"
msgstr[1] "sables afilados"

#. ~ Description for sharpened saber
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"What was once a mostly-harmless fencing saber has had its rounded tip "
"snapped off and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still "
"lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still familiar"
" to the practiced fencer."
msgstr ""
"Lo que una vez fue un inofensivo sable de esgrima ha sido quitado de su "
"punta redondeada y ha sido crudamente afilado en una punta. Aunque todavía "
"carece de un borde cortante, ahora es considerablemente más letal, aunque "
"todavía es familiar para el esgrimista practicante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "hollow cane"
msgid_plural "hollow canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón hueco"
msgstr[1] "bastones huecos"

#. ~ Description for hollow cane
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cane designed to conceal a blade.  This was a popular fashion accessory "
"for the wealthy during the 18th and 19th centuries."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón diseñado para ocultar la hoja. Este fue un accesorio de moda "
"popular para los ricos durante los siglos 18 y 19."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sword cane"
msgid_plural "sword canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón de espada"
msgstr[1] "bastones de espada"

#. ~ Description for sword cane
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A sword with a thin blade designed to be hidden inside a hollow cane."
msgstr ""
"Una espada con una hoja fina diseñada para ser escondida dentro de un bastón"
" hueco."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cutlass"
msgid_plural "cutlasses"
msgstr[0] "sable"
msgstr[1] "sables"

#. ~ Description for cutlass
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a broad saber known for its use by "
"sailors and pirates."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de un sable ancho conocido por su uso "
"por marineros y piratas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "katana"
msgid_plural "katana"
msgstr[0] "katana"
msgstr[1] "katanas"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'katana'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a rare sword from Japan."
msgstr "Esta es una aburrida y barata réplica de una rara espada de Japón."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "zweihänder"
msgid_plural "zweihänders"
msgstr[0] "zweihänder"
msgstr[1] "zweihänders"

#. ~ Description for zweihänder
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a huge two-handed sword from "
"Germany.  It still packs a wallop."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de una enorme espada de dos manos de "
"Alemania. Todavía tiene un golpe."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "broadsword"
msgid_plural "broadswords"
msgstr[0] "espada ancha"
msgstr[1] "espadas anchas"

#. ~ Description for broadsword
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of an early modern sword that saw use "
"in the 16th, 17th, and 18th centuries.  Called 'broad' to contrast with the "
"slimmer rapiers."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de una espada moderna que se usó en "
"los siglos XVI, XVII y XVIII. Llamada \"ancha\" para contrastar con las "
"espadas más delgadas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "cavalry saber"
msgid_plural "cavalry sabers"
msgstr[0] "sable de caballería"
msgstr[1] "sables de caballería"

#. ~ Description for cavalry saber
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of a curved sword associated with "
"cavalry, from the Early Modern period onwards."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica aburrida y barata de una espada curvada asociada con la "
"caballería, desde el período Moderno Temprano en adelante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "rapier"
msgid_plural "rapiers"
msgstr[0] "florete"
msgstr[1] "floretes"

#. ~ Description for rapier
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a blunted, cheap replica of a thin sword with an ornate handguard.  "
"It looks like the preferred weapon of gentlemen and swashbucklers.  Light "
"and quick, it makes any battle a stylish battle."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una réplica roma y barata de una espada delgada con un adorno en la "
"mano. Parece el arma preferida de los caballeros y los espadachines. Ligera "
"y rápida, hace de cualquier batalla una batalla con estilo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
#: lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "wakizashi"
msgid_plural "wakizashi"
msgstr[0] "wakizashi"
msgstr[1] "wakizashi"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'wakizashi'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheap replica of the more common wakizashi.  Smaller and "
"lighter than a katana, but still effective in combat."
msgstr ""
"Es una réplica berreta sin filo de un wakizashi común. Más pequeña y liviana"
" que una katana, pero aún así eficaz en el combate."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/TOOL_from_json.py
msgid "kris"
msgid_plural "krises"
msgstr[0] "kris"
msgstr[1] "krises"

#. ~ Description for kris
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheap replica of a wavy bladed dagger that comes from "
"Southeast Asia."
msgstr ""
"Es una réplica berreta sin filo de una daga de hoja asimétrica, originaria "
"del sureste asiático."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "lajatang"
msgid_plural "lajatangs"
msgstr[0] "lajatang"
msgstr[1] "lajatang"

#. ~ Description for lajatang
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An impractical exotic weapon comprised of a long pole of wood with curved "
"blades on each end."
msgstr ""
"Un arma exótica poco práctica compuesta por un largo palo de madera con "
"hojas curvas en cada extremo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "tiger claws"
msgid_plural "tiger claws"
msgstr[0] "garras de tigre"
msgstr[1] "garras de tigre"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'tiger claws'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Also called bagh nakha or iron paw, this is a small claw-like bladed weapon "
"from India designed to be concealed under and against the palm."
msgstr ""
"También se las llama bagh nakha o garra de hierro. Es una pequeña arma con "
"cuchilla similar a una garra, proveniente de India y diseñada para estar "
"oculta en la palma de la mano."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pair of brass knuckles"
msgid_plural "pairs of brass knuckles"
msgstr[0] "par de nudillos de latón"
msgstr[1] "pares de nudillos de latón"

#. ~ Description for pair of brass knuckles
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A metal weapon made of brass, designed to be gripped in the palm and cause "
"punches to do extra damage.  A good, quick weapon - but you have to get "
"within punching range to use it."
msgstr ""
"Es un arma de metal hecha de latón, diseñada para ser agarrada con la palma "
"y hacer que los piñas hagan daño extra. Un arma rápida y buena, pero tienes "
"que estar cerca del enemigo para poder usarla."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "razorbar katar"
msgid_plural "razorbar katars"
msgstr[0] "katara de varillas"
msgstr[1] "kataras de varillas"

#. ~ Description for razorbar katar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Five pieces of rebar sharpened to cruel points and strapped to a brace "
"fastened at wrist and forearm on both arms.  The next bub better watch out."
msgstr ""
"Cinco varillas corrugadas afiladas y unidas a brazales que se ajustan a la "
"muñeca y antebrazo de los dos brazos. Más vale que el próximo tío tenga "
"cuidado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pair of nail knuckles"
msgid_plural "pairs of nail knuckles"
msgstr[0] "par de nudillos con clavos"
msgstr[1] "pares de nudillos con clavos"

#. ~ Description for pair of nail knuckles
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pair of knuckles consisting of two small squares of wood with several "
"nails coming through them.  Useful in nasty street fights."
msgstr ""
"Un par de nudillos que consiste en dos pequeños cuadrados de madera con "
"varios clavos a lo largo de ellos. Útiles en peleas callejeras sucias."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pair of scrap knuckles"
msgid_plural "pairs of scrap knuckles"
msgstr[0] "par de nudillos de chatarra"
msgstr[1] "pares de nudillos de chatarras"

#. ~ Description for pair of scrap knuckles
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A mass of scrap metal crudely beat into shape, with folded rags underneath "
"to protect the wearers knuckles.  A good, quick weapon - but you have to get"
" within punching range to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una masa de chatarra golpeada parar darle forma, con trapos doblados debajo "
"para proteger la mano. Es un arma rápida y buena, pero tienes que estar "
"cerca del enemigo para poder usarla."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pair of steel knuckles"
msgid_plural "pairs of steel knuckles"
msgstr[0] "par de nudillos de acero"
msgstr[1] "pares de nudillos de acero"

#. ~ Description for pair of steel knuckles
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pair of knuckles forged from steel, designed to be gripped in the palm and"
" cause punches to do more damage.  A good, quick weapon - but you have to "
"get within punching range to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un par de nudillos forjados en acero, diseñados para ser agarrados en la "
"palma de la mano y hacer que los puñetazos hagan más daño. Un arma buena y "
"rápida, pero hay que ponerse a tiro de puñetazo para usarlos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "punch dagger"
msgid_plural "punch daggers"
msgstr[0] "daga de puño"
msgstr[1] "dagas de puño"

#. ~ Description for punch dagger
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A short and sharp double-edged dagger made to be gripped in the palm, with "
"the blade protruding between the fingers."
msgstr ""
"Una daga corta y afilada de doble filo hecha para ser agarrada en la palma "
"de la mano, con la hoja sobresaliendo entre los dedos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "explosive arrowhead"
msgid_plural "explosive arrowheads"
msgstr[0] "punta de flecha explosiva"
msgstr[1] "puntas de flecha explosivas"

#. ~ Description for explosive arrowhead
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This simple IED is designed to be attached to an arrow and detonate on "
"impact."
msgstr ""
"Este simple artefacto explosivo improvisado está diseñado para ser puesto en"
" una flecha y detonar al impacto."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "disc"
msgid_plural "discs"
msgstr[0] "disco"
msgstr[1] "discos"

#. ~ Description for disc
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A plastic disc made for playing disc golf, it is smaller and denser then a "
"normal frisbee."
msgstr ""
"Un disco de plástico hecho para jugar al disc golf, es más pequeño y denso "
"que un frisbee normal."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "frisbee"
msgid_plural "frisbees"
msgstr[0] "frisbee"
msgstr[1] "frisbees"

#. ~ Description for frisbee
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A plastic frisbee made for outdoor games."
msgstr "Un frisbee de plástico hecho para juegos al aire libre."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "lawn dart"
msgid_plural "lawn darts"
msgstr[0] "dardo de plástico"
msgstr[1] "dardos de plástico"

#. ~ Description for lawn dart
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A large plastic dart made for outdoor games."
msgstr "Un dardo largo de plástico para deportes al aire libre."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "throwing axe"
msgid_plural "throwing axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha arrojadiza"
msgstr[1] "hachas arrojadizas"

#. ~ Description for throwing axe
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A lightweight hatchet made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and "
"light weight makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Una hacha de poco peso para ser tirada. No tiene buen filo y su poco peso la"
" hace inservible como herramienta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "throwing knife"
msgid_plural "throwing knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo arrojadizo"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos arrojadizos"

#. ~ Description for throwing knife
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A thin and flat knife made for throwing.  Its ineffective cutting edge and "
"odd shape makes it unsuitable for use as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo delgado y plano hecho para ser tirado. No tiene buen filo y su "
"extraña forma lo hace inservible como herramienta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bakelite phone"
msgid_plural "bakelite phones"
msgstr[0] "teléfono de baquelita"
msgstr[1] "teléfonos de baquelita"

#. ~ Description for bakelite phone
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A vintage, bright-red bakelite phone of famous swedish design.  It would "
"look almost normal, were it not for the fact that its rotary dial has been "
"replaced by a doorknob."
msgstr ""
"Un antiguo teléfono de baquelita de color rojo brillante de famoso diseño "
"sueco. Se vería casi normal, si no fuera por el hecho de que su dial "
"giratorio ha sido reemplazado por un pomo de puerta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "golden comb"
msgid_plural "golden combs"
msgstr[0] "peine dorado"
msgstr[1] "peines dorados"

#. ~ Description for golden comb
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small and delicate golden comb, it was once carefully engraved, but time "
"has smoothed its designs to illegibility."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño y delicado peine dorado, fue una vez cuidadosamente grabada, pero"
" el tiempo ha suavizado sus diseños hasta hacerlos ilegibles."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "shifting keyring"
msgid_plural "shifting keyrings"
msgstr[0] "anillo de llave"
msgstr[1] "anillos de llave"

#. ~ Description for shifting keyring
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A smooth ring of steel, heavy under the weight of numerous keys.  The "
"designs of the keys change over time, but none will fit any keyhole you have"
" ever found."
msgstr ""
"Un suave anillo de acero, pesado bajo el peso de numerosas llaves. Los "
"diseños de las llaves cambian con el tiempo, pero ninguna encajará en "
"ninguna cerradura que hayas encontrado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "engraved cube"
msgid_plural "engraved cubes"
msgstr[0] "cubo gravado"
msgstr[1] "cubos gravados"

#. ~ Description for engraved cube
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small cube of smooth rock.  An uniform grid of nine squares is engraved in"
" each of its faces."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño cubo de roca lisa. Una cuadrícula uniforme de nueve cuadrados "
"está grabada en cada una de sus caras."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "utah teapot"
msgid_plural "utah teapots"
msgstr[0] "tetera de utah"
msgstr[1] "teteras de utah"

#. ~ Description for utah teapot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A squat teapot with a minimalist design.  Its surface shines under the glow "
"of unseen light sources."
msgstr ""
"Una tetera de pie con un diseño minimalista. Su superficie brilla bajo el "
"brillo de fuentes de luz no vistas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "glitching stopwatch"
msgid_plural "glitching stopwatches"
msgstr[0] "cronómetro que falla"
msgstr[1] "cronómetros que fallan"

#. ~ Description for glitching stopwatch
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small digital stopwatch, looking slightly old by today's standards.  Its "
"digital display prints ever-changing gibberish."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño cronómetro digital, que parece un poco viejo para los estándares "
"de hoy en día. Su pantalla digital imprime un galimatías siempre cambiante."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "alien resin chunk"
msgid_plural "alien resin chunks"
msgstr[0] "trozo de resina alienígena"
msgstr[1] "trozos de resina alienígena"

#. ~ Description for alien resin chunk
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a shattered fragment of alien resin.  It looks a bit like a large "
"piece of sea glass, frosted and gritty with the edges rounded off.  It is "
"somewhat warm to the touch."
msgstr ""
"Este es un fragmento destrozado de resina alienígena. Se parece un poco a un"
" gran trozo de cristal marino, escarchado y arenoso con los bordes "
"redondeados. Es algo cálido al tacto."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Exodii chassis"
msgid_plural "Exodii chassis"
msgstr[0] "chasis Exodii"
msgstr[1] "chasis Exodii"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Exodii chassis'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This roughly hexagonal frame and associated bodywork looks like it was "
"constructed as a single monolithic piece.  The fitting holes and attachments"
" are extremely durable, despite showing signs of heavy wear and repair.  The"
" structure is versatile, and could probably be engineered to serve a number "
"of different heavy combat roles."
msgstr ""
"Este marco aproximadamente hexagonal y la carrocería asociada parece haber "
"sido construida como una sola pieza monolítica. Los agujeros de ajuste y los"
" accesorios son extremadamente duraderos, a pesar de mostrar signos de gran "
"desgaste y reparación. La estructura es versátil, y probablemente podría ser"
" diseñada para servir a un número de diferentes roles de combate pesado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "Exodii drone chassis"
msgid_plural "Exodii drone chassis"
msgstr[0] "chasis de dron Exodii"
msgstr[1] "chasis de dron Exodii"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'Exodii drone chassis'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This small, roughly hexagonal frame and associated bodywork looks like it "
"was constructed as a single monolithic piece.  The fitting holes and "
"attachments are extremely durable, despite showing signs of heavy wear and "
"repair.  The structure is versatile, and could probably be engineered to "
"serve a number of different heavy combat roles."
msgstr ""
"Esta pequeña estructura hexagonal y su correspondiente carrocería parece "
"haber sido construida como una sola pieza monolítica. Los agujeros de ajuste"
" y los accesorios son extremadamente duraderos, a pesar de mostrar signos de"
" gran desgaste y reparación. La estructura es versátil, y probablemente "
"podría ser diseñada para servir a un número de diferentes roles de combate "
"pesado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cybernetic neural matrix"
msgid_plural "cybernetic neural matrices"
msgstr[0] "matrix neuronal cibernética"
msgstr[1] "matrices neuronales cibernéticas"

#. ~ Description for cybernetic neural matrix
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A series of tanks and tubes with ports for fluids, electricity, and input "
"and output, this complex arrangement is made to house a brain and spine and "
"the most difficult to replace organs for keeping them alive."
msgstr ""
"Una serie de tanques y tubos con puertos para fluidos, electricidad, y "
"entrada y salida, este complejo arreglo está hecho para albergar un cerebro "
"y una columna vertebral y los órganos más difíciles de reemplazar para "
"mantenerlos vivos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "unfamiliar electronic thingy"
msgid_plural "unfamiliar electronic thingies"
msgstr[0] "cosita electrónica desconocida"
msgstr[1] "cositas electrónicas desconocidas"

#. ~ Description for unfamiliar electronic thingy
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"The wiring and general shape suggest to you that this is a computer, or at "
"least some sort of electronic device, but what it is and what role it serves"
" is lost on you.  It's heavy and sturdy in construction."
msgstr ""
"El cableado y la forma general sugieren que se trata de un ordenador, o al "
"menos de algún tipo de dispositivo electrónico, pero lo que es y el papel "
"que cumple no lo conoces. Es pesado y robusto en su construcción."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "inscribed metal plates"
msgid_plural "inscribed metal plates"
msgstr[0] "placas de metal inscritas"
msgstr[1] "placas de metal inscritas"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'inscribed metal plates'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This device looks electronic, but is unfamiliar.  It is a series of tightly "
"fitted coppery-looking rings, set concentrically.  Wires run from each ring "
"to an axis in the middle."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo parece electrónico, pero no es familiar. Es una serie de "
"anillos de aspecto cobrizo ajustados, colocados concéntricamente. Los cables"
" van de cada anillo a un eje en el centro."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cybernetic sensor"
msgid_plural "cybernetic sensors"
msgstr[0] "sensor cibernético"
msgstr[1] "sensores cibernéticos"

#. ~ Description for cybernetic sensor
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"From the large glassy eye - the size of a small dinner plate - in the front,"
" you deduce this is some sort of camera.  None of the inner workings make "
"any sense to you nor resemble any camera you've seen before."
msgstr ""
"Del gran ojo vidrioso, del tamaño de un pequeño plato de comida, en el "
"frente, se deduce que es una especie de cámara. Ninguno de los mecanismos "
"internos tiene sentido para ti ni se parece a ninguna cámara que hayas visto"
" antes."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "rotary device"
msgid_plural "rotary devices"
msgstr[0] "dispositivo rotatorio"
msgstr[1] "dispositivos rotatorios"

#. ~ Description for rotary device
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You assume from the coils of coppery wire and the protruding piston that "
"this is some sort of motor or generator, but the design doesn't look similar"
" to anything you've seen before, and you can't figure out how to get it to "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Supones por las bobinas de alambre de cobre y el pistón saliente que se "
"trata de algún tipo de motor o generador, pero el diseño no se parece a nada"
" que hayas visto antes, y no puedes averiguar cómo hacer que funcione."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "engraved parabolic dish"
msgid_plural "engraved parabolic dishes"
msgstr[0] "plato parabólico grabado"
msgstr[1] "platos parabólicos grabados"

#. ~ Description for engraved parabolic dish
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This hefty parabolic dish is engraved with an unrecognizable pattern of "
"symbols that might, at a guess, be some sort of circuitry pattern - or maybe"
" a religious incantation."
msgstr ""
"Esta pesada parábola está grabada con un patrón irreconocible de símbolos "
"que podría ser, en una suposición, una especie de patrón de circuitos - o "
"tal vez un encantamiento religioso."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "oblong device"
msgid_plural "oblong devices"
msgstr[0] "dispositivo oblongo"
msgstr[1] "dispositivos oblongos"

#. ~ Description for oblong device
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Perfectly smooth, cool to the touch, and a dull blue-grey colour, this looks"
" almost like a perfect riverstone at first glance.  Its artificial nature is"
" betrayed on closer inspection by a network of intricate patterns visible as"
" a slight difference in the reflection of light off its surface."
msgstr ""
"Perfectamente lisa, fría al tacto y de un color gris azulado mate, a primera"
" vista parece casi una perfecta piedra de río. Su naturaleza artificial es "
"traicionada en una inspección más cercana por una red de intrincados "
"patrones visibles como una ligera diferencia en el reflejo de la luz de su "
"superficie."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous aluminum ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous aluminum ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de aluminio enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de aluminio enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous aluminum ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A block of pure aluminum at least as big as a dishwasher."
msgstr "Un bloque de aluminio puro al menos tan grande como un lavavajillas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous plastic block"
msgid_plural "enormous plastic blocks"
msgstr[0] "bloque de plástico enorme"
msgstr[1] "bloques de plástico enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous plastic block
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a single enormous brick of plastic, big enough to curl up inside "
"were it hollow."
msgstr ""
"Esto es un solo y enorme bloque de plástico, lo suficientemente grande como "
"para poder acurrucarse en su interior si estuviera hueco."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous steel ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous steel ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de acero enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de acero enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous steel ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A single, monolithic block of high quality steel."
msgstr "Un solo bloque monolítico de acero de alta calidad."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous tin ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous tin ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de estaño enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de estaño enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous tin ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "An enormous ingot of pure tin."
msgstr "Un enorme lingote de puro estaño."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous copper ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous copper ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de cobre enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de cobre enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous copper ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A massive solid piece of copper, covered by a blue-green patina."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza masiva y sólida de cobre, cubierta por una pátina azul verdosa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous zinc ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous zinc ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de zinc enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de zinc enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous zinc ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An absolutely massive block of pure zinc.  Bet you didn't expect that - "
"nobody expects zinc."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque absolutamente masivo de zinc puro. Apuesto a que no te lo "
"esperabas, nadie espera a zinc."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "enormous lead ingot"
msgid_plural "enormous lead ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de plomo enorme"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de plomo enormes"

#. ~ Description for enormous lead ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A block of lead so huge you don't even want to think about how heavy it is."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque de plomo tan grande que no quieres ni pensar en lo que pesa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sheet of glass"
msgid_plural "sheets of glass"
msgstr[0] "plancha de cristal"
msgstr[1] "planchas de cristal"

#. ~ Use action done_message for sheet of glass.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You break the pane and place the shards on the ground, ready to be cracked "
"by something passing by."
msgstr ""
"Se rompe el cristal y se colocan los fragmentos en el suelo, listos para ser"
" agrietados por algo que pase."

#. ~ Description for sheet of glass
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large sheet of glass, around three by four feet.  Easily shattered.  "
"Useful for repairing windows."
msgstr ""
"Una gran hoja de vidrio, de unos tres por cuatro pies. Se rompe fácilmente. "
"Útil para reparar ventanas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sheet of reinforced glass"
msgid_plural "sheets of reinforced glass"
msgstr[0] "plancha de cristal reforzado"
msgstr[1] "planchas de cristal reforzado"

#. ~ Description for sheet of reinforced glass
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large sheet of bulletproof glass, it looks to a little over two inches "
"thick."
msgstr ""
"Una gran hoja de vidrio a prueba de balas, parece tener un poco más de dos "
"pulgadas de espesor."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pane of reinforced glass"
msgid_plural "panes of reinforced glass"
msgstr[0] "lámina de cristal reforzado"
msgstr[1] "láminas de cristal reforzado"

#. ~ Description for pane of reinforced glass
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small pane of bulletproof glass, it looks to be a little over two inches "
"thick."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño panel de vidrio a prueba de balas, parece tener un poco más de "
"dos pulgadas de espesor."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sheet of tempered glass"
msgid_plural "sheets of tempered glass"
msgstr[0] "hoja de vidrio templado"
msgstr[1] "hojas de vidrio templado"

#. ~ Description for sheet of tempered glass
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large, durable sheet of tempered glass, approximately six millimeters "
"thick.  A common type of safety glass with the curious property of breaking "
"into small, non-lethal pieces upon shattering."
msgstr ""
"Una gran y duradera hoja de vidrio templado, de aproximadamente seis "
"milímetros de espesor. Un tipo común de vidrio de seguridad con la curiosa "
"propiedad de romperse en pequeños trozos no letales al romperse."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "peephole"
msgid_plural "peepholes"
msgstr[0] "mirilla"
msgstr[1] "mirillas"

#. ~ Description for peephole
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A metal cylinder with a small lens inside intended to be installed on a "
"door."
msgstr ""
"Un cilindro de metal con un pequeño lente adentro, pensado para ser puesto "
"en una puerta."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "mesh screen"
msgid_plural "mesh screens"
msgstr[0] "pantalla de malla"
msgstr[1] "pantallas de malla"

#. ~ Description for mesh screen
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A roll of fine mesh screen for bug barriers on porches."
msgstr ""
"Un rollo de malla fina para las barreras contra insectos en los porches.Un "
"rollo de malla fina para las barreras contra insectos en los porches."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "pipe"
msgid_plural "pipes"
msgstr[0] "tubo"
msgstr[1] "tubos"

#. ~ Description for pipe
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A steel pipe; makes a good melee weapon.  Useful in a few crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Un tubo de acero; es una buena arma de cuerpo a cuerpo. Útil en algunas "
"recetas de fabricación."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "spike"
msgid_plural "spikes"
msgstr[0] "púa"
msgstr[1] "púas"

#. ~ Description for spike
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large and slightly misshapen spike, could do some damage mounted on a "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una púa grande y un poco deforme, puede hacer daño si se la monta en un "
"vehículo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "copper tubing"
msgid_plural "copper tubings"
msgstr[0] "tubería de cobre"
msgstr[1] "tuberías de cobre"

#. ~ Description for copper tubing
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A copper tube; too thin to be much use as a melee weapon, but will do if "
"nothing else is available.  Useful in a few crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Un tubo de cobre; demasiado fino para ser útil como arma de cuerpo a cuerpo,"
" pero servirá si no hay nada más disponible. Útil en algunas recetas de "
"fabricación."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "aluminum ingot"
msgid_plural "aluminum ingots"
msgstr[0] "lingote de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "lingotes de aluminio"

#. ~ Description for aluminum ingot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small aluminum ingot, standardized for further processing.  Light but "
"durable, this could be cast into various shapes for construction or ground "
"down to a powder, for more… high-profile applications."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño lingote de aluminio, estandarizado para su posterior "
"procesamiento. Ligero pero duradero, puede ser moldeado en varias formas "
"para la construcción o molido hasta convertirse en polvo, para más... "
"aplicaciones de alto perfil."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "scrap copper"
msgid_plural "scrap copper"
msgstr[0] "resto de cobre"
msgstr[1] "restos de cobre"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'scrap copper'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A small chunk of copper, usable for crafting or repairs."
msgstr "Es un pequeño trozo de cobre, útil para fabricar o reparar cosas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "bee sting"
msgid_plural "bee stings"
msgstr[0] "aguijón de abeja"
msgstr[1] "aguijones de abeja"

#. ~ Description for bee sting
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A six-inch stinger from a giant bee.  Makes a mediocre melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un aguijón de 15 cm de una abeja gigante. Es una arma mediocre para el "
"cuerpo a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "broom"
msgid_plural "brooms"
msgstr[0] "escoba"
msgstr[1] "escobas"

#. ~ Description for broom
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A long-handled broom.  Makes a terrible weapon unless you're chasing cats."
msgstr ""
"Una escoba de mango largo. Es muy mala como arma salvo que estés "
"persiguiendo gatos."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ceramic shard"
msgid_plural "ceramic shards"
msgstr[0] "fragmento de cerámica"
msgstr[1] "fragmentos de cerámica"

#. ~ Description for ceramic shard
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A broken ceramic shard.  It is heavy and has a somewhat sharp edge, but it's"
" too irregular to cut properly."
msgstr ""
"Es un fragmento roto de cerámica. Es pesado y tiene un poco de filo, pero es"
" demasiado irregular para usarlo para cortar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "fungal fighter sting"
msgid_plural "fungal fighter stings"
msgstr[0] "aguijón de guerrero fúngico"
msgstr[1] "aguijones de guerrero fúngico"

#. ~ Description for fungal fighter sting
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A short dart from a fungal fighter.  Makes a poor melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un dardo corto de un luchador hongo. Es una arma pobre de combate cuerpo a "
"cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/furniture_from_json.py
msgid "mattress"
msgid_plural "mattresses"
msgstr[0] "colchón"
msgstr[1] "colchones"

#. ~ Description for mattress
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This is a single, or twin, sized mattress."
msgstr "Este es un colchón de tamaño individual o doble."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py lang/json/furniture_from_json.py
msgid "down mattress"
msgid_plural "down mattresses"
msgstr[0] "colchón de abajo"
msgstr[1] "colchones de abajo"

#. ~ Description for down mattress
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This is a single, or twin, sized down filled mattress."
msgstr "Este es un colchón relleno de tamaño individual o doble."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "flint"
msgid_plural "flints"
msgstr[0] "pedernal"
msgstr[1] "pedernales"

#. ~ Description for flint
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A rock with sharp edges.  Makes a passable melee weapon, and can also make "
"sparks if struck against high-carbon steel."
msgstr ""
"Una roca con bordes afilados. Es un arma de cuerpo a cuerpo aceptable, y "
"también puede hacer chispas si se golpea contra el acero de alto carbono."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ESAPI ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "ESAPI ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "placa balística ESAPI"
msgstr[1] "placas balísticas ESAPI"

#. ~ Description for ESAPI ballistic plate
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A polygonal ceramic ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile.  Its "
"inner surface is coated with Ultra High Molecular Weight Polyethylene, and "
"is labeled \"TOP\", while its outer surface is labeled \"STRIKE FACE\".  "
"This is intended to be worn in a ballistic vest and can withstand several "
"high energy rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr ""
"Una placa balística de cerámica poligonal con un perfil ligeramente cóncavo."
" Su superficie interior está recubierta con polietileno de peso molecular "
"ultra alto, y está etiquetada como \"TOP\", mientras que su superficie "
"exterior está etiquetada como \"STRIKE FACE\". Está pensada para ser usada "
"en un chaleco balístico y puede soportar varios disparos de rifles de alta "
"potencia antes de romperse."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "ESBI ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "ESBI ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "placa balística ESBI"
msgstr[1] "placas balísticas ESBI"

#. ~ Description for ESBI ballistic plate
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A polygonal ceramic ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile.  "
"\"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  This is designed to be "
"worn in the sides of a plate carrier and can withstand several high energy "
"rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr ""
"Una placa balística de cerámica poligonal con un perfil ligeramente cóncavo."
" \"STRIKE FACE\" está impresa en su superficie exterior. Está diseñado para "
"ser usado en los lados de un portaplacas y puede soportar varios disparos de"
" rifle de alta energía antes de romperse."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "grenade launcher buttstock"
msgid_plural "grenade launcher buttstocks"
msgstr[0] "culata de lanzagranadas"
msgstr[1] "culatas de lanzagranadas"

#. ~ Description for grenade launcher buttstock
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collapsible buttstock designed for the M320 grenade launcher.  When "
"combined with this stock, the M320 can be used as a standalone weapon"
msgstr ""
"Una culata plegable diseñada para el lanzador de granadas M320. Cuando se "
"combina con esta culata, el M320 puede ser usado como un arma independiente"

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "wasp sting"
msgid_plural "wasp stings"
msgstr[0] "aguijón de avispa"
msgstr[1] "aguijones de avispa"

#. ~ Description for wasp sting
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A six-inch stinger from a giant wasp.  Makes a poor melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un aguijón de 15 cm de una avispa gigante. Es una arma pobre para el cuerpo "
"a cuerpo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "cannonball"
msgid_plural "cannonballs"
msgstr[0] "bala de cañón"
msgstr[1] "balas de cañón"

#. ~ Description for cannonball
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 4 pound cannonball.  With some gunpowder, wadding, and a fuse, it could be"
" prepared to load into a cannon."
msgstr ""
"Una bala de cañón de 4 libras. Con un poco de pólvora, relleno y una mecha, "
"podría prepararse para cargarse en un cañón."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "RC car wheel set"
msgid_plural "RC car wheel sets"
msgstr[0] "juego de ruedas de coches RC"
msgstr[1] "juegos de ruedas de coches RC"

#. ~ Description for RC car wheel set
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Small set of wheels for a radio controlled car.  Could be improvised with "
"caster wheels if given rubber treads for grip."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño juego de ruedas para un coche teledirigido. Podría improvisarse "
"con ruedas pivotantes si se le dieran bandas de goma para el agarre."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "plastic sheet"
msgid_plural "plastic sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de plástico"
msgstr[1] "laminas de plástico"

#. ~ Description for plastic sheet
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a large sheet of heavy flexible plastic, the sort that might have "
"been used for commercial wrapping or for weather-sealing a home."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran hoja de plástico flexible y pesado, del tipo que podría "
"haber sido usado para envoltorios comerciales o para sellar una casa."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "polycarbonate sheet"
msgid_plural "polycarbonate sheets"
msgstr[0] "lámina de policarbonato"
msgstr[1] "láminas de policarbonato"

#. ~ Description for polycarbonate sheet
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a stack of polycarbonate sheets that can be used for, among other "
"things, vacuum molding."
msgstr ""
"Esto es una pila de láminas de policarbonato que pueden usarse para, entre "
"otras cosas, hacer molduras al vacío."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "rigid plastic sheet"
msgid_plural "rigid plastic sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de plástico rígida"
msgstr[1] "laminas de plástico rígidas"

#. ~ Description for rigid plastic sheet
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large, rigid sheet of translucent plastic, useful for all manner of "
"things; from construction to art, or even junior snowboarding."
msgstr ""
"Una gran hoja rígida de plástico translúcido, útil para todo tipo de cosas; "
"desde la construcción hasta el arte, o incluso para el snowboarding juvenil."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "large rock"
msgid_plural "large rocks"
msgstr[0] "piedra grande"
msgstr[1] "piedras grandes"

#. ~ Description for large rock
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A heavy and large rock, big enough to be used as a primitive anvil, or "
"shaped into larger stone items."
msgstr ""
"Una roca pesada y grande, lo suficientemente grande para ser usada como un "
"yunque primitivo, o para darle forma a artículos de piedra más grandes."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "grass yarn"
msgid_plural "grass yarns"
msgstr[0] "hilo de hierba"
msgstr[1] "hilos de hierba"

#. ~ Description for grass yarn
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Some primitive yarn made from coarse plant fibers like straw or grass.  Too "
"thick to sew with, but could be woven into a crude sheet of fabric."
msgstr ""
"Algún hilo primitivo hecho de fibras vegetales gruesas como paja o hierba. "
"Demasiado grueso para coserlo, pero podría ser tejido en una hoja de tejido "
"cruda."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "log"
msgid_plural "logs"
msgstr[0] "leño"
msgstr[1] "leños"

#. ~ Description for log
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large chunk of log, cut from a tree.  (a)ctivate a wood axe or wood saw to"
" cut it into planks."
msgstr ""
"Un gran trozo de leño, cortado de un árbol. (a)ctivar un hacha de madera o "
"una sierra de madera para cortarlo en tablones."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "splintered wood"
msgid_plural "splintered wood"
msgstr[0] "madera astillada"
msgstr[1] "maderas astilladas"

#. ~ Description for {'str_sp': 'splintered wood'}
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A splintered piece of wood, could be used as a skewer or for kindling."
msgstr ""
"Una cacho de madera astillado que puede ser usada como un pincho o leña."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "stick"
msgid_plural "sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo"
msgstr[1] "palos"

#. ~ Description for stick
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A respectable length of wood, just big enough to wrap your hand around.  "
"Makes a decent melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una longitud respetable de madera, lo suficientemente grande como para "
"envolver tu mano. Un arma de combate cuerpo a cuerpo decente."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long stick"
msgid_plural "long sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"

#. ~ Description for long stick
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A straight section of wood, about eight feet long and a couple of inches in "
"diameter.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and can be broken into shorter "
"pieces for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Una sección recta de madera, de unos dos metros de largo y un par de "
"centímetros de diámetro. Constituye un arma de cuerpo a cuerpo decente, y "
"puede romperse en trozos más cortos para la fabricación."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "long pole"
msgid_plural "long poles"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"

#. ~ Description for long pole
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A stout, ten-foot pole.  Could be used similarly to a spear.  The Cataclysm "
"gives fresh meaning to walking softly and carrying a big stick."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto de tres metros. Podría usarse de forma similar a una lanza. "
"El Cataclismo le da un nuevo significado a caminar suavemente y llevar un "
"gran palo."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py src/crafting_gui.cpp
msgid "plank"
msgid_plural "planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón"
msgstr[1] "tablones"

#. ~ Description for plank
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A narrow, thick plank of wood, like a 2 by 4 or similar piece of dimensional"
" lumber.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and can be used for all kinds "
"construction."
msgstr ""
"Una tablól de madera estrecha y gruesa, como una pieza de madera de 2 por 4 "
"o similar. Hace un arma cuerpo a cuerpo decente, y se puede utilizar para "
"todo tipo de construcción."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "heavy wooden beam"
msgid_plural "heavy wooden beams"
msgstr[0] "viga de madera pesada"
msgstr[1] "vigas de madera pesadas"

#. ~ Description for heavy wooden beam
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An enormous beam of solid wood, very heavy and hard to lug around, but also "
"very sturdy for construction.  You could saw or chop it into smaller pieces,"
" like planks or panels."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme viga de madera maciza, muy pesada y difícil de arrastrar, pero "
"también muy resistente para la construcción. Podrías serrarla o cortarla en "
"trozos más pequeños, como tablones o paneles."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "wooden panel"
msgid_plural "wooden panels"
msgstr[0] "panel de madera"
msgstr[1] "paneles de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden panel
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wide, thin wooden board - plywood, OSB, MDF, tongue-in-groove boards, or "
"similar, already cut to shape.  These large flat boards are good for all "
"kinds of construction, but for really big projects you'd need a proper sheet"
" of uncut plywood or the like."
msgstr ""
"Un tablero de madera ancho y delgado - contrachapado, OSB, MDF, tablas de "
"lengüeta en ranura, o similar, ya cortado en forma. Estos grandes tableros "
"planos son buenos para todo tipo de construcción, pero para proyectos "
"realmente grandes se necesita una hoja adecuada de madera contrachapada sin "
"cortar o similar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "large wooden sheet"
msgid_plural "large wooden sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de madera grande"
msgstr[1] "laminas de madera grandes"

#. ~ Description for large wooden sheet
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A standard 4x8 sheet of flat wood - usually plywood, OSB, or MDF.  Heavy and"
" bulky, this is extremely useful for all manner of construction, but you "
"might have to cut it to size before doing smaller projects."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja estándar de 4x8 de madera plana, normalmente de contrachapado, OSB "
"o MDF. Pesada y voluminosa, es extremadamente útil para todo tipo de "
"construcción, pero puede que tengas que cortarla a medida antes de hacer "
"proyectos más pequeños."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "steel bottle"
msgid_plural "steel bottles"
msgstr[0] "botella de acero"
msgstr[1] "botellas de acero"

#. ~ Description for steel bottle
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A stainless steel water bottle, holds 750ml of liquid."
msgstr "Es una botella de acero inoxidable, que puede contener hasta 750 ml."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "foldable plastic bottle"
msgid_plural "foldable plastic bottles"
msgstr[0] "botella plegable de plástico"
msgstr[1] "botellas plegables de plástico"

#. ~ Description for foldable plastic bottle
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A non-rigid plastic bottle for easy storage, holds 500 ml of liquid."
msgstr ""
"Es una botella flexible de plástico, fácil de transportar, que puede "
"contener hasta 500 ml."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "atomic coffee maker"
msgid_plural "atomic coffee makers"
msgstr[0] "cafetera atómica"
msgstr[1] "cafeteras atómicas"

#. ~ Description for atomic coffee maker
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is a Curie-G coffeemaker, by CuppaTech.  It famously uses a radioactive"
" generator to heat water for coffee.  Normally the water is heated using "
"energy stored in a capacitor, and makes ordinary coffee.  However, as a "
"special feature, water from the RTG containment area can be used, giving the"
" coffee a very special kick.  The Curie-G is illegal in most countries."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una cafetera Curie-G, de CuppaTech. Es famosa por usar un generador "
"radioactivo para calentar agua para el café. Normalmente el agua se calienta"
" usando la energía almacenada en un condensador, y hace café ordinario. Sin "
"embargo, como característica especial, se puede utilizar el agua del área de"
" contención de RTG, dándole al café un toque muy especial. El Curie-G es "
"ilegal en la mayoría de los países."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "can sealer"
msgid_plural "can sealers"
msgstr[0] "enlatadora"
msgstr[1] "enlatadoras"

#. ~ Description for can sealer
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A hand crank powered cast steel machine designed to automatically seal tin "
"cans."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina de acero fundido accionada por manivela diseñada para sellar "
"automáticamente las latas."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "clay pot"
msgid_plural "clay pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "ollas de arcilla"

#. ~ Description for clay pot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A crude clay pot with lid used for cooking."
msgstr "Una olla de arcilla con tapa que se usa para cocinar."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "clay quern"
msgid_plural "clay querns"
msgstr[0] "mortero de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "morteros de arcilla"

#. ~ Description for clay quern
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "This is a simple hand-powered clay quern for grinding grain."
msgstr "Es un simple mortero de mano hecho de arcilla, para moler grano."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "clay teapot"
msgid_plural "clay teapots"
msgstr[0] "tetera de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "teteras de arcilla"

#. ~ Description for clay teapot
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "A clay teapot.  Now all you need is tea and water."
msgstr "Una tetera de arcilla. Ahora lo único que necesitas es té y agua."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "fermenting eggs jar"
msgid_plural "fermenting eggs jars"
msgstr[0] "bote de huevos fermentados"
msgstr[1] "botes de huevos fermentados"

#. ~ Use action msg for fermenting eggs jar.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"You examine the batch and see that the pickling solution has done its job, "
"so you seal the jar up for storage."
msgstr ""
"Examinas el lote y ves que la solución de encurtido ha hecho su trabajo, así"
" que sellas el frasco para el almacenamiento."

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for fermenting eggs jar.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "The eggs are not done yet."
msgstr "Los huevos no están listos todavía."

#. ~ Description for fermenting eggs jar
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This jar contains a batch of eggs in a pickling solution.  You can seal up "
"the jar once the process is completed."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene un lote de huevos en una solución de encurtido. Puedes "
"sellar el tarro una vez que el proceso se haya completado."

#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "sealed yeast culture"
msgid_plural "sealed yeast culture"
msgstr[0] "cultivo de levadura sellada"
msgstr[1] "cultivo de levadura sellada"

#. ~ Use action msg for {'str_sp': 'sealed yeast culture'}.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
msgid "You open the flask and harvest the culture."
msgstr "Abres el frasco y cosechás el cultivo."

#. ~ Use action not_ready_msg for {'str_sp': 'sealed yeast culture'}.
#: lang/json/GENERIC_from_json.py
